    <node id="AB_NP_DCIS_0000_2c67a0">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
      <data key="d11">AB_NP_DCIS_0000_2c67a0</data>
      <data key="d2">AB_NP_DCIS</data>
      <data key="d3">AB_NP_DCIS</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: imaging_MRI_external_read.pdf] To: Page: 1 of 2 2025-10-02 06:23:28 PDT (845) 783-0764 From: RadNet API HUDSON VALLEY HVRA MONROE RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES 505 RT 208 STES 14 &amp; 18 MONROE, NY [REDACTED] Phone: (845) 783-3444 LHR - A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE Fax: (845) 783-0764 Exam requested by: Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] DAVID ANDERSON MD Date of Birth: [REDACTED] 1176 5TH AVE, 1ST FL Phone: (704) 349-0802 NEW YORK NY [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Date of Exam: [REDACTED] EXAM: MRI BILATERAL BREASTS WITHOUT AND WITH CONTRAST HISTORY: 46-year-old female recently diagnosed with left breast ductal carcinoma in situ. COMPARISON: Screening mammogram from [REDACTED] diagnostic mammogram and breast ultrasound from [REDACTED] stereotactic core biopsy from [REDACTED] Screening mammogram from 2021, 2022, 2023. TECHNIQUE: Images were acquired on a GE HDx 3T MRI with a dedicated breast array coil. Sagittal fat suppressed T2 weighted images were acquired (TR5167, TE99, FA90, 256 x 256 matrix, 4 mm slice thickness). Sagittal FSE T1 weighted images were acquired (TR629, TE19, FA90, 512 x 512, 5 mm slice thickness). Bilateral sagittal T1 weighted images were acquired (TR433, TE9, 4 mm slice thickness). Sagittal fat suppressed Vibrant gradient echo images were acquired through both breasts both before and after dynamic intravenous administration of gadolinium (TR7, TE2, T6, FA10, Matrix 256 x 256, 2.8 mm slice thickness). These images were acquired dynamically out to 6 minutes. After the dynamic sagittal imaging, high resolution axial Vibrant images (TR6, TE2, T118, FA10, Matrix 512 x 512, 1.4 mm post thickness) were acquired. Images were reviewed utilizing breast MRI software which includes subtraction and post processing and enhancement curve analysis. Computer assisted diagnosis (CAD) was used. 20 ml of Clariscan was injected from a 20 ml single use vial. FINDINGS: Right breast: Background parenchymal enhancement is moderate. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] or morphologically abnormal right axillary lymph nodes. Left breast: Background parenchymal enhancement is moderate. Susceptibility artifact is present in the medial mid left breast, likely corresponds to the stereotactic core biopsy labeled medial. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] the biopsy clip. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] correspond to the second stereotactic core biopsy site. A circumscribed enhancing mass in the upper outer mid to posterior left breast at approximately 2:30 o'clock 11 cm from the nipple measures 2.5 x 0.9 cm, not evident on the prior studies. Further evaluation with MRI guided core biopsy is recommended. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] IMPRESSION: Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE, FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 9:23 AM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 2:00 PM) Page 1 of 2 To: Page: 2 of 2 2025-10-02 06:23:28 PDT (845) 783-0764 From: RadNet API HUDSON VALLEY HVRA MONROE RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES 505 RT 208 STES 14 &amp; 18 MONROE, NY Phone: (845) 783-3444 LHR - A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE Fax: (845) 783-0764 Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] 1. 2.5 x 0.9 cm enhancing mass in the left breast at 2:30 o'clock 11 cm from the nipple. Further evaluation with MRI guided core biopsy is recommended. 2. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] to the biopsy-proven DCIS. 3. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] FOLLOW-UP: Biopsy should be considered. ASSESSMENT: BI-RADS Category 4: Suspicious findings. Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. DARIA SETLIK MD Bd Cert Radiologist - [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] FDA Site Name: [REDACTED] 505 RT 208 STES 14 &amp; 18, MONROE, NY [REDACTED] Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE, FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 9:23 AM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 2:00 PM) Page 2 of 2 [DOCUMENT: imaging_mammo2_external_read.pdf] To: Page: 1 of 2 2025-10-02 06:20:13 PDT (845) 565-3617 From: RadNet API LHR LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY Exam requested by: SITE PERFORMED: LHR NEWBURGH ARIEL PEDOEEM DO 377 BROADWAY Patient: [REDACTED] NEWBURGH NY [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Phone: (704) 349-0802 [REDACTED] Date of Exam: [REDACTED] EXAM: DIGITAL BILATERAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM AND TOMOSYNTHESIS AND BREAST ULTRASOUND HISTORY: The patient [REDACTED] since breast biopsy- without palpable mass. Family history of breast cancer maternal aunt. Age: 46 years old. CLINICAL BREAST EXAMINATION: The patient [REDACTED] clinical breast exam. COMPARISON: The present examination is compared to prior imaging studies dating back to 2022. MAMMOGRAM: TECHNIQUE: Low-dose full-field digital breast tomosynthesis examination was performed with 2D and 3D acquisitions. The following views were obtained digitally: bilateral craniocaudal, bilateral mediolateral oblique. Computer-aided detection was applied. FINDINGS: BREAST COMPOSITION: There are scattered areas of fibroglandular density. Stable post biopsy changes are identified in the left breast. An area of density is identified in the upper inner left breast, 9 cm from the nipple, adjacent to a dense calcification shows post biopsy changes and corresponds to the lateral calcifications biopsied on [REDACTED]. This may correspond to the "enhancing mass in the upper outer mid to posterior left breast at approximately 2:30 o'clock 11 cm from nipple" identified on breast MRI [REDACTED]. The remainder of the left as well as the right breast are unremarkable and no [REDACTED] distortion, or significant calcifications are detected. BREAST ULTRASOUND: TECHNIQUE: Complete left breast ultrasound, with evaluation of the four quadrants, retroareolar region, and axilla, was performed. FINDINGS: Left breast: 2:30 11 cm from nipple-second look evaluation of breast MRI finding [REDACTED] iso to mildly hypoechoic nodule versus focus of prominent breast parenchyma-1.4 x 1.4 x 0.4 cm. This does not correlate with the breast MRI finding which Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - [REDACTED] Printed: [REDACTED] 9:19 AM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:20 PM) Page 1 of 2 To: Page: 2 of 2 2025-10-02 06:20:13 PDT (845) 565-3617 From: RadNet AP LHR LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] demonstrated an area of enhancement measuring 2.5 cm AP x 0.9 cm W 9 o'clock 8 cm from nipple</data>
      <data key="d14" />
    </node>
    <node id="AB_NP_DCIS_0001_d61c54">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
      <data key="d11">AB_NP_DCIS_0001_d61c54</data>
      <data key="d2">AB_NP_DCIS</data>
      <data key="d3">AB_NP_DCIS</data>
      <data key="d12">2</data>
      <data key="d13">the nipple, adjacent to a dense calcification shows post biopsy changes and corresponds to the lateral calcifications biopsied on [REDACTED]. This may correspond to the "enhancing mass in the upper outer mid to posterior left breast at approximately 2:30 o'clock 11 cm from nipple" identified on breast MRI [REDACTED]. The remainder of the left as well as the right breast are unremarkable and no [REDACTED] distortion, or significant calcifications are detected. BREAST ULTRASOUND: TECHNIQUE: Complete left breast ultrasound, with evaluation of the four quadrants, retroareolar region, and axilla, was performed. FINDINGS: Left breast: 2:30 11 cm from nipple-second look evaluation of breast MRI finding [REDACTED] iso to mildly hypoechoic nodule versus focus of prominent breast parenchyma-1.4 x 1.4 x 0.4 cm. This does not correlate with the breast MRI finding which Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - [REDACTED] Printed: [REDACTED] 9:19 AM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:20 PM) Page 1 of 2 To: Page: 2 of 2 2025-10-02 06:20:13 PDT (845) 565-3617 From: RadNet AP LHR LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] demonstrated an area of enhancement measuring 2.5 cm AP x 0.9 cm W 9 o'clock 8 cm from nipple cystic collection-0.6 x 0.6 x 0.5 cm. This corresponds to the region of the biopsy and therefore likely represents post biopsy changes. 9 o'clock 8 cm from nipple hypoechoic nodule-0.3 x 0.8 x 0.9 cm. New-6 month short interval follow-up warranted. IMPRESSION: 1. Post biopsy changes left breast as described and discussed above. 2. 1.4 cm nodule identified in the left breast 2:30 11 cm from nipple, however, this does not correlate with the breast MRI 2.5 cm focus of enhancement. The recommendation for MRI guided core biopsy of this area remains unchanged. FOLLOW-UP: Follow-up imaging in 6 months. Targeted left breast ultrasound 9 o'clock 8 cm from nipple. MRI biopsy-enhancing mass identified on [REDACTED] ASSESSMENT: BI-RADS Category 3: Probably benign. Left breast 9 o'clock 8 cm from nipple hypoechoic nodule The patient [REDACTED] situ-status post stereotactic [REDACTED] This examination should not preclude the clinical evaluation of a suspicious palpable abnormality. As per the FDA requirements, a lay letter has been generated and sent to your patient [REDACTED] recommendations of this breast imaging study. We have entered your patient [REDACTED] them when they are due for their next breast imaging exam. Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. STEVEN G REICHARD DO - Electronically Signed: [REDACTED] 3:53 PM Physician [REDACTED] FDA Site Name: [REDACTED] 320 Robinson Ave, Newburgh, NY [REDACTED] Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - [REDACTED] Printed: [REDACTED] 9:19 AM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:20 PM) Page 2 of 2 [DOCUMENT: imaging_mammo_external_read.pdf] HUDSON VALLEY RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES LHR A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE 2025-05-12 11:16:53 PDT (845) 565-3617 From: RadNet HVRA NEWBURGH 320 ROBINSON AVE NEWBURGH, NY Phone: (845) 565-3664 Fax: (845) 565-3617 Exam requested by: ARIEL PEDOEEM DO 377 BROADWAY NEWBURGH NY [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Phone: (704) 349-0802 [REDACTED] Date of Exam: [REDACTED] EXAM: DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC LEFT BREAST CALLBACK MAMMOGRAM AND TOMOSYNTHESIS WITH CAD AND BREAST ULTRASOUND HISTORY: The patient [REDACTED] demonstrated: left breast calcifications. Age: 46 years old. COMPARISON: The present examination is compared to prior imaging studies dating back to 2021 MAMMOGRAM: TECHNIQUE: Low-dose full-field digital left breast tomosynthesis examination was performed with tomosynthesis acquisitions and synthesized 2D reconstructed mammogram obtained. Magnification compression CC, magnification compression ML and full-field ML views were obtained. Computer-aided detection was applied. FINDINGS: BREAST COMPOSITION: There are scattered areas of fibroglandular density. The calcifications and architectural distortion identified on examination of [REDACTED] are better defined on the additional views, are suspicious and histologic evaluation is warranted via stereotactic core biopsy. An additional grouping of calcifications located approximately 2.5 cm medial and slightly posterior to the above calcifications is also noted. The second grouping of calcifications are, clustered, pleomorphic and therefore stereotactic core biopsy is also warranted. The remainder of the visualized left breast, on the additional views is unremarkable and no [REDACTED] architectural distortion, or additional foci of suspicious calcifications are identified. BREAST ULTRASOUND: TECHNIQUE: Targeted left breast ultrasound was performed. FINDINGS: Left breast: Retroareolar mild duct ectasia without nodule, mass or filling defect. Retroareolar complex cyst/cluster of cysts-0.8 x 0.5 x 0.8 cm. IMPRESSION: Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:16 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:00 PM) Page 1 of 2 HUDSON VALLEY RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES LHR A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE 2025-05-12 11:16:53 PDT (845) 565-3617 From: RadNet HVRA NEWBURGH 320 ROBINSON AVE NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] Phone: (845) 565-3664 Fax: (845) 565-3617 Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] 1. (2) groupings of mammographically suspicious calcifications in the left breast for which (2) site stereotactic biopsy is warranted. 2. The remainder of the unilateral left mammogram and targeted left breast ultrasound are unremarkable. FOLLOW-UP: Stereotactic biopsy. ASSESSMENT: BI-RADS Category 5: Highly suggestive of malignancy. I personally discussed the above findings and recommendations with the patient [REDACTED] stereotactic-guided core biopsy was recommended. The patient [REDACTED] action. The above findings and recommendations will be faxed and called to the office of ARIEL Y PEDOEEM DO on [REDACTED] by our staff. This examination should not preclude the clinical evaluation of a suspicious palpable abnormality. As per the FDA requirements, a layman's letter has been generated and sent to your patient [REDACTED] recommendations of this breast imaging study. We have entered your patient [REDACTED] them when they are due for their next breast imaging exam. Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. STEVEN G REICHARD DO Bd Cert Radiologist - [REDACTED] Physician [REDACTED] FDA Site Name: [REDACTED] 320 ROBINSON AVE, NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:16 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:00 PM) Page 2 of 2</data>
