with complete evaluation of the four quadrants, retroareolar regions, and axillae. COMPARISON: [REDACTED] FINDINGS: In the right breast in the 12 o'clock position 5 cm from the nipple is a 4 mm cyst with low-level internal echoes which is new from prior. There is an 8 mm cyst in the right breast 12 o'clock position 5 cm from the nipple stable from prior. In the right breast at the 7 o'clock position is a 1.2 x 1.1 x 1 cm cyst. This demonstrates low-level internal echoes which may be due to its deep location. In the right breast at the 10 o'clock position 6 cm the nipple is a 1.1 cm cyst. In the left breast at the 4 o'clock position 4 cm the nipple is a 6 x 8 x 4 mm cyst. No [REDACTED] in either breast. There is no [REDACTED] IMPRESSION: Multiple cysts identified bilaterally including a new 4 mm cyst with low-level internal echoes in the right breast at 12 o'clock position 5 cm from the nipple as well as a new 1.4 cm cyst with low-level internal echoes in the right breast at the 10 o'clock position 6 and from the nipple. Six-month follow-up focal right breast sonography is suggested to ensure stability. FOLLOW-UP: Follow-up imaging in 6 months. ASSESSMENT: BI-RADS Category 3: Probably benign. This examination should not preclude the clinical evaluation of a suspicious palpable abnormality. Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:14 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 3:00 PM) Page 1 of 2 To: Page: 2 of 2 2025-05-12 11:14:51 PDT (845) 565-3617 From: RadNet API HUDSON VALLEY RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES LHR A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE HVRA NEWBURGH 320 ROBINSON AVE NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] Phone: (845) 565-3664 Fax: (845) 565-3617 Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. ANAND E KAKKANATT MD Bd Cert Radiologist - [REDACTED] Physician [REDACTED] FDA Site Name: [REDACTED] 320 ROBINSON AVE, NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:14 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 3:00 PM) Page 2 of 2 → HVRA NEWBURGH pg 1 of 2 HUDSON VALLEY RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES HVRA NEWBURGH 320 ROBINSON AVE LHR A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] Phone: (845) 565-3664 Fax: (845) 565-3617 ARIEL PEDOEEM DO 377 BROADWAY Patient: [REDACTED] NEWBURGH NY [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Phone: (704) 349-0802 [REDACTED] Date of Exam: [REDACTED] EXAM: DIGITAL BILATERAL SCREENING MAMMOGRAM AND TOMOSYNTHESIS WITH CAD AND BREAST ULTRASOUND HISTORY: The patient [REDACTED] a screening mammogram. Family history of breast cancer-maternal aunt. CLINICAL BREAST EXAMINATION: The patient [REDACTED] clinical breast exam. COMPARISON: The present examination is compared to prior imaging studies dating back to 2021. MAMMOGRAM: TECHNIQUE: The following views were obtained digitally: bilateral craniocaudal, bilateral mediolateral oblique. Low- dose full-field digital breast tomosynthesis examination was performed with tomosynthesis acquisitions and synthesized 2D reconstructed mammogram. Examination was reviewed with Saige-Dx, an Artificial Intelligence Diagnostic Aid Software. FINDINGS: BREAST COMPOSITION: There are scattered areas of fibroglandular density. In the left central to central upper breast middle 1/3rd there is an area of architectural distortion with calcifications for which additional mammographic evaluation and targeted left breast ultrasound is indicated. Mammographically benign subcentimeter nodules are identified bilaterally. The remainder of the left, as well as the right breast are unremarkable and no [REDACTED] distortion, or significant calcifications are detected. BREAST ULTRASOUND: HISTORY: Supplemental screening evaluation. TECHNIQUE: A bilateral breast ultrasound was performed with complete evaluation of the four quadrants, retroareolar region, and axilla. FINDINGS: Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:14 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:00 PM) Page 1 of 2 [REDACTED] 2:14 PM (845) 565-3617 → HVRA NEWBURGH pg 2 of 2 HUDSON VALLEY HVRA NEWBURGH RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES 320 ROBINSON AVE NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] LHR A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE Phone: (845) 565-3664 Fax: (845) 565-3617 Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Right breast: Flushing cysts are identified throughout the breasts. 10 o'clock 6 cm</data>
