      <data key="d13">Examination was reviewed with Saige-Dx, an Artificial Intelligence Diagnostic Aid Software. FINDINGS: BREAST COMPOSITION: There are scattered areas of fibroglandular density. In the left central to central upper breast middle 1/3rd there is an area of architectural distortion with calcifications for which additional mammographic evaluation and targeted left breast ultrasound is indicated. Mammographically benign subcentimeter nodules are identified bilaterally. The remainder of the left, as well as the right breast are unremarkable and no [REDACTED] distortion, or significant calcifications are detected. BREAST ULTRASOUND: HISTORY: Supplemental screening evaluation. TECHNIQUE: A bilateral breast ultrasound was performed with complete evaluation of the four quadrants, retroareolar region, and axilla. FINDINGS: Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:14 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:00 PM) Page 1 of 2 [REDACTED] 2:14 PM (845) 565-3617 → HVRA NEWBURGH pg 2 of 2 HUDSON VALLEY HVRA NEWBURGH RADIOLOGY ASSOCIATES 320 ROBINSON AVE NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] LHR A LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY AFFILIATE Phone: (845) 565-3664 Fax: (845) 565-3617 Continued: Page 2 of 2 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Right breast: Flushing cysts are identified throughout the breasts. 10 o'clock 6 cm from nipple complex cyst/cluster of cysts-1.0 cm-new. Left breast: Fluctuating cysts are identified. No [REDACTED] in either breast. No [REDACTED] nodes are detected. IMPRESSION: 1. Focus of architectural distortion and calcifications in the left breast for which additional mammographic evaluation and targeted left breast ultrasound is indicated. 2. The remainder of the bilateral mammography and bilateral breast ultrasound are unremarkable. FOLLOW-UP: Additional imaging. A diagnostic left mammogram with targeted ultrasound is recommended. The Mammography Tracking Team will attempt to contact the patient [REDACTED] ASSESSMENT: BI-RADS Category 0: Incomplete: Need additional imaging evaluation. This examination should not preclude the clinical evaluation of a suspicious palpable abnormality. As per the FDA requirements, a layman's letter has been generated and sent to your patient [REDACTED] recommendations of this breast imaging study. We have entered your patient [REDACTED] them when they are due for their next breast imaging exam. Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. STEVEN G REICHARD DO Bd Cert Radiologist - [REDACTED] Physician [REDACTED] FDA Site Name: [REDACTED] 320 ROBINSON AVE, NEWBURGH, NY [REDACTED] Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] ACCREDITATIONS: AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ULTRASOUND IN MEDICINE/FETAL MEDICINE FOUNDATION ACR AND MQSA FOR MAMMOGRAPHY Printed: [REDACTED] 2:14 PM PATTERSON, NADIA (Exam: [REDACTED] 1:00 PM) Page 2 of 2 To: Page: 1 of 2 2025-05-12 11:12:50 PDT (845) 634-9018 From: RadNet API Ramapo Radiology Orange Radiology Associates, P.C. Associates, P.C. Ramapo Diagnostic Imaging Orange Radiology (Monroe) Orange Radiology (Newburgh) 11 North Airmont Road, Suffern, NY [REDACTED] 545 Route 208, Monroe, NY [REDACTED] 320 Robinson Avenue, Newburgh, NY [REDACTED] Ph: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] Ph: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] Ph: 845.565.3664 - Fax: [REDACTED] Exam requested by: Patient: [REDACTED] MIGRATED REFERRING MD Date of Birth: [REDACTED] MIGRATED RECORD Phone: (704) 349-0802 [REDACTED] Date of Exam: [REDACTED] February 28, 2023 Andrei Munzer, MD Crystal Run Healthcare 155 Crystal Run Rd Middletown , NY [REDACTED] Tel# (845) 703-6999 Fax# 845/703-6265 RE: NADIA PATTERSON DOB: [REDACTED] PT TEL# 704/349-0802 ACCT#: [REDACTED] STUDY DATE: [REDACTED] Dear Andrei Munzer, MD: PROCEDURE: BILATERAL SCREENING [DOCUMENT: path_biopsy_external_read.pdf] Patient: 252983RAM PATTERSON, NADIA L Acct#: [REDACTED] [MA Stereotactic BX 2 Sites [MABX05] - Breast - L] Scheduled: May 05, 2025 10:52 To: [REDACTED] Page: 1/2 From: Pathline [REDACTED] LABORATORY MEDICINE ASSOCIATES, LLP Surgical Pathology Report Montefiore Nyack Hospital Laboratory 160 North Midland Ave, Nyack NY [REDACTED] Tel: 845 348 2270 Fax: 845 348 8430 PATIENT Patterson, Nadia L ST25-010494 Steven Reichard, DO 185 First Street COLLECTED: [REDACTED] Hudson Valley Radiology Associates Apt 1 RECEIVED: [REDACTED] of Westchester Newburgh, NY [REDACTED] REPORTED: [REDACTED] 505 Route 208 DOB: [REDACTED] Monroe, NY 10950 AGE: 46 SEX: Female CC: Anderson, Melissa Patient [REDACTED] Final Diagnosis A. Left breast, medial calcifications, stereotactic biopsy, suros assisted: - Benign breast tissue. B. Left breast, medial tissue, stereotactic biopsy, suros assisted: - Benign breast tissue with a rare calcification within lobules. - Focal fibrocystic changes. C. Left breast, lateral calcifications, stereotactic biopsy, suros assisted: -Ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform type, with associated calcifications. -Radial sclerosing lesion. -Fibrocystic changes with calcifications. Breast Cancer Biomarker Results (Block C): Estrogen Receptor (ER): Positive( 98%, strong) Progesterone Receptor (PR): Positive( 100%, strong) Status of internal controls (for ER and PR immunohistochemistry): _X_ Internal control cells present and stain as expected. Methods: Immunohistochemistry (IHC) for ER and PR was performed at Pathline - Histopathology Services, Ramsey, NJ, and interpreted at Montefiore Nyack Hospital, Nyack, NY. ER and PR IHC are laboratory-developed tests. Cold ischemia and fixation times meet requirements specified in the latest version of the ASCO/CAP guidelines. The fixative used is 10% buffered formalin. The following primary antibodies were used on the Leica Bond III system: ER (SP1); PR (312). D. Left breast, lateral tissue, stereotactic biopsy, suros assisted: -Ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform type, -Radial sclerosing lesion. -Fibrocystic changes with calcifications. Electronically Signed By: [handwritten signature] Vandana Hoon, MD On [REDACTED] 01:46 PM EST Patterson, Nadia L Page 1 of 2 ST25-010494 Scanned Document Type:PATH, front side, page 1/2 Acquired on [REDACTED] 2:54 PM --- Patient: 252983RAM PATTERSON, NADIA L Acct#: [REDACTED] [MA Stereotactic BX 2 Sites [MABX05] - Breast - L] Scheduled: May 05, 2025 10:52 To: [REDACTED] Page: 2/2 From: Pathline Fax: [REDACTED] ACCESSION [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Clinical History: Left breast stereotactic biopsy, suros assisted, 2 sites. Gross Description: A) Received in formalin labeled with patient's name, [REDACTED] single tan- yellow to white cylindrical fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue core measuring 2.7 cm in length by 0.2 to 0.3 cm in diameter. Entirely submitted in one cassette. B) Received in formalin labeled with patient's name, [REDACTED] tan- yellow to white irregular to cylindrical fragments of fibrofatty soft tissue cores measuring and 2.7 x 2.6 x 0.2 cm in aggregate. Entirely submitted in two cassettes. C) Received in formalin labeled with patient's name,</data>
