    <node id="AH_UD_INV_L1_feature_13_receptor_status">
      <data key="d0">ClinicalFeature</data>
      <data key="d6">AH_UD_INV_L1_feature_13_receptor_status</data>
      <data key="d2">AH_UD_INV</data>
      <data key="d7">L1_feature_13_receptor_status</data>
      <data key="d8">{'tests_performed': {'value': 'ER, PR, HER2, and Ki67 tests', 'evidence': "Results of ER, PR, HER2, and Ki67 tests, to be performed on 'A1' sections"}, 'ER': {'value': 'ESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE &gt;95% STRONG', 'evidence': 'ESTROGEN RECEPTOR: &gt;95% STRONG... Since &gt;1% of tumor cell nuclei express estrogen receptors, this tumor is considered to be ESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE'}, 'PR': {'value': 'PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE ~90% STRONG', 'evidence': 'PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR: ~90% STRONG... Since &gt;1% of tumor cell nuclei express progesterone receptors, this tumor is considered to be PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE'}, 'HER2_IHC': {'value': 'HER2: 0 NEGATIVE', 'evidence': 'HER2: 0... result indicates NEGATIVE HER2 by immunohistochemistry'}, 'HER2_ISH': {'value': 'Not reported', 'evidence': ''}}</data>
      <data key="d9">1.0</data>
      <data key="d10" />
    </node>
    <node id="AH_UD_INV_0000_14fd3d">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
      <data key="d11">AH_UD_INV_0000_14fd3d</data>
      <data key="d2">AH_UD_INV</data>
      <data key="d3">AH_UD_INV</data>
      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_External1.pdf] 12:38 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Media Information 5:07 PM Connect - Test Details US-Guided Breast Core Biopsy - Left Important Information About Your Test Results ▼ Results Addendum EXAM: Pathology Results 25006788344; 25006788345 PATHOLOGY OUTCOME: Malignant PATHOLOGY RESULT: A. Breast, left, 3:00 NG, ultrasound guided core biopsy: Invasive ductal carcinoma and atypical lobular hyperplasia (ALH). Please see dedicated pathology report for the full assessment. RECOMMENDATION: Recommendation: Surgical Consultation Side: Left Follow-Up: Prompt follow up COMMENTS: The pathology results are concordant with the imaging findings. The results and recommendations were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. A secure Epic message was sent to referrer Dr. Kelly Greening. Electronically Signed By: Jill Gluskin on September 12, [REDACTED] PM Addended by Gluskin, Jill S, MD on [REDACTED] 2:49 PM Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression EXAM: Ultrasound guided core biopsy, Post procedure mammogram 25006788344; 25006788345 COMPARISON: 08/22/2025, [REDACTED] DESCRIPTION: INDICATION: 81-year-old with screening detected left breast 3 o'clock axis 6 cm from the nipple mass, for which ultrasound-guided biopsy was recommended. Following universal protocol, patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] with a "time out" prior to the procedure. Preliminary ultrasound evaluation of the left breast with special attention to the area of concern, confirms the presence of a 1.1 cm mass at the 3 o'clock axis, 6 cm from the nipple. Informed consent was obtained. https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24JixSALQ1fsHVQeXG593bQg-3D-3D-245TmaVnT8GN-2... 1/3 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:38 PM 1/4 12:38 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) 5:07 PM Connect - Test Details The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] the lesion was localized with real-time sonography. The skin was cleansed and marked. A total of 5 mL 1% lidocaine was used for local anesthesia. A lateral approach to the target was used. A 14-gauge needle, secured to a spring-loaded device, was advanced to the preselected target. A total of 5 biopsy specimens were obtained, with pre- and post-fire images documenting needle placement for each pass. Specimens were sent for pathologic analysis. A heart shaped biopsy clip was placed at the biopsy site. Following the procedure, the wound was cleansed and compressed. Steri-strips and sterile gauze were applied and the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] instructions. Images from the procedure were sent to PACS. Dr. Jill Gluskin was present during the entire procedure, performed the procedure and reviewed all pertinent imaging. There was minimal blood loss during the procedure. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] in good condition. PATHOLOGY STATUS: Results pending EXAM: Post procedure mammogram BREAST COMPOSITION: Density: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. FINDINGS: Post procedure mammogram demonstrates appropriate positioning of the heart shaped biopsy marker at the mammographic finding. IMPRESSION: Ultrasound-guided core biopsy of a left breast mass. ASSESSMENT: BI-RADS mammogram: Post procedure mammograms for marker placement Electronically Signed By: Jill Gluskin on September 08, 2025 04:59 PM Scans on Order 951017745 Scan on [REDACTED] 4:33 PM by Morelus, Princess; tech rad Scans Related to Order 951017745 Scan on [REDACTED] 12:33 PM by Contrino, Joely; bx protocol + questionnaire Scans on Order 951017745 Scan on [REDACTED] 4:43 PM by Tambadou, Isatou; Mammo Tech Result History US-Guided Breast Core Biopsy - Left (Order #951017745) on [REDACTED] Order Result History Report - Result Edited https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24JixSALQ1fsHVQeXG593bQg-3D-3D-245TmaVnT8GN-2... 2/3 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:38 PM 2/4 12:38 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) 9/15/25, 5:07 PM Connect - Test Details Images [Camera Icon] Scan 1 https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24JixSALQ1fsHVQeXG593bQg-3D-3D-245TmaVnT8GN-2... 3/3 Document Information Other: Outside Procedure US_GUIDED CORE Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:38 PM 3/4 12:38 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE OTHER ORDERS [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Waynasia Memminger | Msk Pas Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:38 PM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External2.pdf] [REDACTED] 12:39 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Media Information [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details MAMMOGRAPHY FOLLOWING CLIP PLACEMENT - LEFT Important Information About Your Test Results ⌄ Results Addendum EXAM: Pathology Results 2500678834; 2500678345 PATHOLOGY OUTCOME: Malignant PATHOLOGY RESULT: A: Breast, left, 3:00 N6, ultrasound guided core biopsy: Invasive ductal carcinoma and atypical lobular hyperplasia (ALH). Please see dedicated pathology report for the full assessment. RECOMMENDATION: Recommendation: Surgical Consultation Side: Left Follow-Up: Prompt follow up COMMENTS: The pathology results are concordant with the imaging findings. The results and recommendations were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED]. A secure Epic message was sent to referrer Dr. Kelly Stenning. Electronically Signed By: Jill Gluskin on September 12, [REDACTED] PM Addended by Gluskin, Jill S, MD on [REDACTED] 2:49 PM Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression EXAM: Ultrasound guided core biopsy, Post procedure mammogram 2500678834; 2500678345 COMPARISON: 08/22/2025, [REDACTED] DESCRIPTION: INDICATION: 81-year-old with screening detected left breast 3 o'clock axis 6 cm from the nipple mass, for which ultrasound-guided biopsy was recommended. Following universal protocol, patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] with a "time out" prior to the procedure. Preliminary ultrasound evaluation of the left breast with special attention to the area of concern, confirms the presence of a 1.1 cm mass at the 3 o'clock axis, 6 cm from the nipple. Informed consent was obtained. https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;accordianId=WP-24vPE9R4WLrMmQ35pNILJ-ZFA-3D-3D-24Z2LvRE1OG.... 1/3 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 1/4 [REDACTED] 12:39 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] the lesion was localized with real-time sonography. The skin was cleansed and marked. A total of 5 mL 1% lidocaine was used for local anesthesia. A lateral approach to the target was used. A 14-gauge needle, secured to a spring-loaded device, was advanced to the preselected target. A total of 5 biopsy specimens were obtained, with pre- and post-fire images documenting needle placement for each pass. Specimens were sent for pathologic analysis. A heart shaped biopsy</data>
