n: Ultrasound Biopsy Side: Left Follow-Up: Prompt follow up COMMENTS: OVERALL BI-RADS: 4C: Suspicious (moderate). Results and recommendations were discussed in person with the patient [REDACTED] time of examination. A reminder letter will be sent to the patient. Electronically Signed By: Michael DeStefano on August 22, 2025 01:04 PM Scans on Order 943272641 Scan on [REDACTED] 12:07 PM by Coronado, Connie: tech rad Result History US Breast Diagnostic Left (Order #943272641) on [REDACTED] Order Result History Report Images [Camera icon] Scan 1 https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;orderid=WP-24qgsZ5d3R29NaSTrkYOodw-3D-3D-24zVqJADaOMXz... 2/2 Document Information Misc Administration: Outside Radiology, Breast US Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:40 PM 2/3 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE OTHER ORDERS [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Waynasia Memminger | Msk Pas Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:40 PM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External4.pdf] [REDACTED] 12:41 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Media Information [REDACTED] 5:10 PM Connect - Test Details Mammogram Screening Digital with Tomosynthesis - Bilateral Important Information About Your Test Results ⌄ Results Out of Range Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression EXAM: Screening Mammogram 25003933434 COMPARISON: 06/17/2024, 03/27/2023, [REDACTED] and priors CLINICAL HISTORY: Screening. Last clinical breast exam: Feb</data>
