Id=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 2/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 2/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details Surgical Pathology (AP) Value New York-Presbyterian Hospital/Weill Cornell Medical Center Department of Pathology Surgical Pathology Laboratory Starr 1028 [REDACTED] 525 East 68th Street, NY,NY [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Surgical PathologyReport [REDACTED] Specimen Date: [REDACTED] In Lab Date: [REDACTED] 18:13 Report Date: [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 60 E 8TH ST APT 16L Cornell Medical Associates APT 16L 12 West 72nd Street New York, NY [REDACTED] Telephone: (646) 962-7800 Fax: 962-0413 [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Encounter #: 315706558 Location: WCINYP US 61ST Age/Sex: 81 / F Copy To: Jill S. Gluskin, MD CLINICAL INFORMATION: Abnormal finding on breast imaging (R92.8). Left breast 3:00 axis 6 cmFN 1.3 cm mass, BI-RADS 4C. DIAGNOSIS: A. Breast, left, 3:00 NG, ultrasound guided core biop sy: Invasive ductal carcinoma and atypical lobular hyperplasia (ALH). The invasive carcinoma is moderately differentiated, i.e., grade 2; 3+2+1, displays lobular features, and involves multiple cores, wherein it spans ~0.8 cm. Neither lymphovascular involvement nor in situ carcinoma is identified. A brisk lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate is absent (&lt;50%). Results of ER, PR, HER2, and Ki67 tests, to be performed on 'A1' sections, will follow. https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 3/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 3/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details follow. E-cadherin immunoreactivity of the invasive carcinoma, also on 'A1', supports the ductal phenotype of the invasive carcinoma. E-cadherin immunonegativity of the lesional cells ('A1') supports the diagnosis of ALH. Rebecca Fliorent/gea905 [REDACTED] GROSS DESCRIPTION: A. Received in formalin, the specimen is labeled "ultrasound-guided core biopsy left breast 3:00 N6" and consists of four cores of yellow-white tissue measuring from 0.8 x 0.1 x 0.1 cm to 1.5 x 0.1 x 0.1 cm. Also received are fragments of yellow- white soft tissue measuring 0.4 x 0.4 x 0.1 cm in aggregate. The specimen was placed in formalin at 4:36 p.m. and placed into the tissue processor at 4 o'clock. 100% submitted. Summary of sections: A1-A3. (RLK/REF) ** Electronically Signed Out ** Andy Phan, MD Attending [REDACTED] The attending [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] the diagnostic slides, and has edited the gross and microscopic portions of the report in rendering the final diagnosis. ICD Codes: A; C50.812 Z17.0 Z17.21 Billing Codes: A; 23883051, 23883421, 23883601(4) (Epic Outpatient Billing) SNOMED: AVP900/pm PROCEDURES/ADDENDA: Specimen: Left breast (invasive carcinoma) Block: A1 RESULTS OF ANCILLARY IMMUNOPATHOLOGY STUDIES PERCENTAGE OF POSITIVE CELLS STAINING INTENSITY ESTROGEN RECEPTOR: &gt;95% STRONG https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 4/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 4/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR: ~90% STRONG PROLIFERATION</data>
