      <data key="d12">10</data>
      <data key="d13">[REDACTED] GROSS DESCRIPTION: A. Received in formalin, the specimen is labeled "ultrasound-guided core biopsy left breast 3:00 N6" and consists of four cores of yellow-white tissue measuring from 0.8 x 0.1 x 0.1 cm to 1.5 x 0.1 x 0.1 cm. Also received are fragments of yellow- white soft tissue measuring 0.4 x 0.4 x 0.1 cm in aggregate. The specimen was placed in formalin at 4:36 p.m. and placed into the tissue processor at 4 o'clock. 100% submitted. Summary of sections: A1-A3. (RLK/REF) ** Electronically Signed Out ** Andy Phan, MD Attending [REDACTED] The attending [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] the diagnostic slides, and has edited the gross and microscopic portions of the report in rendering the final diagnosis. ICD Codes: A; C50.812 Z17.0 Z17.21 Billing Codes: A; 23883051, 23883421, 23883601(4) (Epic Outpatient Billing) SNOMED: AVP900/pm PROCEDURES/ADDENDA: Specimen: Left breast (invasive carcinoma) Block: A1 RESULTS OF ANCILLARY IMMUNOPATHOLOGY STUDIES PERCENTAGE OF POSITIVE CELLS STAINING INTENSITY ESTROGEN RECEPTOR: &gt;95% STRONG https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 4/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 4/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR: ~90% STRONG PROLIFERATION INDEX (Ki-67): 20% HER2: 0 INTERPRETATION: Since &gt;1% of tumor cell nuclei express estrogen receptors, this tumor is considered to be ESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE. Since &gt;1% of tumor cell nuclei express progesterone receptors, this tumor is considered to be PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE. HER2: no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] result indicates NEGATIVE HER2 by immunohistochemistry. This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Immunopathology Laboratory. It has not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary. This test is used for clinical purposes. It should not be regarded as investigational or for research. This laboratory is certified under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amen dments of 1988 (CLIA-88) as qualified to perform high complexity clinical laboratory testing. Antibodies and methodology: ER (Ventana/Roche SP1); PR (Leica, 16); Anti-HER2/neu (4B5) Rabbit Monoclonal Primary Antibody (Ventana/Roche)/Ultraview Universal DAB Detection Kit; Ki-67 (Dako MiB-1). The interpretation criteria are in accordance with the guidelines of the American Society of Clinical Oncology/College of American Pathologists Guideline Recommendations for Immunohistochemical Testing of Estrogen and Progesterone Receptors in Breast Cancer by American Society of Clinical Oncology (2010 and 2020) and American Society of Clinical Oncology/College of American Pathologists Guideline and Focused Update Recommendations for Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2 Testing in Breast Cancer in Journal of Clinical Oncology (2007, 2013, and 2018). Duration of fixation in neutral buffered formalin is between 6 and 72 hours. This assay has not been validated decalcified tissues. Results should be interpreted with caution given the likelihood of false negativity on decalcified specimens. ** Electronically Signed Out By ** Andy Phan, MD Attending [REDACTED] The attending [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] the diagnostic slides, and has edited the gross and microscopic portions of the report in rendering the https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 5/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 5/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details final diagnosis. All control slides for immunohistochemical tests show appropriate immunoreactivity. Immunohistochemical, in-situ hybridization and flow cytometric assays were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Immunopathology Laboratory. The limit of enumeration for flow cytometry minimal residual diagnosis (MRD) detection assays is 0.01% of viable cells. These tests have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary. These tests are used for clinical purposes and should not be regarded as investigational or for research. This laboratory is certified under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments of 1988 (CLIA- 88) as qualified to perform high complexity clinical laboratory testing. The testing was performed at New York Presbyterian - Weill Cornell Medical Center, 525 East 68th Street, New York, NY [REDACTED] CLIA # 33D0653378. https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 6/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 6/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details 📄 Scan 1 Ordering provider: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Collection date: Sep 08, 2025 4:05 PM Specimens: AP Specimen (Surgical) Result date: Sep 12, 2025 2:14 PM Result status: Final (Edited) Resulting lab: CORNELL PATHOLOGY https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD-2BHGjXzd4FBGut-2Fw-2Fw-3D-3D-24qwr1UTNI... 7/9 Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 12:39 PM 7/10 [REDACTED] 12:40 PM Day, Ursula (MR # 39095007) [REDACTED] 5:08 PM Connect - Test Details https://www.myconnectnyc.org/mychart/app/test-results/details?pageMode=1&amp;recorderId=WP-24CaeD