      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_Bmmg_Rus_external.pdf] 10:42 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] Prisma Health Outside Information Results US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC RIGHT (Order [REDACTED]) US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC RIGHT Order: [REDACTED] Narrative FROM: PRISMA HEALTH PATEWOOD OUTPATIENT CENTER 200 Patewood Drive, Ste A16 Greenville, SC [REDACTED] Phone: [REDACTED] BILATERAL DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM 3D/2D AND TARGETED RIGHT ULTRASOUND: [REDACTED] No [REDACTED] Real-time ultrasound of the right breast was performed. The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Digital mammography views were performed including tomosynthesis. Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] right breast. Irregular spiculated high density mass within the upper inner right breast middle depth with associated pleomorphic calcifications measures approximately 5.8 x 4.0 x 3.5 cm (oblique TV, oblique AP, CC). There is skin thickening of the right breast predominantly involving the medial and inferior aspects. There is also mild right nipple retraction. ULTRASOUND: Targeted ultrasound of the palpable area of concern in the right breast 2:00 3 cm from the nipple demonstrates an irregular hypoechoic mass with internal specular reflections measuring approximately 6.0 x 2.4 x 4.0 cm. Skin thickening noted within the lower inner quadrant measuring up to 6 mm. Targeted ultrasound of the right axilla demonstrates an abnormal lymph node versus 2 adjacent abnormal lymph nodes, which is also palpable to the patient. IMPRESSION: HIGHLY SUGGESTIVE OF MALIGNANCY, ULTRASOUND HIGHLY SUGGESTIVE OF MALIGNANCY 1. Right breast mass is highly suspicious of malignancy. 2. Right breast skin thickening for which clinical evaluation is recommended for possible punch biopsy. 3. Abnormal right axillary lymphadenopathy is suspicious. Ultrasound-guided biopsy of the right breast mass and abnormal axillary lymph node is recommended. Electronically Signed By: Allie Franklin MD [REDACTED] 11:39:06 letter sent: Same Day BiRads 4/5 OVERALL STUDY BIRADS: Category 5: Highly Suggestive of Malignancy Images on Order [REDACTED] External Radiology and Imaging - Scan on [REDACTED] US Breast Complete Right Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 10:42 PM 1/2 10:42 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [THIS IS FIGURE: Ultrasound image showing breast tissue] Exam End: [REDACTED] 15:24 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 14:51 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 11:39 Received From: Prisma Health Result Received: [REDACTED] 11:46 View Encounter Received Information Procedure US BREAST COMPLETE RIGHT Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 10:42 PM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_dxmmg_external.pdf] [REDACTED] 10:49 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [LOGO] Prisma Health Outside Information Results BI MAMMO DIAGNOSTIC RIGHT (Order [REDACTED]) BI MAMMO DIAGNOSTIC RIGHT Order: [REDACTED] Narrative FROM: PRISMA HEALTH PATEWOOD OUTPATIENT CENTER 200 Patewood Drive, Ste A16 Greenville, SC [REDACTED] Phone: [REDACTED] UNILATERAL RIGHT DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM: [REDACTED] Comparison is made to exams dated: [REDACTED] ultrasound and [REDACTED] mammogram - PRISMA HEALTH PATEWOOD OUTPATIENT CENTER. The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Unilateral mammogram was performed of the right breast post ultrasound guided biopsy of the mass located in the 2:00 position with COIL clip placement and post ultrasound guided biopsy of the abnormal lymph node located in the right axilla with VISION clip placement. Post procedure imaging confirms good COIL clip placement with respect to the palpable mass seen mammographically and good VISION clip placement in an abnormal right axillary lymph node. IMPRESSION: POST PROCEDURE MAMMOGRAM FOR MARKER PLACEMENT AS ABOVE. Electronically Signed By: Pavani Shah M.D. [REDACTED] 10:10:57 Mammogram BI-RADS: Post-Procedure Mammogram for Marker Placement Images on Order [REDACTED] External Radiology and Imaging - Scan on [REDACTED] Mammography diagnostic right [THIS IS IMAGE: A medical scan/mammogram image with "d" markers visible] Exam End: [REDACTED] 09:01 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 10:10 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 08:44 Result Received: [REDACTED] 11:46 Received From: Prisma Health C Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 10:49 PM 1/2 [REDACTED] 10:49 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 👁 View Encounter 🌙 Received Information Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 10:49 PM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_internal_review.pdf] [REDACTED] 10:52 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] FOREIGN TOMO BREAST BILATERAL Status: Edited Result - FINAL PACS Images (Link Unavailable) Show images for FOREIGN TOMO BREAST BILATERAL Addendum ADDENDUM: EXAM: REVIEW OF SUBMITTED BREAST IMAGING: BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS August 28, 2025: Technique: bilateral mammogram: tomosynthesis images were obtained. RIGHT LIMITED BREAST ULTRASOUND August 20, 2025: Technique: right breast us: limited breast ultrasound was performed. Electronically Signed By: TALI AMIR MD on [REDACTED] 3:27 PM Addended by Tali Amir, MD on [REDACTED] 3:27 PM Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression ACCESSION#(s): A000224096, A000224098 DATE: [REDACTED] 12:33 PM EXAM: REVIEW OF SUBMITTED BREAST IMAGING: BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS August 28, 2025: Technique: bilateral mammogram: tomosynthesis images were obtained. RIGHT LIMITED BREAST ULTRASOUND August 20, 2025: Technique: bilateral breast us: limited breast ultrasound was performed. CLINICAL HISTORY: Newly diagnosed palpable right breast cancer. COMPARISON(S): None FINDINGS: MAMMOGRAM: BREAST DENSITY: Heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. RIGHT BREAST: Subjacent to a BB denoting site of patient's palpable lump upper inner breast, 2:00 axis posterior depth there is a spiculated mass with associated architectural distortion. Associated calcifications appear to extend beyond the mass, not evaluated with magnification views. There is diffuse skin thickening of the lower breast, involving the periareolar. There is slight nipple retraction. A BB is noted overlying the right axilla. Palpable lymph nodes on ultrasound outside the field-of-view on mammogram. LEFT BREAST: Left outer central breast posterior depth there is a 1.4 cm asymmetry (CC 36/73; MLO 10/71). ULTRASOUND: Evaluation is limited as interpretation is based on static images. Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 10:52 PM 1/4 [REDACTED] 10:52 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] RIGHT BREAST: Labeled palpable, 2:00 axis III cm from the nipple there is a 6.0 x 2.5 x 4.0 cm irregular hypoechoic mass with indistinct margins, containing calcifications. Sonographic core biopsy was performed (limited needle position evaluation on submitted images). Post procedure mammogram demonstrates a coil marker in expected position. Outside pathology yielded invasive carcinoma. RIGHT AXILLA: Labeled palpable in the right axilla there is a 3.5 x 1.2 cm lymph node with nodular</data>
