      <data key="d13">cm from the nipple there is a 6.0 x 2.5 x 4.0 cm irregular hypoechoic mass with indistinct margins, containing calcifications. Sonographic core biopsy was performed (limited needle position evaluation on submitted images). Post procedure mammogram demonstrates a coil marker in expected position. Outside pathology yielded invasive carcinoma. RIGHT AXILLA: Labeled palpable in the right axilla there is a 3.5 x 1.2 cm lymph node with nodular cortical thickening to 0.7 cm. Ultrasound-guided core biopsy was performed with needle seen traversing the lymph node. Post procedure mammogram demonstrates a vision marker in expected position. Outside pathology was yielded metastatic carcinoma. ADDITIONAL IMAGING RECOMMENDED: 1. Right breast magnification views as surgically warranted 2. Left breast mammogram and possible subsequent ultrasound. If MRI is planned the queried asymmetry may be further evaluated on MRI in lieu of mammogram and ultrasound IMPRESSION: 1. Biopsy-proven palpable right breast cancer at the 2:00 axis with coil marker in expected position. MSK pathology review is pending. There is skin thickening of the lower right breast, areola and mild nipple retraction, suspicious. If it will alter surgical management, right breast magnification views are recommended to fully delineate extent of calcifications. 2. Metastatic right axillary lymphadenopathy with associated vision marker. MSK pathology review is pending. 3. Left breast asymmetry. Recommend left breast mammogram and possible subsequent ultrasound. If MRI is planned the queried asymmetry may be further evaluated on MRI in lieu of mammogram and ultrasound. Electronically Signed By: TALI AMIR MD on [REDACTED] 5:48 PM Exam Ended: [REDACTED] 12:33 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:27 📋 Order Details 📧 View Encounter 🧪 Lab and Collection Details 📧 Routing 🔄 Result History - Result Edited Result Care Coordination 📧 Patient [REDACTED] 📧 Released ⚠️ Not seen Study Details Open Study Details Weaver, Rachel Victoria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 10:52 PM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: Path_Biopsy.pdf] Case ID: [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] MRN: 974694034 PRISMA HEALTH™ Printing Department Weaver, Rachel 974694034 F, 48 yrs, [REDACTED] Surgicals (Final result) [REDACTED] Authorizing Provider: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Ordering Location: Prisma Health Outpatient Collected: [REDACTED] 08:48 AM Radiology - Patewood Hospital Pathologist: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Specimens A Breast, Right, Right Breast 2:00 3cmfn (6cm mass), Coil Clip - Dr. P. Shah B Lymph Node, Axillary, Right abnormal axillary lymph node, Vision Clip - Dr. P. Shah Clinical Information Diagnosis: N63.10 - Mass of right breast, unspecified quadrant [ICD-10-CM] Final Diagnosis A. Right breast, 2:00, 3 cm from nipple, 6 cm mass, coil clip, ultrasound-guided core biopsy: Invasive carcinoma of no [REDACTED] type. Histologic grade: 3 (poorly differentiated); (3 for tubule formation, 3 for nuclear pleomorphism, and 3 for mitotic activity). Tumor size: 15 mm on submitted cores. Presence of associated DCIS/LCIS: Not identified. Microcalcifications: Absent. Lymph-vascular space extension: Not identified. Hormone receptor and HER2 status: Pending. Addendum report to follow. Cold ischemia time: &lt;1 minute. Overall formalin fixation time: 12-14 hours. See comment. B. Right abnormal axillary lymph node, vision clip, ultrasound-guided core biopsy: Metastatic carcinoma. Size of metastatic deposit: At least 14 mm. Electronically signed by Abbie Lee Husman, MD on [REDACTED] at 0926 EDT Comment Clinical and radiographic correlation is recommended. [REDACTED] Page: 1 of 2 Printed: [REDACTED] 9:26 AM Case ID: [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] MRN: 974694034 PRISMA HEALTH™ Printing Department Findings were emailed to Dr. Shah at 9:24 AM on [REDACTED] Gross Description A. Breast, Right. Received in formalin labeled with the patient's proper identification and "right breast 2:00 3 cm FN (6 cm mass)," is a 1.7 x 0.4 x 0.2 cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue fragments. The specimen is inked green and submitted entirely in cassette A1. Time out of body: 8:48 AM September 2, 2025 Time placed in formalin: 848 Total time in formalin: 12 to 14 hours B. Lymph Node, Axillary. Received in formalin labeled with the patient's proper identification and "right abnormal axillary lymph node," is a 1.6 x 0.4 x 0.2 cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue fragments. The specimen is inked yellow and submitted entirely in cassette B1. Time out of body: 8:48 AM September 2, 2025 Time placed in formalin: 848 Total time in formalin: 12 to 14 hours SWB Microscopic Description A. The tissue is inked green, corresponding with the gross description. There is invasive carcinoma. The Nottingham histologic score is 3 for tubule formation, 3 for nuclear pleomorphism, and 3 for mitotic activity for an overall grade of 3. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] seen. B. The tissue is inked yellow, corresponding with the gross description. Sections show a lymph node involved by metastatic carcinoma. The metastatic deposit measures at least 14 mm. Blocks for Additional Testing A1 Disclaimer Unless otherwise specified, formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded sections, all routine, IHC, or special stains and cytology screening, are performed at PCI Laboratory, 8 Memorial Medical Ct., Greenville, SC [REDACTED] Resulting Labs GMH PRISMA HEALTH GREENVILLE MEMORIAL HOSPITAL LABORATORY, 701 Grove Rd., GREENVILLE SC [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Page: 2 of 2 Printed: [REDACTED] 9:26 AM [DOCUMENT: Path_biopsy2.pdf] [REDACTED] 10:45 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria (MR # 39091629) Media Information PATHOLOGY 8 Memorial Medical Court CONSULTANTS Phone: (864) 295-3492 Greenville, SC [REDACTED] specialized diagnostic services Fax: (864) 455-8926 IHC Prognostic Report Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDA