      <data key="d12">10</data>
      <data key="d13">literature that adjuvant endocrine therapy (tamoxifen) significantly decreases the risk of local and systemic tumor invasion, and/or future invasive cancer in these patients. Although only ER should be used to select these patients for endocrine therapy, reporting PR results may still provide prognostic information and is considered optional in DCIS patients. With selected invasive breast cancer subtypes, ER results are usually histologically concordant with these tumors. Thus, when tumor histology is concordant with ER results (&lt; 10%, staining intensity (1+), and/or is reported as "ER-POSITIVE." But if the tumor histology is not concordant with these results, ER should be repeated. Staining intensity (1+) OR any other ER result are classified in relation to tumor histology, invasive lobular carcinoma (ILC), or is cytoplasm is staining instead of nuclear, the pathologist must correlate with Histochemical findings on the Primary invasive carcinoma: (1) Discordant tumors that are aberrantly ER NEGATIVE. For example, LG invasive ductal carcinoma of no special type (Lobular Carcinoma Type, Apocrine differentiations), and (2) Discordant tumors that are aberrantly ER POSITIVE. For example, high grade ductal carcinomas or [?] Invasive papillary carcinomas]. In a recent study (Neunier, 2023), an optimal p53 Index cutoff of &gt; 35% was utilized to help identify luminal breast cancer with TP53 mutations in comparative patient specimens (with high specificity of 92% and accuracy of 89%). In contrast, an endocrine therapy response cutoff was 25% (with high specificity of 95% and accuracy of 90%). Scoring Criteria of HER2 (4B5) results for invasive breast carcinoma are substantiated as follows: [THIS IS TABLE: HER2 IHC Score table showing staining patterns and HER2 IHC Overall Results] HER2 IHC Staining Pattern of HER2 IHC results for Breast Carcinoma HER2 IHC Overall Result Score (Without Staining) No membrane staining is observed (Null) Negative (Null) 0+ (With Staining) Membrane staining that is incomplete and is faint/barely perceptible Negative (Ultra-Low) 1+ in &lt; 10% of invasive tumor cells 2+ Incomplete membrane staining that is faint/barely perceptible in &gt; 10% of invasive tumor cells OR Complete membrane staining that is non-uniform or weak in &lt; 10% of invasive tumor cells 3+ Weak to moderate complete membrane staining in &gt; 10% of tumor cells OR Complete membrane staining Equivocal that is intense but in &lt; 10% of tumor cells Circumferential membrane staining that is complete, intense, and &gt; 10% of invasive tumor cells Positive *HER2-Low encompasses both HER2 IHC 1+ and IHC 2+/FISH non-amplified. In accordance with the CAP Biomarker Reporting protocol, HER2 tests results of invasive breast cancer samples with either 2+ (Equivocal) or 3+ (Positive) should also provide the percentage of tumor cells with uniform, intense, complete membrane staining (3+ percentage). In addition, equivocal (2+) IHC results will be automatically referred to "HER2/CEP17 FISH testing." The HER2 FISH criteria remain unchanged as described in the ASCO/CAP Guidelines (2018), and the CAP Cancer Protocol for Breast Biomarker Testing (2020). Patient Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Weaver, Rachel Victoria (MR # 39091629) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:45 PM 3/5 [REDACTED] 10:45 PM Weaver, Rachel Victoria (MR # 39091629) 8 Memorial Medical Court PATHOLOGY Greenville, SC [REDACTED] CONSULTANTS Phone: (864) 295-3492 specialized diagnostic services Fax: (864) 455-8926 Patient Name IHC Prognostic Report Weaver, Rachel DOB Specimen ID Account CSI Case Number 03/24/1977 M25-35797-A1 C00499 WHC25-012873 Following the initial invasive needle core biopsy or HER2 Negative (IHC or FISH) or the biopsy is not representative of the different treatment or potential areas of invasive carcinoma, tissue processing error and HER2 may/shall be obtained if one of the invasive areas show a different result. (1) Absence of invasive tumor in the same tissue, (2) The core biopsy result is equivocal (2+) for HER2 by IHC (3) If the test is conclusive but histologic pattern is not compatible, (4) If all different treatment for potential areas show (5) Different results observed between the test results from the core biopsy of the tumor and the (6) Internal control tissue in the same slide is not satisfactory, (7) preanalytic factors (fixation delay&gt;72 h, temperature "hotspots") if any of these limitations are present, HER2 in situ hybridization test on separate specimens), (8) Non-formalin fixatives, delayed fixation &gt; 6 hours, and samples, are determinant. These conditions should NOT automatically be considered "INDETERMINATE." Instead, (9) If tumor shows a significant "intra-tumoral" heterogeneity without any immunoreactivity, or (o) test specimens show mixed areas: should an overall negative assessment should be made with determination due to possible preservation issues. HER2 INVASIVE AND IN BREAST CANCER: Patients who are HER2 Negative or HER2/neu result (Phased 3 DESTINY-Breast04 trial, NCT03734029), the use of T-DXd (fam-trastuzumab-deruxtecan) or trastuzumab 2+FISH not amplified, HER2/IHC 1+ but with metastatic, if only other metastatic single-agent chemotherapy regimens are available or trastuzumab-ad-lah-HER2 1+, 2+ or 3+ in HER2+ metastatic setting, These include the treatment of adult patients with unresectable and/or metastatic HER2-low (IHC1+or2+/ISH non-amplified) breast cancer who have received a prior anti-HER2-based or chemotherapy regimen in the metastatic setting, or relapse during or within 6 months of completing adjuvant chemotherapy. Since anti-HER2 signalin pathways. Patients with breast cancers that are HER2 IHC 3+ or ISH amplified may be eligible for several therapies that act on HER2 signaling pathways. HER2 FISH CRITERIA: [THIS IS TABLE: DUAL PROBE FISH ASSAY showing Groups 1-5 with HER2/CEP 17 ratio and Average HER2 copy number criteria] HER2 FISH GROUPINGS: HER2 POSITIVE Categories GROUP 1 HER2 Positive (regardless of IHC result) GROUP 2 AND Concurrent IHC 3+ GROUP 3 AND Concurrent IHC 3+ GROUP 4 AND Concurrent IHC 3+ GROUP 2 AND Concurrent IHC 0, 1+ or 2+ GROUP 3 AND Concurrent IHC 2, 3+ IHC = 3+ HER2 Positive (regardless of FISH result) GROUP 4 AND Concurrent IHC 0, 1+ or 2+ GROUP 5 References: 1. Bardia A, N Engl J Med. 2024;384:1143-1154. 2. Wolff AC, Arch Pathol Lab Med [REDACTED] 2023:147:1-43. 3. Jiang SCY, NPJ Breast Cancer 2</data>
