      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: imaging_US_internal.pdf] [REDACTED] 1:14 PM Faccidomo, Bonela [REDACTED] US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT Status: Final result PACS Images (Link Unavailable) Show images for US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT Related Results ⚠ SURGICAL PATHOLOGY ORDER Edited Result - FINAL [REDACTED] Final Diagnosis 1. Breast, Left; us left breast biopsy 7:00 periareolar; US BREAST CORE BIOPSY LEFT: Invasive carcinoma type Invasive mammary carcinoma Tumor size Invasive carcinoma spans at least 3.5 mm in this material Differentiation Moderately to poorly differentiated Results of immunohistochemical studies Will be reported in an addendum I ATTEST THAT THE ABOVE DIAGNOSIS IS BASED UPON MY PERSONAL EXAMINATION OF THE SLIDES (AND/OR OTHER MATERIAL), AND THAT I HAVE REVIEWED AND APPROVED THE REPORT. DILIP D GIRI, MD Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression ACCESSION#(s): [REDACTED] [REDACTED] DATE: [REDACTED] EXAM: BILATERAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM. Limited bilateral ultrasound. CLINICAL HISTORY: Annual mammogram. Status post right conservation surgery. TECHNIQUE: Mammographic examination was performed using full breast digital technique. Limited bilateral ultrasound. COMPARISON(S): 2024 dating back to 2020 LAST CLINICAL BREAST EXAM: Within the past year BREAST DENSITY: Scattered areas of fibroglandular density. FINDINGS: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] asymmetry in the outer middle depth right breast resolves with spot compression imaging. Limited same day right breast ultrasound demonstrate normal fibroglandular tissue in the outer right breast. Within the lower inner periareolar anterior depth left breast there is an irregular high dense spiculated mass with associated overlying skin retraction. Limited same day left breast ultrasound demonstrates an irregular shadowing hypervascular hypoechoic mass in the 7:00 periareolar left breast measuring 0.3 x 0.4 x 0.4 cm. This corresponds to mammographic abnormality. IMPRESSION: Faccidomo, Bonnie [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 1:14 PM 1/5 [REDACTED] 1:14 PM Faccidomo, Bonela [REDACTED] Left breast mass. Ultrasound-guided biopsy recommended. BI-RADS 4 - Suspicious RECOMMENDATION(S): Ultrasound-guided breast biopsy- Left Electronically Signed By: NICOLE SAPHIER MD on [REDACTED] 1:22 PM Result History US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT (Order [REDACTED] on [REDACTED] - Order Result History Report Supplies Charge Name ■ [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Quantity No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] ⚡ Implants No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Supplies Charge Name ■ [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Quantity No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Breast Imaging Recommendations - Order Faccidomo, Bonnie Ultrasound-guided breast biopsy - Left (Status: Resolved, Due: [REDACTED]) Overall Assessment: 4 - Suspicious Reading Physicians: Nicole Berardoni Saphier, MD Performed Procedures: US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT (Accession #: [REDACTED] [REDACTED]) Performing Departments: MON US No [REDACTED] Resolving appointments and orders Appt Appt Date Department Appt Status Visit Type Procedure Study Status [REDACTED] MON US Completed US BRST CORE US BREAST CORE BIOPSY LEFT Final 1:30 PM BX LEFT Result Letters Created by SAPHIER, NICOLE BERARDONI on [REDACTED] Mammography Recommendations Recommendation Side Entered By Due Ultrasound-guided breast Left Interface, Radiology Results In Resolved biopsy Reading Physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Nicole Berardoni Saphier, MD [REDACTED] 📞[REDACTED] Faccidomo, Bonnie [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 1:14 PM 2/5 [REDACTED] 1:14 PM Faccidomo, Bonela [REDACTED] Signed by Signed Time Phone Pager Nicole Berardoni Saphier, MD [REDACTED] 13:22 [REDACTED] Exam Information Status Exam Begun Exam Ended Final [REDACTED] 12:40 [REDACTED] 13:03 External Results Report Encounter There is an external results report available. View Encounter Total Sedation Time ✓ Follow-Ups No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Recommendation Procedure Ordered Performed Authorizing Ultrasound-guided 📋 US BREAST CORE [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Brendan J Mulholland breast biopsy BIOPSY LEFT ⚠ US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT Order: [REDACTED] Status: Final result Next appt: None Dx: Encounter for screening, unspecified Test Result Released: No [REDACTED] ■ [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Assessment Overall 4 - Suspicious Breast Density Overall Breast Composition b - Scattered fibroglandular density Details Reading Physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Nicole Berardoni Saphier, MD [REDACTED] Routine Physician [REDACTED] ■ [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Nicole Berardoni Saphier, MD Signed Narrative &amp; Impression ACCESSION#(s): [REDACTED] [REDACTED] DATE: [REDACTED] EXAM: BILATERAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM. Limited bilateral ultrasound. CLINICAL HISTORY: Annual mammogram. Status post right conservation surgery. TECHNIQUE: Mammographic examination was performed using full breast digital technique. Limited bilateral ultrasound. COMPARISON(S): 2024 dating back to 2020 LAST CLINICAL BREAST EXAM: Within the past year Faccidomo, Bonnie [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 1:14 PM 3/5 [REDACTED] 1:14 PM Faccidomo, Bonela [REDACTED] BREAST DENSITY: Scattered areas of fibroglandular density. FINDINGS: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] asymmetry in the outer middle depth right breast resolves with spot compression imaging. Limited same day right breast ultrasound demonstrate normal fibroglandular tissue in the outer right breast. Within the lower inner periareolar anterior depth left breast there is an irregular high dense spiculated mass with associated overlying skin retraction. Limited same day left breast ultrasound demonstrates an irregular shadowing hypervascular hypoechoic mass in the 7:00 periareolar left breast measuring 0.3 x 0.4 x 0.4 cm. This corresponds to mammographic abnormality. IMPRESSION: Left breast mass. Ultrasound-guided biopsy recommended. BI-RADS 4 - Suspicious RECOMMENDATION(S): Ultrasound-guided breast biopsy- Le