      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_External.pdf] [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Media Information 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 1 [REDACTED] RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) 3D DIAGNOSTIC BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM TOMO (051111462; 06212025 12:00am) 2025-08-21 16:53 02 0000000000 &gt;&gt; [REDACTED] 12 P 3/4 Jersey Diagnostic Imaging 532 North Wood Ave. (Suites 84 &amp;104a; P908-341-5252; (F) 908-241-6832 DIGITAL X-RAY - 3D MAMMOGRAPHY - ULTRASOUND - VASCULAR &amp; ECHO STUDIES - MRI PATIENT'S NAME: [REDACTED] DATE OF BIRTH: 13-Oct-1961 DATE OF SERVICE: 20-Aug-2025 04:40:00 PM 20-Aug-2025 05:50:07 PM PATIENT NO: [REDACTED] REF. DOCTOR: [REDACTED] Diagnostic Bilateral Mammogram with Tomosynthesis and Bilateral Ultrasound. INDICATION: Left breast lump. TECHNICAL FACTORS: Bilateral CC and MLO views were performed with tomosynthesis. Spot compression views of the left breast were done. Bilateral global sonography was performed. COMPARISON: None Available. BREAST DENSITY: B Scattered Fibroglandular tissue is seen. FINDINGS: A tubular-like mass lesion has been placed on the upper central left breast, elevating the site of reported palpable abnormality. There is an underlying 4 cm mass with spiculated and indistinct margins. Bilateral complete breast ultrasound was done. There is a hypoechoic mass with angular margins measuring 4.2 cm in the 11 o'clock position, 10 cm from the nipple in the left breast, corresponding to the area of reported palpable abnormality. An enlarged ipsilateral left lymph node measuring 1.1 cm in the left axilla. There is also an abnormal round lymph node measuring 1.1 cm in the left axilla as well. CONCLUSION: Highly suspicious left breast mass at the 11 o'clock position with suspicious corresponding axillary lymph nodes. Surgical consultation and tissue sampling are advised. The findings and recommendations were discussed with Nurse Janet over the phone on August 21, 2025 at 3:00 p.m. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 5 BI-RADS CATEGORY AS PER ACR: Category 0: Incomplete - Needs Additional Imaging Evaluation. Category 1: Negative. Category 2: Benign Finding - Routine Follow Up. Category 3: Probably Benign Finding - Short Interval Follow up to 6 Months. Category 4: Suspicious Finding - Biopsy should be considered. Category 5: Highly Suspicious or Malignancy - Appropriate Action Should be Taken Category 6: Biopsy Proven Malignancy Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM 1/7 [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 1 [REDACTED] RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) 2025-08-21 16:54 02 [REDACTED] &gt;&gt; 1855774547a 12 P 4/4 Jersey Diagnostic Imaging 532 North Wood Ave. (Suites 84 &amp;104a; P908-341-5252; (F) 908-241-6832 DIGITAL X-RAY - 3D MAMMOGRAPHY - ULTRASOUND - VASCULAR &amp; ECHO STUDIES - MRI PATIENT'S NAME: [REDACTED] DATE OF BIRTH: [REDACTED] DATE OF SERVICE: 20-Aug-2025 04:40:00 PM 20-Aug-2025 05:50:07 PM PATIENT NO: [REDACTED] REF. DOCTOR: [REDACTED] The patient has an annual outcome consistent with HIPAA, and allows 50% for doing biopsies. Palpable abnormalities line: Left inverted ultrasound. A focus mammographically that shows nodular tissue. At request by New York law the patient will be notified that she has dense breast. Dense breast tissue can make it harder to find cancer on a mammogram and can also be associated with an increased risk of breast cancer. Dr. Solange Bayard recommends that you and your doctor discuss what these results mean for you and whether [REDACTED] and bilateral breast ultrasound should be considered after discussion between the patient and [REDACTED] physician. Jersey Diagnostic Imaging endorses a comprehensive breast program for our patients and our patients care, imaging study. The program may involve multiple physicians and health care providers. We may assist patient in scheduling mammograms, breast ultrasound, breast MRI, breast biopsy, consultation, coordination of care between specialists, treatment options, genetics, health education, patient navigation and more. Our dedicated staff can help with all your breast care needs. Our facility has been inspected for and meets all the FDA (U.S. Food and Drug Administration) quality standards; therefore you are eligible to be offered all services offered at Jersey Diagnostic Imaging and you will receive the highest medical care and patient care available. A board accredited Fellowship trained breast radiologist has reviewed and interpreted your results. Jersey Diagnostic Imaging electronically reports your results to your primary care physician within 24-48 hours after completion of testing. The final results are available to the patient and physicians. Please call us if you have any questions or concerns regarding your results or if you need to schedule additional tests or procedures. We are proud to partner your health care provider. Thank you, and 2-4 hours after completion of the study. We will also provide the referring physician with additional imaging information if needed. Electronically Signed by SOLANGE BAYARD MD on 21-Aug-2025 [REDACTED]PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM 2/7 [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 1 [REDACTED] RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) 3D DIAGNOSTIC BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM TOMO (0517273604; 06202025 12:00am) 2025-09-04 10:28 02 0000000000 &gt;&gt; 1855774547a 2 P 1/3 Jersey Diagnostic Imaging DIGITAL X-RAY - 3D MAMMOGRAPHY - ULTRASOUND - VASCULAR &amp; ECHO EETRASOUNMD - MRI 532 NORTH WOOD AVENUE - LINDEN, NJ 07036 - TEL: 908-241-5252 - FAX: [REDACTED] [handwritten] 2nd Read -VI JDI 31 back to q ask [handwritten] 2015 August 21, 2025 Dear Dr. Shannon Fouty MD Please find the enclosed Mammogram and or Breast Ultrasound report for your patient: Derrica Rucker, DOB: [REDACTED] which shows a positive finding. Although we did fax this report to your office, by law what there is a positive result with Mammography and or Breast Ultrasound, we need to have a hard copy of this letter on file confirming your receipt - acknowledgement of the diagnostic report. Please sign and fax back. Also our facility (Jersey Diagnostic Imaging) is requesting a consultant the pathology report on all patients whom the radiologist [REDACTED] recommends a biopsy/pathology consultation. Please fax the enclosed report back from whichever the patient selects whether to your office attention or our facility. Thank you for your cooperation regarding this matter. Sincerely, Jersey Diagnostic Imaging Dear Dr. Shannon</data>
