      <data key="d13">Derrica (id [REDACTED]) 3D DIAGNOSTIC BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM TOMO (0517273604; 06202025 12:00am) 2025-09-04 10:28 02 0000000000 &gt;&gt; 1855774547a 2 P 1/3 Jersey Diagnostic Imaging DIGITAL X-RAY - 3D MAMMOGRAPHY - ULTRASOUND - VASCULAR &amp; ECHO EETRASOUNMD - MRI 532 NORTH WOOD AVENUE - LINDEN, NJ 07036 - TEL: 908-241-5252 - FAX: [REDACTED] [handwritten] 2nd Read -VI JDI 31 back to q ask [handwritten] 2015 August 21, 2025 Dear Dr. Shannon Fouty MD Please find the enclosed Mammogram and or Breast Ultrasound report for your patient: Derrica Rucker, DOB: [REDACTED] which shows a positive finding. Although we did fax this report to your office, by law what there is a positive result with Mammography and or Breast Ultrasound, we need to have a hard copy of this letter on file confirming your receipt - acknowledgement of the diagnostic report. Please sign and fax back. Also our facility (Jersey Diagnostic Imaging) is requesting a consultant the pathology report on all patients whom the radiologist [REDACTED] recommends a biopsy/pathology consultation. Please fax the enclosed report back from whichever the patient selects whether to your office attention or our facility. Thank you for your cooperation regarding this matter. Sincerely, Jersey Diagnostic Imaging Dear Dr. Shannon Fouty MD Please see the following diagnostic report for your patient, which shows a positive finding. Please sign, date, print name and fax back to our office, at 908-241-6832. Signature_____________________________ Date______________ Printed name__________________________ Thank you! JDI Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM 3/7 [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 1 [REDACTED] 09-05-2025 18:35 P 2/3 RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) 2025-09-04 10:28 02 0000000000 &gt;&gt; 1855774547a 2 Jersey Diagnostic Imaging DIGITAL X-RAY - 3D MAMMOGRAPHY - ULTRASOUND - VASCULAR &amp; ECHO ULTRASOUND - MRI 532 NORTH WOOD AVENUE - LINDEN, NJ [REDACTED] TEL: [REDACTED] FAX: [REDACTED] Date: August 21, 2025 Dear Dr. Shannon Fouty MD As part of our Mammography and or Breast Ultrasound Program, an annually outcome analysis is performed on patients who had mammography reports concerning biopsy or surgical pathology consult. This outcome analysis is part of the FQJA mandated quality program. We would appreciate receiving the following information on the following patient: Patient [REDACTED] needs appropriate follow-up information for this patient [REDACTED] Please fax this letter to our facility either by mail or fax to (908) 241-6832. this letter to our facility either by mail or fax to (908) 241-6832. ____ Patient opted not to have biopsy at this time. ____ Upon further evaluation, a biopsy is not indicated at this time. ____ Patient [REDACTED] following: (PLEASE ATTACH A COPY OF THE PATHOLOGY REPORT) _________________________________________________ _________________________________________________ _________________________________________________ _________________________________________________ _________________________________________________ _________________________________________________ We thank you for your assistance in this matter. If you have any questions regarding this letter, please call (908) 241-5252. If you have questions regarding the release of this information on our HIPAA regulations, Section 164.512(b)(1)(i) of the HIPAA regulation allows a covered entity (e.g., mammography, pathology laboratory or physician) to release patient biopsy information to a Mammography facility for the purposes of outcome analysis. Further, where FQDA medical outcome analysis, the disclosure IS to a person as the MQSA regulation, states that Quality Assurance (QA) programs are FDA regulated process, and subject to MQSA guidelines. (QA processes are FDA regulated process, and all MQSA to the Quality Assurance of the process of care). Quality test mammography and (2) actions to the Quality, safety, or effectiveness of the product or activity. 4/7 Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] D 13/14 RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) 2025-09-04 10:29 02 0000000000 &gt;&gt; 1855774547a 2 P 3/3 Jersey Diagnostic Imaging 532 North Wood Ave. (Suites 84 [REDACTED] P908-341-5252 (F) 908-241-6832 DIGITAL X-RAY - 3D MAMMOGRAPHY - ULTRASOUND - VASCULAR &amp; ECHO ULTRASOUND - MRI PATIENT'S NAME: RUCKER, DERRICA DATE OF BIRTH: [REDACTED] DATE OF SERVICE: 20-Aug-2025 04:40:00 PM 20-Aug-2025 05:50:07 PM PATIENT NO: [REDACTED] REF. DOCTOR: [REDACTED] Diagnostic Bilateral Mammogram with Tomosynthesis and Bilateral Ultrasound. INDICATION: Left breast lump. TECHNICAL FACTORS: Bilateral CC and MLO views were performed with tomosynthesis. Spot compression views of the left breast were done. Bilateral global sonography was performed. COMPARISON: None Available. BREAST DENSITY: B Scattered Fibroglandular tissue is seen. FINDINGS: A tubular-like mass lesion has been placed on the upper central left breast, elevating the site of reported palpable abnormality. There is an underlying 4 cm mass with spiculated and indistinct margins. The ipsilateral mammographic abnormality is present on the right. Bilateral complete breast ultrasound was done. There is a hypoechoic mass with angular margins measuring 4.2 cm at the 11 o'clock position, 10 cm from the nipple in the left breast, corresponding to the area of reported palpable abnormality. An enlarged ipsilateral left lymph node measuring 1.1 cm in the left axilla. There is also an abnormal round lymph node measuring 1.1 cm in the left axilla as well. CONCLUSION: Highly suspicious left breast mass at the 11 o'clock position with suspicious corresponding axillary lymph nodes. Surgical consultation and tissue sampling are advised. The findings and recommendations were discussed with Nurse Janet over the phone on August 21, 2025 at 3:00 p.m. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 5 BI-RADS CATEGORY AS PER ACR: Category 0: Incomplete - Needs Additional Imaging Evaluation. Category 1: Negative. Category 2: Benign Finding - Routine Follow Up. Category 3: Probably Benign Finding - Short Interval Follow up to 6 Months. Category 4: Suspicious Finding - Biopsy should be considered. Category 5: Highly Suspicious of Malignancy - Appropriate Action Should be Taken Category 6: Biopsy Proven Malignancy Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM 5/7 [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 1 [REDACTED] RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) Lab Results Document Information Radiology and Imaging: Outside Radiology MAMMO Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180)</data>
