      <data key="d13">to the area of reported palpable abnormality. An enlarged ipsilateral left lymph node measuring 1.1 cm in the left axilla. There is also an abnormal round lymph node measuring 1.1 cm in the left axilla as well. CONCLUSION: Highly suspicious left breast mass at the 11 o'clock position with suspicious corresponding axillary lymph nodes. Surgical consultation and tissue sampling are advised. The findings and recommendations were discussed with Nurse Janet over the phone on August 21, 2025 at 3:00 p.m. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 5 BI-RADS CATEGORY AS PER ACR: Category 0: Incomplete - Needs Additional Imaging Evaluation. Category 1: Negative. Category 2: Benign Finding - Routine Follow Up. Category 3: Probably Benign Finding - Short Interval Follow up to 6 Months. Category 4: Suspicious Finding - Biopsy should be considered. Category 5: Highly Suspicious of Malignancy - Appropriate Action Should be Taken Category 6: Biopsy Proven Malignancy Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM 5/7 [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 1 [REDACTED] RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) Lab Results Document Information Radiology and Imaging: Outside Radiology MAMMO Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:32 PM 6/7 [REDACTED] 4:32 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) 00:00 Attached To [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External2.pdf] [REDACTED] 4:33 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Media Information 09-05-2025 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 0 6/14 RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) MRI BREAST BILATERAL (RT/LT) W/WO CONTRAST (4515521616, Final [REDACTED] 9:39am) [LOGO] Summit Health Summit Health Part of VillageMD® 524 Springfield [REDACTED] Westfield NJ [REDACTED] 908.233.6210 Patient Name: DERRICA RUCKER Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Patient MRN: 39092180 Accession Number: [REDACTED] Referring Doctor: WILLIAM DIEHL Exam Date: 06/26/2025 MRI BREAST BILATERAL (RT/LT) W/WO CONTRAST CLINICAL HISTORY: Highly suspicious imaging findings in the left breast and left axilla. Patient underwent ultrasound-guided biopsy to the left breast mass for melanoma 06/26/25. Pathology is pending. TECHNIQUE: Bilateral breast MRI was obtained using standard protocol. Multiple sequences were employed in the axial and sagittal planes, including axial T1 weighted, axial and sagittal fat suppressed T2 weighted and dynamic contrast-enhanced MRI pre- and post contrast. 20 ml of Gadolinium (MultiHance) was administered intravenously. Multiple reformats and subtraction imaging were obtained. COMPARISON: No prior breast MRI examinations are available for comparison. Correlation was made with prior relevant mammogram and screening from outside institution. DENSITY: There is scattered fibroglandular tissue. FINDINGS: There is mild background parenchymal enhancement. There is highly suspicious irregular enhancing and linear partially eccentric calcifications in the upper outer quadrant of the left breast, measuring about 3.5 cm. There is associated hippocampus nodules within the duct walls. This was recently biopsied. Pathology is pending. There is also a foci of enhancement inferiorly. The largest morphologically abnormal left auxiliary lymph node measures 3 cm and contains. biopsy marker clip. Pathology is pending at this time. There are no suspicious masses in the contralateral right breast. There is no right axillary lymphadenopathy. There is no internal mammary chain lymphadenopathy. There is no abnormal chest wall or skin enhancement. IMPRESSION: 1. Recently biopsied highly suspicious enhancing mass in the upper outer quadrant central left breast. There is associated hippocampus clip. Pathology is pending at this time. Is seen will follow up with the breast surgeon and radiologist regarding the pathology results and further management. Interpreted by a Board Certified Radiologist at Summit Health 973-404-0509 Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:33 PM 1/3 [REDACTED] 4:33 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) [REDACTED] 18:35 Datavant Fax Id: [REDACTED] 0 [REDACTED] RUCKER, Derrica (id [REDACTED]) RUCKER, DERRICA Page 2 of 2 06/26/2025 2. Largest left axillary lymphadenopathy. The largest lymph node morphologically abnormal left auxiliary lymph node central to the masses clip. Pathology is pending at this time. Patient will follow-up with the breast surgeon and oncologist regarding the further management. 3. No suspicious findings at the contralateral right breast. BI-RADS Category 6: Highly Suggestive for Malignancy Electronically signed by Meeqay Ramachan MD (Aug 28, 2025 14:45 34) Interpreted by a Board Certified Radiologist at Summit Health 973-404-0509 Document Information Radiology and Imaging: Outside Radiology MRI Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:33 PM 2/3 [REDACTED] 4:33 PM Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Jaslee Quinones | Msk Pas Rucker, Derrica Y (MR # 39092180) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:33 PM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Path_Biopsy.pdf] Case: 3580691-1 Patient [REDACTED] Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center New York, NY, [REDACTED] Phone [REDACTED] Fax [REDACTED] Needed By: September 09 2025 STAT REQUEST- URGENT! Authorization for Release of Medical Records and Protected Health Information (PHI) for Continuity of Care Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center and Dr. Giacomo Montagna hereby request the release of protected health information on the following patient [REDACTED] under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996[45 CFR 164.506], as amended ("HIPAA"). The below named patient [REDACTED] from Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center / Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Cen