she lost her job I was very preoccupied trying to look for a job. She finally started another job in June and then last week she woke up and noticed that the mass was now quite large. She got a mammogram and sonogram that showed a 4.1 cm solid mass along with left axillary lymphadenopathy. She has also recently started to experience some pain in the upper thoracic area. She has been in good health except for obesity. Her family history is significant for maternal grandmother who developed breast cancer around the age of 60 and her maternal great grandmother at an unknown age. She has one 2-year-old daughter. ROS Additionally reports: [REDACTED] There are no [REDACTED] neurologic, psychiatric, endocrine, metabolic or general symptoms than those described above Physical Exam On physical examination her neck is without masses, thyromegaly, adenopathy or bruits. Her breasts are symmetrical without skin or nipple changes. She is examined in the sitting and lying positions. There are no [REDACTED] in her left [REDACTED] abnormalities. In the left 11 o'clock position is a large 4 cm suspicious mass. She has palpable left axillary lymphadenopathy. Her right axilla is negative. Procedure Documentation Ultrasound Breast Biopsy: PREOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: BI-RADS 4 lesion, left breast. POSTOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: Same as above. [REDACTED] 00:36:27 [REDACTED]Summit_Health → [REDACTED] [REDACTED]Summit_Health Page 007 RUCKER, DERRICA (ID #20740116, DOB: 10/13/1991) PROCEDURE: Ultrasound guided core needle biopsy. ANESTHESIA: Local PROCEDURE: Informed consent was obtained. A timeout was performed with the biopsy team. The breast was imaged. The lesion at the 11 o'clock position about 10 cm from the nipple was located. Correlation was made to prior exams. The breast was cleansed with Chlorhexadine. The skin and breast tissue was infiltrated with 4 cc of 1% Xylocaine. A skin incision was made. A lateral to medial 08:50:31 Summit_Health -&gt; 64163_Summit_Health Page 819 RUCKER, DERRICA (