      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_External.pdf] 4:03 PM Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) Media Information From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 1/3 Date: 8/22/2025 3:27:50 PM [LOGO: MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY] Tel (718) 428-1500 • Fax (718) 428-2675 www.mainstreetradiology.com Bayside 5th St Ave 42-75 Parsons Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11358 Bayside 26th Ave 48-01 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11361 Downtown Flushing 136-25 37th Ave, Flushing, NY 11354 Western Queens 73-06 Northern Blvd, Jackson Hts, NY 11372 Glendale 82-14 Cooper Ave, Glendale, NY 11385 :: YUAN YI LI, MD :: 39-16 PRINCE ST, SUITE 351 FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Referrer Phone: [REDACTED] Name: XULI MA PH: /917)602-1253 Gender: Female DOB: 8/8/1977 Patient [REDACTED] Exam Date: 8/1/2025 02:46 PM CC: QILI LI, MD Acc #: 10004224 Secondary ID: [REDACTED] Exam Name: [REDACTED] EXAM: MA 3D DIGITAL SCREENING MAMMOGRAPHY, US BREAST BILATERAL History: Patient [REDACTED] screening. Breast ultrasound to evaluate dense breasts. The patient [REDACTED] at age 40 - benign. The patient [REDACTED] no [REDACTED] Last reported clinical breast exam: Within the past year Risk factors: NCI 5 year:1.1% NCI Lifetime:9.8% Views obtained: Bilateral 3-D tomosynthesis MLO/CC views. Digital mammography was performed with additional image analysis utilizing CAD. Deep learning algorithms (AI) were applied to mammography images and DBT slices as a concurrent reading aid. Comparison: [REDACTED] (mammogram), [REDACTED] (mammogram), [REDACTED] (mammogram) and 07/26/2024 (mammogram). FINDINGS: The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Right lower central breast, posterior depth there is nodular focal asymmetry. Scattered benign punctate calcifications are again noted. Left central breast, middle depth there is a 0.8 cm nodule, stable. The left breast demonstrates no [REDACTED] abnormalities. BILATERAL BREAST ULTRASOUND, performed around the clock: This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:03 PM 1/4 4:03 PM Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 2/3 Date: 8/22/2025 3:27:50 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: XULI MA Date of Birth: 8/8/1977 Comparison: 7/26/2024, 7/7/2023, 7/22/2022. Breast composition: Heterogeneous RIGHT BREAST: 2:00, 2 cm from nipple is a hypoechoic lesion measuring 0.5 cm, stable. 6:00, 4 cm from nipple there is an irregular mass measuring 0.7 x 0.7 x 0.7 cm, newly visualized. There is an adjacent/abutting irregular mass measuring 0.5 x 0.4 x 0.4 cm This correlates with the right lower central breast mammographic nodule focal asymmetry. In its entirety, the 2 nodules measuring approximately 1.2 cm. Ultrasound-guided biopsy is recommended. No [REDACTED] LEFT BREAST: 11:00, 2 cm from nipple there is a circumscribed nodule measuring 0.8 cm, unchanged. No [REDACTED] IMPRESSION: Right 6:00 sonographic abutting irregular masses measuring 0.7 cm and 0.5 cm, which correlate with the right lower central mammographic nodule focal asymmetry. Ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy (x1) with clip placement and postprocedural mammogram is recommended. RECOMMENDATION: Recommendation: Ultrasound Biopsy. Right breast ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy clip placement and postprocedural mammogram. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 4 - Suspicious Abnormality Message left with medical secretary at Dr. YUAN YI LI MD's office on [REDACTED] 10:06 AM. A copy of this report will be faxed to the doctor's office. A letter has been sent to the patient [REDACTED] reminder system with a target due date for their next mammogram. Approximately 10% of breast carcinomas are not radiographically detectable. A negative report should not delay biopsy if a clinically suspicious mass is present. Dense breasts may obscure an underlying neoplasm. BIRADS 0: Incomplete - Need Additional Imaging Evaluation and/or Prior Mammograms for Comparison BIRADS 1: Negative BIRADS 2: Benign BIRADS 3: Probably Benign BIRADS 4: Suspicious Abnormality - Biopsy should be considered. BIRADS 5: Highly Suspicious of Malignancy This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:03 PM 2/4 4:03 PM Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 3/3 Date: 8/22/2025 3:27:50 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: 8/8/1977 BIRADS 6: Known Malignancy The New York State Department of Health requires us to indicate the date of the patient's last clinical breast examination. If NCI risk has been calculated, the results are based on information provided by the patient. Electronically signed by: Mrugank Shukla MD [REDACTED] 10:06 AM Workstation: MSR5READPC531 Report Electronically Signed by: Mrugank Shukla MD Report Electronically Signed on: 8/4/2025 10:00 AM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Misc Administration: Outside Radiology, Breast MAMMO Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:03 PM 3/4 4:03 PM Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Mary Everil Fletcher | Msk Pas Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 4:03 PM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External2.pdf] [REDACTED] 4:03 PM Ma, Xuli (MR # 39089057) Media Information From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 1/3 Date: 8/22/2025 3:27:35 PM [LOGO] MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY Bayside 33rd Ave 53-35 Francis Lewis Blvd. Bayside, NY 11358 Bayside 46th Ave 46-01 Francis Lewis Blvd. Bayside, NY 11361 Tel (718) 428-1500 • Fax (718) 428-2273 Downtown Flushing 136-20 37th Ave. Flushing, NY 11354 www.mainstreetradiology.com Whitestone Queens 25-06 Northern Blvd. Jackson Hts, NY 11372 Glendale 83-19 Cooper Ave. Glendale, NY 11385 :: YUAN YI LI, MD :: 39-16 PRINCE ST. SUITE 351 FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Referrer Phone: [REDACTED] Name: XULI MA Pt#: (917)602-1253 Gender: Female DOB: 8/8/1977 Patient [REDACTED] Exam Date: 8/1/2025 03:36 PM CC: QIL I LI, MD Acc #: 10004225 Secondary ID: [REDACTED] Exam Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] EXAM: MA 3D DIGITAL SCREENING MAMMOGRAPHY, US BREAST BILATERAL History: Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] screening. Breast ultrasound to evaluate dense breasts. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at age 40 - benign. The patient [REDACTED] no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Last reported clinical breast exam: Within the past year Risk factors: NCI 5 year:1.1% NCI Lifetime:9.8% Views obtained:</data>
