lient Comment# [C00-046-91 DIAGNOSIS A ● RIGHT BREAST LESION. HIGH SUSPICION. 1.3x0.9CM AT 5:00 1CM N. SONOGRAM GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY. DIAGNOSIS: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED Notes: Invasive carcinoma: Ductal, NOS. Nottingham score: 6/9 (tubules 3, nuclear grade 2, mitoses 1). Invasive tumor measures at least 1.1 cm. Ductal carcinoma in situ: Not identified. Microcalcifications: Not identified. Lymphovascular Invasion: No definite lymphovascular invasion is identified. Uninvolved breast tissue: Unremarkable. Receptor studies: ER: &gt;99% strong staining. PR: 100% strong staining. HER-2neu: Negative by IHC studies will be performed and reported separately. Ki67 approximately 20% E-cadherin is positive confirming ductal origin of tumor cells. P53 shows staining pattern supporting the diagnosis. Preliminary Reasons: ER, PR, HER2NEU, KI-67, P63, E-CADHERIN Blocks: 2:2, P63 Blocks: 1:2 [Extended technical note about immunohistochemical staining and interpretation] Color-key: Photomicrograph of A ● Cancer ★</data>
