      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_External1.pdf] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Outside Information Mammo US Breast, RIGHT Limited Anatomical Region Laterality Modality Breast right Ultrasound Impression Persistent architectural distortion at the right breast 9:00 axis, 4 cm the nipple is found to be a solid mass by ultrasound. This is considered suspicious based on the appearance on mammography and ultrasound. Recommendation: Right ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy is recommended for definitive histologic diagnosis. A core needle biopsy and clip placement were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] interested in core biopsy for diagnosis and will schedule an appointment with us for the procedure before she leaves the department today. BI-RADS code: 4 - Suspicious. 4C High suspicion for malignancy. This document passed e-signature verification by Dr. Amanda J Ferrell on [REDACTED] 3:05 PM Narrative UNILATERAL RIGHT DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM with TOMOSYNTHESIS AND RIGHT BREAST ULTRASOUND Procedure Date/Time: [REDACTED] 1:30 PM History: This is a 70-year-old asymptomatic woman who presents today for additional images of a questioned architectural distortion at about the 9:00 axis at middle depth and another in the lateral and posterior right breast. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Comparison: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Technique: Tomosynthesis and 2-dimensional spot compression and 90 degree images are obtained and reviewed. Findings: Density: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Right Breast: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] microcalcifications. There is a persistent architectural distortion at about the 9:00 axis at the junction of the anterior to middle one thirds of the breast tissue. This is 0.8 x 0.6 x 1.0 cm. The questioned area of distortion at the slightly lateral and posterior right breast, at the posterior fat parenchymal junction, has effaced. Right ultrasound: At the 9:00 axis, 4 cm the nipple there is a hypoechoic mass with ill-defined margins. This is irregular is oriented parallel to the skin Printed by Teneshia Taylor [TAYLOR14] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 1/2 [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] surface. This mass is 0.8 x 0.6 x 0.9 cm. This corresponds in size, shape, and location to the mammographic abnormality. Exam End: [REDACTED] 15:20 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 15:58 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 16:05 Received From: Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Result Received: [REDACTED] 12:28 View Encounter Printed by Teneshia Taylor [TAYLOR14] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External2.pdf] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Outside Information ⚠ Mammo Diagnostic W Tomosynthesis Right Anatomical Region Laterality Modality Breast right Mammography Impression Persistent architectural distortion at the right breast 9:00 axis, 4 cm the nipple is found to be a solid mass by ultrasound. This is considered suspicious based on the appearance on mammography and ultrasound. Recommendation: Right ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy is recommended for definitive histologic diagnosis. A core needle biopsy and clip placement were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] interested in core biopsy for diagnosis and will schedule an appointment with us for the procedure before she leaves the department today. BI-RADS code: 4 - Suspicious. 4C High suspicion for malignancy. This document passed e-signature verification by Dr. Amanda J Ferrell on [REDACTED] 3:05 PM Narrative UNILATERAL RIGHT DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM with TOMOSYNTHESIS AND RIGHT BREAST ULTRASOUND Procedure Date/Time: [REDACTED] 1:30 PM History: This is a 70-year-old asymptomatic woman who presents today for additional images of a questioned architectural distortion at about the 9:00 axis at middle depth and another in the lateral and posterior right breast. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Comparison: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Technique: Tomosynthesis and 2-dimensional spot compression and 90 degree images are obtained and reviewed. Findings: Density: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Right Breast: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] microcalcifications. There is a persistent architectural distortion at about the 9:00 axis at the junction of the anterior to middle one thirds of the breast tissue. This is 0.8 x 0.6 x 1.0 cm. The questioned area of distortion at the slightly lateral and posterior right breast, at the posterior fat parenchymal junction, has effaced. Right ultrasound: At the 9:00 axis, 4 cm the nipple there is a hypoechoic mass with ill-defined margins. This is irregular and oriented parallel to the skin Printed by Tomashia Taylor [TAYLOR14] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 1/2 [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] [REDACTED] surface. This mass is 0.8 x 0.6 x 0.9 cm. This corresponds in size, shape, and location to the mammographic abnormality. Exam End: [REDACTED] 14:40 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 15:58 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 16:05 Received From: Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Result Received: [REDACTED] 12:28 C ʘP View Encounter Printed by Tomashia Taylor [TAYLOR14] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External3.pdf] [REDACTED] 2:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Outside Information Mammo ABUS Bilat Anatomical Region Laterality Modality Breast bilateral Ultrasound Impression Impression: Negative Recommendation: She has been recalled from screening for additional views based on mammographic findings which are occult on the automated whole breast ultrasound. She remains a candidate for supplemental screening with automated whole breast ultrasound based on her breast tissue density assessment on