      <data key="d13">Breast bilateral Ultrasound Impression Impression: Negative Recommendation: She has been recalled from screening for additional views based on mammographic findings which are occult on the automated whole breast ultrasound. She remains a candidate for supplemental screening with automated whole breast ultrasound based on her breast tissue density assessment on mammography. BI-RADS: 1 - Negative. This document passed e-signature verification by Dr. Amanda J Ferrell on [REDACTED] 3:56 PM Narrative AUTOMATED WHOLE BREAST ULTRASOUND SCREENING (ABUS), BILATERAL Date/Time: [REDACTED] 2:31 PM History: Z12.39: Encounter for other screening for malignant neoplasm of breast, Dense breasts, unspecified. Comparison Ultrasound: [REDACTED] Comparison Mammography: This examination is performed in conjunction with screening mammography today. Technique: Whole breast ultrasound of each breast is performed. Sagittal and coronal reformatted images are rendered. Breast Composition: Homogeneous background echotexture - Fibroglandular Right Breast: Mass: None Architectural Distortion: None Adenopathy: None Other: None Left Breast: Mass: None Printed by Trinnphin Jaylor [TAYL97134] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 1/2 [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] Architectural Distortion: None Adenopathy: None Other: None Exam End: [REDACTED] 16:07 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 16:55 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 16:56 Received From: Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Result Received: [REDACTED] 12:28 View Encounter Printed by Trinnphin Jaylor [TAYL97134] 10/4/2025 12:48 PM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External4.pdf] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Outside Information ⚠ Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis Anatomical Region Laterality Modality Breast bilateral Mammography Impression Negative FINAL ASSESSMENT: BIRADS: Category 1 - Negative. RECOMMENDATION: As long as there is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] The imaging department will send a letter written in lay language of the results to the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] This report was generated at Baptist Health Medical Center - Little Rock Breast Center Narrative Digital Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis [REDACTED] 3:37 PM COMPARISON: Compared to: [REDACTED] Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis, [REDACTED] Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis, [REDACTED] Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis, [REDACTED] Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis, and [REDACTED] Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis FINDINGS: Tomosynthesis was performed in each standard projection, with a two dimensional view reconstructed from each data set. Standard digital views of each breast reveal they are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] microcalcifications, or area of architectural distortion. Tomosynthesis images were reviewed and show no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Exam End: [REDACTED] 16:37 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 16:45 Received From: Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Result Received: [REDACTED] 12:28 C ⚡F View Encounter 📋 Full Result Image Retrieve Images cannot be retrieved in the current platform. Report on [REDACTED] 4:37 PM EDT: MAMMO SCREENING BILATERAL Printed by Taneshia Taylor [TAYLOT14] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 1/2 [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External5.pdf] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM Coman, Mihaela [REDACTED] Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Outside Information (!) Mammo Screening W Tomosynthesis Bilateral Anatomical Region Laterality Modality Breast bilateral Mammography Impression Question of two areas of architectural distortion in the right lateral breast, new. Left breast is benign. Recommendation: She should return for right focal spot compression and 90 degrees series for further characterization. BI-RADS code: 0 - Incomplete-Needs additional imaging evaluation This document passed e-signature verification by Dr. Amanda J Ferrell on [REDACTED] 3:55 PM Narrative BILATERAL DIGITAL SCREENING MAMMOGRAMS WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS WITH CAD Procedure Date/Time: [REDACTED] 2:10 PM History: This is a 70-year-old asymptomatic woman. Comparison: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Technique: Tomosynthesis and 2-dimensional images are obtained and reviewed. Findings: Density: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Right breast: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] is a questioned area of architectural distortion at about the 9:00 axis at the junction of the anterior to middle one thirds of the breast tissue. There is also questioned architectural distortion at the lateral breast tissue along the posterior fat parenchymal junction without correlate on the MLO series. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] separately today. Left breast: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] architectural distortion. Exam End: [REDACTED] 15:27 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 16:52 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 16:55 Received From: Baptist Health Medical Center - Arkansas Result Received: [REDACTED] 12:28 View Encounter Printed by Teneshia Taylor [TAYLOR14] [REDACTED] 12:48 PM 1/1 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_Internal_Review.pdf] [REDACTED] 8:06 PM Coman, Mihaela Maria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] FOREIGN TOMO BREAST UNI Status: Final result PACS Images (Link Unavailable) Show images for FOREIGN TOMO BREAST UNI Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression ACCESSION#(s): A000253620, A000253621, A000253622, A000253623 DATE: [REDACTED] 9:12 AM EXAM: REVIEW OF SUBMITTED BREAST IMAGING: BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS September 30, 2025: Technique: bilateral mammogram: tomosynthesis images were obtained. BILATERAL COMPLETE BREAST ULTRASOUND September 30, 2025: Technique: bilateral breast us: whole breast ultrasound was performed, including sonographic evaluation of all four quadrants and the retroareolar tissues. RIGHT MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS [REDACTED] Technique: right mammogram: tomosynthesis images were obtained. RIGHT LIMITED BREAST ULTRASOUND [REDACTED] Technique: right breast us: limited breast ultrasound was performed. CLINICAL HISTORY: Recently diagnosed right breast invasive ductal carcinoma (internal review pending) . Review of outside imaging requested. COMPARISON(S): April 9, 2024, March 7, 2023, March 4, 2022 FINDINGS: MAMMOGRAM: BREAST DENSITY: Extremely dense, which lowers the sensitivity of mammography. RIGHT BREAST: * Subtle distortion in the anterior slightly upper, outer breast. The finding persists on diagnostic mammogram October 2, 2025, both on full 90 degree lateral and spot compression views. * Queried asymmetry in the posterior right central/slightly outer breast only the CC view. This dissipates on spot compression views, and is not seen on the 90 degree lateral view, suggesting overlapping dense fibroglandular tissue. LEFT BREAST: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] ULTRASOUND: Evaluation is limited as interpretation is based on automated whole breast images. RIGHT BREAST: * No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] breast automated ultrasound. * On subsequent diagnostic ultrasound October 2, 2025, in the 9:00 axis, 4 cm from the nipple, is an irregular hypoechoic mass measuring 0.9 x 0.7 x 0.8 cm, corresponding to the distortion on mammography. This underwent stereotactic biopsy on October 8, 2025.Outside pathology revealed invasive ductal carcinoma</data>
