      <data key="d13">[REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 8:06 PM 3/4 [REDACTED] 8:06 PM Coman, Mihaela Maria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Biopsy-proven invasive ductal carcinoma (MSK pathology review pending) in the right 9:00 breast. Biopsy marker along the anterior aspect of the distortion on postbiopsy mammogram. Electronically Signed By: PRIYA SHAH on [REDACTED] 5:05 PM Exam Ended: [REDACTED] 09:03 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 17:05 📄 Order Details 🏃 View Encounter 🧪 Lab and Collection Details 📧 Routing 🔄 Result History Result Care Coordination 👥 Patient [REDACTED] 📤 Released 🔔 Not seen Study Details Open Study Details Coman, Michaela Maria [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 8:06 PM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: Path_Biopsy.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:56 PM Coman, Mihaela Maria (MR # 39102467) Media Information [REDACTED] Baptist Health Baptist Health Medical Center 9601 Baptist Health Drive Little Rock, Arkansas 72205 Coman, Mihaela M 00543619 Department/Submitter Info: F, 70 yrs. [REDACTED] Baptist Health Breast Center 21 BURNTTREE CT, LITTLE ROCK AR [REDACTED] 9500 Kanis Road W: [REDACTED] M: [REDACTED] Little Rock AR [REDACTED] Addended Report: SURG Surgical Pathology Report (Final result) S25-[REDACTED] Authorizing Provider: [REDACTED] V. [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Health Breast Center Pathologist: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Collected: [REDACTED] 1436 Received: [REDACTED] 1509 Specimens A Breast, Right, RIGHT BREAST ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION @ 9:00 CLINICAL INFORMATION Right breast architectural distortion ABNORMAL/SIGNIFICANT FINDINGS (Abnormal) Yes Ref. Range: No FINAL DIAGNOSIS A. Breast, Right Architectural Distortion, Core Biopsy: - Invasive ductal carcinoma, Nottingham grade 1 of 3, 0.2 cm in this material; see comment. Electronically signed by Melody Harrison, MD on [REDACTED] at 1704 CDT DIAGNOSIS COMMENT A p63 immunostain demonstrates loss of myoepithelial cells in the areas of interest, supporting the above diagnosis. The Nottingham grade is based on scores of 2 for architecture, 2 for cytology, and 1 for mitotic activity. Ancillary studies for ER, PR, HER2, and Ki-67 are in progress, and the results will be issued in a supplemental report. GROSS DESCRIPTION Coman, Mihaela M 00543619 [REDACTED] 11:54 AM 1 of 4 9/L d I269888991L &lt;&lt; 029LZ0ZL05 A80J04J3d 38I3d8B 00:EL 5L-0L-5Z0Z Coman, Mihaela Maria (MR # 39102467) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:56 PM 1/5 [REDACTED] 7:56 PM Coman, Mihaela Maria (MR # 39102467) [REDACTED] Baptist Health Baptist Health Medical Center 9601 Baptist Health Drive Little Rock, Arkansas [REDACTED] A. RIGHT BREAST ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION @ 9:00 Received in 10% neutral buffered formalin in a container labeled with the patient's name [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] architectural distortion at 9:00 are multiple fragmented pieces of fibrofatty tissue that measure 2.7 cm in aggregate. This entire specimen is submitted. (Multiple sections, 1 block) Gross description performed by Savannah Jenkins ANCILLARY TESTING ESTROGEN AND PROGESTERONE RECEPTORS SOURCE: RIGHT BREAST (blk A1) Estrogen Receptor IHC: POSITIVE % of Nuclei Staining (ER): 94% Staining Intensity: STRONG Progesterone Receptor IHC: NEGATIVE % of Nuclei Staining (PR): &lt;1% Staining Intensity: N/A INTERPRETATION: See note NOTE: Staining of greater than or equal to 1% of tumor cell nuclei is considered positive or favorable and correlates with the presence of ER and PR receptors by biochemical assay. Staining of less than 1% of tumor cell nuclei is considered negative or unfavorable. Control case and benign tissue in the block stained appropriately. There are limited data on the overall benefit of endocrine therapies for patients with low level (1-10%) ER expression, but they currently suggest possible benefit; therefore, these patients are considered eligible for endocrine treatment. There are data that suggest invasive cancers with these results are heterogeneous in both behavior and biology and often have gene expression profiles more similar to ER-negative cancers. The "Low Positive" designation only applies to invasive carcinoma. HER-2/NEU RESULT: NEGATIVE Staining Intensity: 1+ INTERPRETATION: See note NOTE: This test is performed by immunohistochemical methodology. HER2/neu staining intensity of 3+ is considered Coman, Mihaela M 00543619 [REDACTED] 11:54 AM 2 of 4 9/Z d I269888991L &lt;&lt; 029LZ0ZL05 A80J04J3d 38I3d8B 00:EL 5L-0L-5Z0Z Coman, Mihaela Maria (MR # 39102467) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:56 PM 2/5 [REDACTED] 7:56 PM Coman, Mihaela Maria (MR # 39102467) [REDACTED] Baptist Health Baptist Health Medical Center 9601 Baptist Health Drive Little Rock, Arkansas 72205 unequivocally positive. Staining intensity of 2+ is considered equivocal, therefore in situ hybridization (ISH) analysis will be reflexively ordered by our laboratory and the results will be given in an addendum report. HER2/neu staining of 0 and 1+ is considered negative. If HER2/neu ISH is required on cases other than those with 2+ staining, please notify this office. Control case tissue and benign tissue in the block stain appropriately. KI-67 RESULT: FAVORABLE Percent Positive: 5.6% INTERPRETATION: See note NOTE: This test is performed by immunohistochemical methodology. Staining of less than 10% of tumor cell nuclei is considered negative or favorable. Staining of 10% to less than 20% of tumor cell nuclei is considered borderline. Staining of greater than or equal to 20% of tumor cell nuclei is unfavorable. This ER, PR, and Ki67 test was developed by Pathology Labs of Arkansas has been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. This laboratory is certified under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments of 1988 (CLIA) as qualified to perform high complexity clinical laboratory testing. These assays have not been validated on decalcified specimens or tissue other than breast. Nor is it FDA approved for these specimens. This test panel was analyzed using the Ventana Image Analysis System (DP200). Type of fixation, 10% neutral buffered formalin. Embedded in paraffin. Tissue is fixed in 10% NBF for 6 to 72 hours. As in the ASCO/CAP HER2 guideline, storage of slides for more than 6 weeks before analysis is not recommended. Immunohistochemical stains were performed on Ventana automated analyzers. Ventana Ultraview DAB detection system, antibodies: Anti ER clone SP1 Ventana, Anti PR clone 1E2 Ventana, Anti Ki 67 clone K-2 Ventana, Anti Her-2/neu clone 4B5 Ventana. Addendum electronically signed by Melody Harrison, MD on [REDACTED] at 1310 CDT DISCLAIMER Pathology report signed out by Pathology Laboratories of Arkansas at: Baptist Health Medical Center - Little Rock 9601 Baptist Health Dr., Little Rock, AR</data>
