      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_External1.pdf] [REDACTED] 3:29 PM Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) Media Information 08/25/2025 09:34 AM [REDACTED] FROM [REDACTED] Page: 3 SELECT DIAGNOSTIC Farzam Kashanian, M.D. IMAGING MEDICAL DIRECTOR 2530 OCEAN AVENUE, SUITE 1 [REDACTED] N.Y. 11229 TEL: (718)676-4350 FAX: (718)676-4357 Report Details Patient Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Gender: [REDACTED] Accession: [REDACTED] Referring Physician: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Report Text EXAM: DIGITAL BILATERAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM EXAM: BILATERAL BREAST ULTRASOUND History: Palpable lump in the upper outer right breast. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Technique: Bilateral MLO and Craniocaudal mammographic views were performed using digital technique. Findings: The breast parenchyma is heterogeneously dense, 50 to 75% fibroglandular, lowering the sensitivity of the study. Palpable nodule in the upper outer periareolar right breast was marked with a marker. Spot compression over this region demonstrates several ill defined nodular densities measuring 1.5 cm and smaller. These are irregular. Nodularity is also seen in the upper outer right breast. Within the left breast, mild nodularity is seen in the upper outer left breast. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Sonographic evaluation of both breasts was performed using a high frequency linear transducer. All four quadrants, retroareolar regions and axillae were evaluated bilaterally. The breast parenchyma is heterogeneously dense. Within the right breast, at the 10 o'clock retroareolar region, a lobulated irregular mass measures 1.6 x 1.4 x 1.8 cm corresponding to the palpable lump. An adjacent irregular nodule measures 0.7 x 0.7 x 0.6 cm. At the right 11 o'clock periareolar region, a lobulated nodule measures 1.0 x 1.0 x 0.8 cm. Right axillary lymph nodes are seen demonstrating thickened cortex. Within the left breast, an ill defined nodule at the 2 o'clock axis measures 0.7 x 0.6 x 0.6 cm. Benign appearing lymph nodes are seen in the left axilla. IMPRESSION: PALPABLE LUMP IN THE RIGHT RETROAREOLAR REGION CORRESPONDS TO 1.8 CM IRREGULAR SOLID MASS. AN ADJACENT 0.7 CM SOLID MASS IS ALSO SEEN AS WELL AS RIGHT 11 O'CLOCK 1.0 CM SOLID MASS. THESE ARE ALL SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY. 0.7 CM ILL DEFINED NODULE IS ALSO SEEN AT THE LEFT BREAST 2 O'CLOCK POSITION THAT IS ALSO SUSPICIOUS. LYMPH NODES IN THE RIGHT AXILLA ALSO SEEN THAT ARE INDETERMINATE. RECOMMEND FURTHER EVALUATION WITH ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY OF BOTH BREASTS. BILATERAL BREAST MRI WITH CONTRAST ENHANCEMENT IS ALSO RECOMMENDED. BI-RADS CATEGORY (SIGHTLY SUGGESTIVE OF MALIGNANCY-APPROPRIATE ACTION SHOULD BE TAKEN) THE RESULTS WERE REPORTED TO RADA AT DR TRAKHTENBERG'S OFFICE ON [REDACTED] Please be advised that the false negative rate of mammography is approximately 10% and management of a palpable mass should be based on clinical grounds. page 1 of 2 Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 3:29 PM 1/3 [REDACTED] 3:29 PM Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) 08/25/2025 09:34 AM TD:1646272408 FROM [REDACTED] Page: 4 As per the FDA requirements, a layman's letter has been generated and sent to your patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] results and recommendations of this breast imaging study. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] system and will be notified when they are due for their next breast imaging exam. FARZAM KASHANIAN MD Signed by: Kashanian, Farzam Date Signed: 6/15/2025 Transcribed By: TRANSCRIPTIONIST, EXCEL Date Transcribed: [REDACTED] page 2 of 2 Document Information Radiology and Imaging: Outside Radiology MAMMO Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 3:29 PM 2/3 [REDACTED] 3:29 PM Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Megan Thomas | Msk Pas Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 3:29 PM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External2.pdf] [REDACTED] 09:34 AM [REDACTED] FROM: [REDACTED] Page: 1 SELECT DIAGNOSTIC IMAGING Farzam Kashanian, M.D. MEDICAL DIRECTOR 2350 OCEAN AVENUE, SUITE 4 N.Y. 11229 TEL:718/676-4550 FAX:718/676-4557 Report Details Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Gender: F Accession: [REDACTED] Referring Physician: [REDACTED] Report Text EXAM: ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY OF TWO SITES IN THE RIGHT BREAST AND ONE SITE IN THE LEFT BREAST FOLLOWED BY CLIP PLACEMENT EXAM: DIAGNOSTIC BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM WITH ICAD History: This is followup to the mammogram and sonogram of [REDACTED] Technique: An initial targeted ultrasound was performed using a high frequency linear transducer. Within the right retroareolar region, a lobulated irregular mass measures 1.8 cm. At the right 11 o'clock axis periareolar region, a lobulated soft tissue nodule measures 1.0 cm. At the left 2 o'clock axis, 5 cm from the nipple, a hypoechoic nodule measures 0.6 cm. Consent: The patient [REDACTED] and alternative to the procedure. The risks include infection, bleeding. Informed consent was given by the patient. Procedure: Both breasts was prepped and draped in the usual sterile fashion. 1% lidocaine was used to infiltrate the skin and subcutaneous tissues. Under ultrasound guidance, a core needle biopsy was performed upon the right retroareolar nodule. A marker was deployed. Under ultrasound guidance, a core needle biopsy was performed upon the right 11 o'clock nodule. Marker was then deployed. Under ultrasound guidance, fine needle aspiration/core needle biopsy was performed upon the 0.6 left 2 o'clock nodule. A marker was then deployed. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] did not reveal a hematoma. The samples were submitted to CBL pathology laboratories for further evaluation. Bilateral diagnostic MLO and Craniocaudal views were performed that demonstrate bilateral markers with postbiopsy changes. IMPRESSION: STATUS POST ULTRASOUND GUIDED BIOPSY OF RIGHT RETROAREOLAR IRREGULAR NODULE, RIGHT 11 O'CLOCK NODULE AND LEFT 2 O'CLOCK NODULE. page 1 of 2 [REDACTED] 09:34 AM [REDACTED] FROM: [REDACTED] Page: 2 RESULTS: AS PER THE BREAST PATHOLOGY REPORT, THE DIAGNOSIS FOR THE RIGHT RETROAREOLAR NODULE AND RIGHT 11 O'CLOCK NODULE ARE INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA, ARCHITECTURAL GRADE 3. THE DIAGNOSIS FOR THE LEFT 2 O'CLOCK NODULE IS BENIGN BREAST TISSUE AND STROMAL FIBROSIS. THESE FINDINGS ARE CONCORDANT. FOLLOWUP WITH SURGICAL CONSULTATION IS ADVISED. BILATERAL BREAST MRI WITH CONTRAST ENHANCEMENT IS RECOMMENDED. BI-RADS CATEGORY 6(KNOWN BIOPSY-PROVEN MALIGNANCY-APPROPRIATE ACTION</data>
