      <data key="d13">was used to infiltrate the skin and subcutaneous tissues. Under ultrasound guidance, a core needle biopsy was performed upon the right retroareolar nodule. A marker was deployed. Under ultrasound guidance, a core needle biopsy was performed upon the right 11 o'clock nodule. Marker was then deployed. Under ultrasound guidance, fine needle aspiration/core needle biopsy was performed upon the 0.6 left 2 o'clock nodule. A marker was then deployed. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] did not reveal a hematoma. The samples were submitted to CBL pathology laboratories for further evaluation. Bilateral diagnostic MLO and Craniocaudal views were performed that demonstrate bilateral markers with postbiopsy changes. IMPRESSION: STATUS POST ULTRASOUND GUIDED BIOPSY OF RIGHT RETROAREOLAR IRREGULAR NODULE, RIGHT 11 O'CLOCK NODULE AND LEFT 2 O'CLOCK NODULE. page 1 of 2 [REDACTED] 09:34 AM [REDACTED] FROM: [REDACTED] Page: 2 RESULTS: AS PER THE BREAST PATHOLOGY REPORT, THE DIAGNOSIS FOR THE RIGHT RETROAREOLAR NODULE AND RIGHT 11 O'CLOCK NODULE ARE INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA, ARCHITECTURAL GRADE 3. THE DIAGNOSIS FOR THE LEFT 2 O'CLOCK NODULE IS BENIGN BREAST TISSUE AND STROMAL FIBROSIS. THESE FINDINGS ARE CONCORDANT. FOLLOWUP WITH SURGICAL CONSULTATION IS ADVISED. BILATERAL BREAST MRI WITH CONTRAST ENHANCEMENT IS RECOMMENDED. BI-RADS CATEGORY 6(KNOWN BIOPSY-PROVEN MALIGNANCY-APPROPRIATE ACTION SHOULD BE TAKEN) THE RESULTS WERE REPORTED TO IRADA AT DR TRAKHTENBERG'S OFFICE ON [REDACTED] FARZAM KASHANIAN MD Signed by: Kashanian, Farzam Date Signed: [REDACTED] Transcribed By: TRANSCRIPTIONIST, EXCEL Date Transcribed: [REDACTED] page 2 of 2 [DOCUMENT: Path_Biopsy.pdf] 3:31 PM Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) Media Information [Quest Diagnostics Logo] Quest Report Status: Final - Courtesy Copy MALASI, MARJETA Patient Information Specimen Information Client Information MALASI, MARJETA Specimen: CF096534V Client #: 48039280 NYNMAIL Requisition: 789152 KASHANIAN, FARZAM DOB: [REDACTED] AGE: [REDACTED] FARZAM KASHANIAN,MD Gender: F Fasting: U Collected: / 14:00 EDT 2350 OCEAN AVE STE 4 Phone: [REDACTED] Received: 08/19/2025 / 02:18 EDT [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] Faxed: 08/25/2025 / 16:48 EDT COMMENTS: ADD ON Test Name [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] AMD ER/PR, PARAFFIN BLOCK see note HISTOPATH TISSUE/BIOPSY TESTS: Processed Specimen Quantity (1) HER2, IHC WITH REFLEX TO FISH (1) CLINICAL DIAGNOSIS / INFORMATION: Interpretation of Submitting Facility: Infiltrating ductal carcinoma SITE OF BIOPSY / SOURCE: Block(s) - CT25-8077086-A2 Breast, right, retro areolar, core needle biopsy (1 blk) GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received is one paraffin-embedded tissue block labeled CT25-8077086-A2. MICROSCOPIC DESCRIPTION: The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. The paraffin sections [REDACTED] using a polymer based technique and DAB as a chromogen. Controls stain appropriately unless otherwise noted. Specimen Adequacy: Adequate for evaluation. Type of Fixation: Formalin Duration of Fixation: 6-48 hours Type of tissue processing: Routine Cold ischemic time: Not provided Estrogen Receptor (Dako clone EP1) Scoring Guide: Positive: &gt;1% / Low Positive: 1-10% / Negative: &lt;1% Progesterone Receptor (Dako clone PgR636) Scoring Guide: Positive: ≥/≥1% / Negative: &lt;1% HER2/neu(c-erbB-2) immunohistochemistry, Ventana Pathway 4B5. Specimen Adequacy: Adequate for evaluation. Internal and External Controls: Stain appropriately. There is no membrane staining of cells in the lesion. ------------------------ FINAL DIAGNOSIS ------------------------ SOURCE: BREAST, RIGHT, RETRO AREOLAR, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY ESTROGEN RECEPTOR (IHC): POSITIVE: ≥≥1%, STRONG INTENSITY PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR (IHC): POSITIVE: 95%, STRONG INTENSITY HER2: NEGATIVE FOR OVER-EXPRESSION, SCORE 0 - NO [REDACTED] [REDACTED] COMMENTS: In the DESTINY-Breast 04 and 06 trials, "HER2 Low" was considered IHC score 1+ or 2+/ISH negative, and "HER2 Ultra-Low" was HER2 IHC Score 0. CLIENT SERVICES: 866.697.8378 SPECIMEN: CF096534V PAGE 1 OF 4 Quest, Quest Diagnostics, the associated logos and all associated Quest Diagnostics marks are the trademarks of Quest Diagnostics. Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 3:31 PM 1/6 3:31 PM Malasi, Marjeta (MR # 39089385) [Quest Diagnostics Logo] Quest Report Status: Final - Courtesy Copy MALASI, MARJETA Patient Information Specimen Information Client Information MALASI, MARJETA Specimen: CF096534V Client #: 48039280 Collected: / 14:00 EDT KASHANIAN, FARZAM DOB: 04/05/1978 AGE: 47 Received: 08/19/2025 / 02:18 EDT Gender: F Fasting: U Faxed: [REDACTED] / [REDACTED] Patient: NG Test Name [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Lab 0 (pattern 0+) with membrane staining that is incomplete and faint/barely perceptible in less than or equal to 10% of tumor cells. Breast cancers with these staining patterns may be eligible for treatment with trastuzumab-deruxtecan in the metastatic setting (but those with no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]). *The oncoSIGN primary anti-HER2/neu (4B5) is a semi-quantitative immunohistochemistry assay to determine HER2/neu over-expression in breast cancer tissue that has been processed for histologic evaluation. This test has been approved by the FDA as an aid in the assessment of patients for whom trastuzumab (Herceptin) treatment is being considered. The kit used in the staining has been FDA approved for primary and metastatic cancers. As with any IHC type assay, a false negative result is possible. A negative result does not exclude the possibility of HER2/neu over-expression; if clinically warranted, a more sensitive DNA based methodology (i.e. FISH) for evaluating gene amplification may be indicated. This assay is performed in concordance with CAP/ASCO criteria. The results of the test may be altered/affected by variables beyond our laboratory's control, e.g. fixatives other than formalin and fixation times other than those recommended in the CAP/ASCO guidelines. The reporting ranges have been modified from the original FDA approved reporting criteria to reflect those recommended in the updated CAP/ASCO guidelines. This test is not intended as a confirmation of the original diagnosis and should be used in conjunction with other established risk factors, clinical and diagnostic procedures. Patients with breast cancers that are HER2 IHC 1+ or IHC 2+/ISH amplified may be eligible for several therapies that disrupt HER2 signaling pathways. Invasive breast cancers that are HER2 negative* (IHC 0, 1+ or 2+/ISH not-amplified) are more specifically considered "HER2-negative for protein overexpression/gene amplification" and overexpressed levels of the HER2 protein may be present in these cases. Patients with breast cancers that are HER2 IHC 1+ or IHC 2+/ISH not-amplified (within &lt;/= 10% of the tumor cells), 1+, or non-amplified/non-overexpressed may be eligible for a treatment that targets cytotoxic drug delivery. HER2 Reporting Guidelines per ASCO and CAP: Negative (Score 0): No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]</data>
