      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: Imaging_External.pdf] [REDACTED] 8:53 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Media Information O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services &gt; [REDACTED] pg 16 of 34 &gt; 06/25, 2:25 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse RIS ami Atlantic Medical Imaging Accurate answers. Fast. 6529 Black Horse Pike, Egg Harbor Township, NJ 08234 • P: [REDACTED] • F: [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] MRN: 39041184l Address: 629 SHORE ROAD DOB: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Acc #: [REDACTED] Referrer Phone#: (609) 926-6353 Sec Acct: [REDACTED] Referrer Fax#: [REDACTED] Exam Date: 6/9/2025 12:52 PM cc: cc: BILATERAL BREAST MRI WITHOUT AND WITH CONTRAST WITH COMPUTER-AIDED DETECTION [REDACTED] 12:00 AM INDICATION: 33 years old presenting for short interval follow-up for right upper outer breast enhancement and for correlation to prior mammographic finding on diagnostic mammogram dated [REDACTED] COMPARISON: 2/2/2024, [REDACTED] and 11/16/2023. Correlation is made to prior ultrasound biopsy dated [REDACTED] and diagnostic mammogrambreast ultrasound dated 8/4/2025. PERSONAL HISTORY/RISK FACTORS: Benign right breast ultrasound-guided biopsy in 2025. FAMILY HISTORY OF BREAST CANCER: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] RISK ASSESSMENT: The patient's lifetime breast cancer risk according to the Tyrer-Cuzick model is 7.7%. (Based on a revised TC model (version 8) which now incorporates breast density). TECHNIQUE: Multisequence, multiplanar images of both breasts were obtained without and with contrast. Subtracted MIP images were performed using the CAD stream system. The patient received: IV CONTRAST VIALS USED: Dotarem one 15cc vial. IV CONTRAST INJECTED: 15 cc. WASTED CONTRAST: 0 cc. The study was reviewed on the PACS workstation and in conjunction with the data supplied from computer aided detection software, CADstream. Available pathology was reviewed. FINDINGS: RIGHT BREAST: amims\WebForms\Patient\PatientInformation.aspx?pg=RG&amp;pt=39041184I 16/33 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:53 AM 1/3 [REDACTED] 8:53 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services &gt; [REDACTED] pg 17 of 34 &gt; 06/25, 2:25 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse RIS RATIO OF FIBROGLANDULAR TISSUE: Heterogeneously dense fibroglandular tissue. BACKGROUND PARENCHYMAL ENHANCEMENT: Marked, which limits sensitivity of this study. In the upper outer right breast, 8 cm from the nipple, there is an enhancing 7 mm mass (series 10 image 141, series 5 image 33, and CAD 36), likely correlate for previously identified mammographic asymmetry identified on study dated [REDACTED] Stereotactic guided biopsy is recommended. There are scattered complicated oil cysts some which demonstrate rim enhancement. Visualized portion of the axilla is unremarkable. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] LEFT BREAST: RATIO OF FIBROGLANDULAR TISSUE: Heterogeneously dense fibroglandular tissue. BACKGROUND PARENCHYMAL ENHANCEMENT: Marked, which limits sensitivity of this study. There is no suspicious enhancement. There are scattered complicated oil cysts some which demonstrate rim enhancement. Visualized portion of the axilla is unremarkable. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] IMPRESSION: 1. Right upper outer breast, 8 cm from the nipple, enhancing 7 mm mass, likely correlate for previously identified mammographic asymmetry identified on study dated 8/4/2025. Stereotactic guided biopsy is recommended. 2. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] BI-RADS: 4. Suspicious. MANAGEMENT RECOMMENDATIONS: Right breast stereotactic guided biopsy is recommended in the absence of clinical contraindication. If stereotactic guided biopsy is unsuccessful, MRI guided biopsy would then be recommended. If you are the referring physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] (609)650-0004 to reach a radiologist. Date Of Signature: 6/10/2025 8:53 AM Report Electronically Signed by: Kahn, D.O., Julia Report Electronically Signed on: [REDACTED] 08:53 AM Patient Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] amims\WebForms\Patient\Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Document Information Misc Administration: Outside Radiology, Breast MRI BREAST Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:53 AM 2/3 [REDACTED] 8:53 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) 10000 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Priscilla P. Hazel | Msk Pas Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:53 AM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External2.pdf] 8:54 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Media Information O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services • [REDACTED] pg 5 of 34 •04/25, 2:26 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS [LOGO: ami Atlantic Medical Imaging] Accurate answers. Fast. 30 East Maryland Avenue, Somers Point, NJ 08244 • P: [REDACTED] • F: [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] MRN: 39041194 Address: 590 SHORE RD STE 101 DOB: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Acc #: 207426 1676 Referrer Phone#: (609)926-8353 Svc Acct#: 207426 1876 Referrer Fax#: (555)451-0550 Exam Date: 8/4/2025 10:42 AM cc: cc: DIGITAL BILATERAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM with CAD and 3D DIGITAL TOMOGRAPHY AND BILATERAL BREAST ULTRASOUND: 8/4/2025 9:09 AM INDICATION: 53 years old presenting for further evaluation of increasing bilateral nipple inversion. COMPARISON: Multiple prior mammograms, the most recent dated [REDACTED] though dating back to [REDACTED]. Breast MRIs dated [REDACTED], [REDACTED] and [REDACTED]. PERSONAL HISTORY/RISK FACTORS: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. FAMILY HISTORY OF BREAST CANCER: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. RISK ASSESSMENT: The patient's lifetime breast cancer risk according to the Tyrer-Cuzick model is 7.7%. (Based on a revised TC model (version 8) which now incorporates breast density). DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM TECHNIQUE: 2D and 3D combo digital tomography images were obtained. Standard images were reviewed with computer-aided detection. BREAST DENSITY: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses (Category C). FINDINGS: There is an asymmetry superiorly on true lateral view at posterior depth, localizing to the lateral breast (true lateral slice 15/59), which persists with spot compression (true lateral spot compression slice 17/49). Elsewhere in either breast, there are stable mammographic findings including oil cysts and coarse calcifications. No suspicious finding is identified in the contralateral left breast. BILATERAL ULTRASOUND amiims\WebForms\Patient\PatientInformation.aspx?pg=RG&amp;pt=39041194 1 5/33 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:54 AM 1/3 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) pg 6 of 34 [REDACTED] 8:54 AM O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services [REDACTED] Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS •04/25, 2:26 PM Targeted sonographic</data>
