      <data key="d13">Breast MRIs dated [REDACTED], [REDACTED] and [REDACTED]. PERSONAL HISTORY/RISK FACTORS: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. FAMILY HISTORY OF BREAST CANCER: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. RISK ASSESSMENT: The patient's lifetime breast cancer risk according to the Tyrer-Cuzick model is 7.7%. (Based on a revised TC model (version 8) which now incorporates breast density). DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM TECHNIQUE: 2D and 3D combo digital tomography images were obtained. Standard images were reviewed with computer-aided detection. BREAST DENSITY: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses (Category C). FINDINGS: There is an asymmetry superiorly on true lateral view at posterior depth, localizing to the lateral breast (true lateral slice 15/59), which persists with spot compression (true lateral spot compression slice 17/49). Elsewhere in either breast, there are stable mammographic findings including oil cysts and coarse calcifications. No suspicious finding is identified in the contralateral left breast. BILATERAL ULTRASOUND amiims\WebForms\Patient\PatientInformation.aspx?pg=RG&amp;pt=39041194 1 5/33 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:54 AM 1/3 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) pg 6 of 34 [REDACTED] 8:54 AM O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services [REDACTED] Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS •04/25, 2:26 PM Targeted sonographic images of the bilateral retroareolar regions due to patient's concern of increasing nipple inversion and right upper outer quadrant in the area of questioned mammographic finding were obtained. In the bilateral retroareolar regions there is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] bilateral nipple inversion. At 10 00, 10 cm from the nipple there is an irregular hypoechoic mass measuring 0.5 x 0.2 x 0.3 cm. This finding corresponds to a mammographic asymmetry. Survey ultrasound of the right axilla shows normal morphology lymph nodes. IMPRESSION: (D) Right breast: 0.5 cm irregular hypoechoic mass at 10 00, 10 cm from the nipple, corresponding to a mammographic asymmetry. Ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy is recommended. (D) No right axillary adenopathy. (D) No suspicious mammographic or sonographic abnormality in the bilateral retroareolar regions to explain patient's bilateral increasing nipple inversion. (D) No suspicious mammographic finding in the left breast. BI-RADS 4B: Suspicious Finding RECOMMENDATION: Right breast ultrasound guided core needle biopsy should be performed in the absence of clinical contraindications. Recommend this ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy is performed prior to recommended short-term follow-up breast MRI. These findings and recommendations were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at opportunity to answer questions and acknowledge understanding. ******************************************************************************** In accordance with New Jersey law, the following statement must be included in all mammography reports, regardless of an individuals breast tissue density "Your mammogram may show that you have dense breast tissue as determined by the Breast Imaging Reporting and Data System established by the American College of Radiology. Dense breast tissue is very common and is not abnormal. However, in some cases, dense breast tissue can make it harder to find cancer or a mammogram and may also be associated with a risk factor for breast cancer. Discuss this and other risks for breast cancer that pertain to your personal medical history with your health care provider. A report of your results was sent to your health care provider. [REDACTED] [REDACTED] density at the website of the American College of Radiology. www.acr.org." [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] to reach a radiologist. If you are the referring physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED]. Date Of Signature: 8/4/2025 1:07 PM Report Electronically Signed by: Bhimani, D.O., Chandni Report Electronically Signed on: 8/4/2025 01:07 PM [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] amiims\WebForms\Patient\Patient [REDACTED] Document Information Misc Administration: Outside Radiology, Breast 2/3 MAMMO Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:54 AM [REDACTED] 8:54 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Priscilla P. Hazel | Msk Pas Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:54 AM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_Internal_review.pdf] [REDACTED] 8:55 AM Wirth, Susan A [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] FOREIGN US BREAST BILAT Status: Final result PACS Images (Link Unavailable) Show images for FOREIGN US BREAST BILAT Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression ACCESSION#[REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] DATE: [REDACTED] 3:43 PM EXAM: REVIEW OF SUBMITTED BREAST IMAGING: BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS August 4, 2025: Technique: bilateral mammogram: tomosynthesis images were obtained. BILATERAL LIMITED BREAST ULTRASOUND August 4, 2025: Technique: bilateral breast us: limited breast ultrasound was performed. BILATERAL BREAST MRI WITH AND WITHOUT IV CONTRAST September 19, 2025: Technique: bilateral breast MR: multiplanar, multisequence MR images were obtained before and after intravenous administration of gadolinium-based contrast agent. CLINICAL HISTORY: Newly diagnosed right breast cancer (MSK pathology review pending). Evaluate outside imaging. COMPARISON(S): Multiple prior exams, most recent September 25, 2023 and September 12, 2023 FINDINGS: MAMMOGRAM: BREAST DENSITY: Heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Unchanged appearance of bilateral areas of oil cysts and microcalcifications. RIGHT BREAST: In the upper outer quadrant of the right breast, posterior depth, best appreciated on the MLO view, is a 0.7 cm spiculated mass. The finding persists on same day spot compression views. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] mass on September 25, 2025. Post procedure mammogram shows a well-positioned stoplight biopsy marker in the upper outer right breast approximately 1 cm laterally displaced. And outside pathology showed invasive ductal carcinoma. LEFT BREAST: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] ULTRASOUND: Evaluation is limited as interpretation is based on static images. RIGHT BREAST: Hypoechoic mass at the 10:00 axis, 10 cm from the nipple measuring 0.3 x 0.5 x 0.2 cm. This mass underwent ultrasound-guided biopsy on August 8, 2025. Same day post procedure mammogram shows a Top-Hat biopsy marker within the upper outer right breast, posterior depth however not associated with the originally visualized mammographic mass. Outside pathology yielded benign results of benign breast tissue with focally prominent stromal fibrosis which is concordant with the sonographic appearance. RIGHT AXILLA: Not imaged. MRI: BREAST COMPOSITION:</data>
