      <data key="d13">LEFT BREAST: No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] OTHER: None. ADDITIONAL IMAGING RECOMMENDED: None IMPRESSION: Newly diagnosed right breast cancer with associated stoplight biopsy marker 1 cm laterally displaced. Appropriate action is recommended pending MSK pathology review. Wirth, Susan A [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 8:55 AM 3/4 [REDACTED] 8:55 AM Wirth, Susan A [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Electronically Signed By: MOLLY P. HOGAN MD on [REDACTED] 5:35 PM Exam Ended: [REDACTED] 15:37 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 17:35 📄 Order Details 🔗 View Encounter 🧪 Lab and Collection Details 📧 Routing 📈 Result History Result Care Coordination 📞 Patient [REDACTED] 📧 Released ⚠️ Not seen Study Details Open Study Details Wirth, Susan A [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 8:55 AM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: Path_biopsy.pdf] 8:52 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Media Information O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services [REDACTED] pg 7 of 34 10/6/25, 2:25 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS [LOGO: Atlantic Medical Imaging logo with text "Accurate answers. Fast."] 44 East Jimmie Leeds Road, Galloway, NJ [REDACTED] • P: [REDACTED] • F: [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] MRN: 930411541 Address: 599 SHORE RD STE 101 DOB: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Acc #: [REDACTED] Referrer Phone#: (609)926-8353 Spc Acc#: 2074296786 Referrer Fax#: [REDACTED] Exam Date: [REDACTED] 03:21 PM co: cp: Addendum 1 PATHOLOGY ADDENDUM CREATED [REDACTED] AM PROCEDURE: 1. Right breast ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy of right breast mass at 10:00 approximate 10 cm from nipple (tophat clip) Pathology demonstrates: "Benign breast tissue with focally prominent stromal fibrosis.". See complete pathology report, which has been faxed to the ordering clinicians office. MANAGEMENT: 1. The radiological imaging and pathology results are benign and concordant. 2. Patient was initially scheduled for breast MRI 8/14/2025. However, on phone conversation with her on [REDACTED] at 1015 she stated insurance authorization has been delayed and MRI had been rescheduled for 9/9/2025. At this time plan is to follow-up MRI findings to see if there is a region of enhancement anterior to the biopsy site by approximately 2 cm, corresponding to the region of questioned asymmetry on diagnostic mammography. [REDACTED] Pending MRI results decision will be made for MRI versus stereotactic biopsy versus short-term follow-up. The results and recommendations for follow-up were discussed by myself, Dr. Clinton Vesels, with and acknowledged by the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] understanding and all questions were answered to her satisfaction. Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] states the biopsy site is healing well. The results were also sent to the patient's clinician. amirisWebForms/PatientPatientInformation.aspx?cpºRGs*p=930411541 7/33 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:52 AM 1/4 [REDACTED] 8:52 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services pg 8 of 34 10/6/25, 2:25 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS If you are the referring physician: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] (609)650-0004 to reach a radiologist. Date Of Signature 8/14/2025 10:18 AM Transcribed By: Vesels, M.D., Clinton Transcribed Date: 8/14/2025 10:18 AM Electronically Signed by: Vesels, M.D., Clinton Signed Date: 8/14/2025 10:18 AM ULTRASOUND-GUIDED CORE BIOPSY RIGHT AND RIGHT POST-PROCEDURE MAMMOGRAM FOR MARKER PLACEMENT 8/5/2025 3:31 PM INDICATION: 53 years old, with irregular hypoechoic mass at 10:00 centimeters from the nipple with right breast asymmetry on mammography. COMPARISON: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 8/12/2023 Findings: The procedure including risks, benefits and alternatives were explained to the patient. The discussion of risks included but was not limited to pain, bleeding/bruising, and infection. The patient was given the opportunity to ask questions and acknowledged understanding. A written informed consent was obtained. The patient was brought into the ultrasound suite for biopsy. Multiple sonographic images of the right breast irregular hypoechoic mass at 10:00 10 cm from the nipple were obtained. A time out procedure was performed to verify the patient's identity and location of the biopsy. The skin was antiseptically cleansed and draped. Local anesthesia was achieved to the skin puncture site using a 1% lidocaine solution and a 1% lidocaine solution with epinephrine deeper surrounding the biopsy site. A skin nick was made with an 11 blade. Under real-time sonographic guidance, multiple core biopsies were obtained using a Bard, 14-gauge, Marquee. The needle was seen to pass through the lesion during the procedure. After assuring adequate sampling, a biopsy marker clip in the shape of a tophat was placed. Hemostasis was achieved with manual compression. Sterile dressing was applied after compression was held. No complications occurred. All cores were placed in formalin and submitted to pathology for histologic analysis. Right POST-PROCEDURE MAMMOGRAM FOR MARKER PLACEMENT: BREAST COMPOSITION: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses (Category C). A post-procedure two-view mammogram shows biopsy marker clip is posterior to the previously reported right breast mammographic asymmetry by approximately 2 cm. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient was given verbal and written postprocedure instructions. The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] experienced no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] amirisWebForms/PatientPatientInformation.aspx?cp=RGs*p=930411541 8/33 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:52 AM 2/4 [REDACTED] 8:52 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services pg 9 of 34 10/6/25, 2:25 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS IMPRESSION: 1. Technically successful ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy of right breast mass at 10:00 approximately 10 cm from the nipple (tophat clip). Post procedure mammogram demonstrates the biopsy clip posterior to the questioned mammographic asymmetry. Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] had with the patient that right breast ultrasound guided biopsy correctly targeted ultrasound findings from prior diagnostic ultrasound 8/4/2025, however, right breast asymmetry may be distinct from right breast ultrasound findings and therefore scheduled right breast MRI on [REDACTED] is still recommended as this mammographic asymmetry may represent a separate finding from ultrasound finding. Decision to perform stereotactic/tomographic versus MRI guided biopsy will be dependent upon both MRI and pathologic results. 2. Right post-procedure mammogram for marker placement. Awaiting pathology report. An addendum to this report will be made with final pathology results. **************************************************************************************************** In accordance with New Jersey law, the following statement must be included</data>
      <data key="d14" />
    </node>
    <node id="LK_SW_INV_0004_a6cc91">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
      <data key="d11">LK_SW_INV_0004_a6cc91</data>
      <data key="d2">LK_SW_INV</data>
      <data key="d3">LK_SW_INV</data>
      <data key="d12">10</data>
      <data key="d13">patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] experienced no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] amirisWebForms/PatientPatientInformation.aspx?cp=RGs*p=930411541 8/33 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:52 AM 2/4 [REDACTED] 8:52 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) O [REDACTED] 9:46 AM Fax Services pg 9 of 34 10/6/25, 2:25 PM Atlantic Medical Imaging - Synapse EIS IMPRESSION: 1. Technically successful ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy of right breast mass at 10:00 approximately 10 cm from the nipple (tophat clip). Post procedure mammogram demonstrates the biopsy clip posterior to the questioned mammographic asymmetry. Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] had with the patient that right breast ultrasound guided biopsy correctly targeted ultrasound findings from prior diagnostic ultrasound 8/4/2025, however, right breast asymmetry may be distinct from right breast ultrasound findings and therefore scheduled right breast MRI on [REDACTED] is still recommended as this mammographic asymmetry may represent a separate finding from ultrasound finding. Decision to perform stereotactic/tomographic versus MRI guided biopsy will be dependent upon both MRI and pathologic results. 2. Right post-procedure mammogram for marker placement. Awaiting pathology report. An addendum to this report will be made with final pathology results. **************************************************************************************************** In accordance with New Jersey law, the following statement must be included in all mammography reports, regardless of an individual's breast tissue density. "Your mammogram may show that you have dense breast tissue as determined by the Breast Imaging Reporting and Data System established by the American College of Radiology. Dense breast tissue is very common and is not abnormal. However, in some cases, dense breast tissue can make it harder to find cancer on a mammogram and may also be associated with a risk factor for breast cancer. Discuss this and other risks for breast cancer that pertain to your personal medical history with your health care provider. A report of your results was sent to your health care provider. [REDACTED] at the website of the American College of Radiology, www.acr.org." If you are the referring physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] (609)650-0004 to reach a radiologist. Date Of Signature [REDACTED] 4:35 PM Report Electronically Signed by: Vesels, M.D., Clinton Report Electronically Signed on: [REDACTED] 04:35 PM Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] BX w/Clip [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] amirisWebForms/PatientPatientInformation [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Document Information Other: Outside Pathology PATH ADDENDUM 3/4 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:52 AM [REDACTED] 8:52 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE PATHOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Priscilla P. Hazel | Msk Pas Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:52 AM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: path.pdf] [REDACTED] 9:12 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Media Information Sonic Healthcare [REDACTED] 9:03:20 AM PAGE 3/004 Fax Server Wirth, Susan DOB: [REDACTED] #: [REDACTED] Gender: F Age: 63 Atlantic Medical Imaging - Somers Point [REDACTED] Social [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Patient [REDACTED] Somers Point, NJ [REDACTED] Date of Collection: [REDACTED] (609) 653-0209 Date Received: [REDACTED] Clinical Information: 63 year old Female with enhancing 7 mm mass also seen to enhance on MRI Right Breast, upper outer quadrant, posterior depth; stop light clip marker; Mammotome; Stereotactic ADDENDUM Breast Pathology Report RESULTS Right Left 1: Diagnosis Right Breast, upper outer quadrant, posterior depth: Moderately differentiated invasive ductal carcinoma (tubule formation 3/3, nuclear pleomorphism 2/3, mitotic count 1/3), measuring 0.6 cm in maximal length in this material. PHOTOMICROGRAPH Gross Description: Received in formalin labeled with the patient's name [REDACTED] are multiple light tan to yellow tan soft tissue fragments measuring 2.5 x 2.5 x 0.3 cm in aggregate. The entire specimen is submitted in 3 cassette(s) labeled "1A-1C". Ischemic time: 0 hrs: 25 min; fixation time: 19 hrs: 5 min. yellow/po Specimen 1: Right Breast, upper outer quadrant, posterior depth Comments Prognostic/predictive marker studies are being performed, the results will follow in an addendum. Following CAP/ASCO guidelines HER2 FISH will be performed on all invasive breast carcinomas if HER2 IHC is 2+ (EQUIVOCAL). Case reviewed in departmental conference. Specimens processed and interpreted at CBLPath, Inc., 760 Westchester Ave, Wirth, Susan Page 1 of 2 Rye Brook, NY [REDACTED] Phone (877) 225-7284. Dr. Crit-Christian Rizk, Accession #: [REDACTED] Laboratory Director, NY PP# 3954; CLIA# [REDACTED] CAP LAP# 7184143. A copy of this report has been sent to the referring physician [REDACTED] been supplied by the requesting physician's office. 1/3 Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 9:12 AM [REDACTED] 9:12 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Sonic Healthcare [REDACTED] 9:03:20 AM PAGE 4/004 Fax Server Wirth, Susan DOB: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] #: [REDACTED] Addendum [REDACTED] 10:00:52 AM Studies for calponin and p63 underscore the absence of myoepithelial cells (MEC) in the area of invasive cancer. Loss of membranous E-cadherin and B-catenin immunostaining supports the additional finding of atypical lobular hyperplasia (ALH) and lobular carcinoma in situ (LCIS), nuclear grade 2, classic type. Atypical ductal hyperplasia (ADH) is also present. The invasive carcinoma demonstrates: Estrogen receptor (ER): POSITIVE - &gt;90% strong intensity nuclear staining; Progesterone receptor (PgR): POSITIVE - &gt;90% strong intensity nuclear staining; HER-2 neu score: 1+/low (NEGATIVE) (faint/incomplete membranous staining observed in &gt;10% of tumor cells)*; Proliferation index (Ki-67): 15% nuclear staining. *Patients with breast cancers that are HER2 IHC 1+ or IHC 2+/ISH not-amplified may be eligible for a treatment that targets non-amplified/non-overexpressed levels of HER2 expression for cytotoxic drug delivery (IHC 0 results do not result in eligiblity currently). Wolff AC, Somerfield MR, Dowsett M, Hammond MEH, Hayes DF, McShane LM, Saphner TJ, Spears PA, Allison KH. Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2 Testing in Breast Cancer. Arch Pathol Lab Med. 2023 Sep 1;147(9):1326-1000. doi: 10.5858/arpa.2023-0950-SA. PMID: 37303228. ER clone (SP1) ultraview DAB detection; computer assisted quantitative IHC using Leica Aperio AT2 and Leica ImageScope PgR clone (1E2) ultraview DAB detection; computer assisted quantitative IHC using Leica Aperio AT2 and Leica ImageScope Ventana Pathway HER2 neu/4B5 ultraview DAB detection Ki67 clone MIB-1 (Dako); computer assisted</data>
      <data key="d14" />
    </node>
    <node id="LK_SW_INV_0005_c5f907">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
