      <data key="d12">12</data>
      <data key="d13">E-cadherin and B-catenin immunostaining supports the additional finding of atypical lobular hyperplasia (ALH) and lobular carcinoma in situ (LCIS), nuclear grade 2, classic type. Atypical ductal hyperplasia (ADH) is also present. The invasive carcinoma demonstrates: Estrogen receptor (ER): POSITIVE - &gt;90% strong intensity nuclear staining; Progesterone receptor (PgR): POSITIVE - &gt;90% strong intensity nuclear staining; HER-2 neu score: 1+/low (NEGATIVE) (faint/incomplete membranous staining observed in &gt;10% of tumor cells)*; Proliferation index (Ki-67): 15% nuclear staining. *Patients with breast cancers that are HER2 IHC 1+ or IHC 2+/ISH not-amplified may be eligible for a treatment that targets non-amplified/non-overexpressed levels of HER2 expression for cytotoxic drug delivery (IHC 0 results do not result in eligiblity currently). Wolff AC, Somerfield MR, Dowsett M, Hammond MEH, Hayes DF, McShane LM, Saphner TJ, Spears PA, Allison KH. Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2 Testing in Breast Cancer. Arch Pathol Lab Med. 2023 Sep 1;147(9):1326-1000. doi: 10.5858/arpa.2023-0950-SA. PMID: 37303228. ER clone (SP1) ultraview DAB detection; computer assisted quantitative IHC using Leica Aperio AT2 and Leica ImageScope PgR clone (1E2) ultraview DAB detection; computer assisted quantitative IHC using Leica Aperio AT2 and Leica ImageScope Ventana Pathway HER2 neu/4B5 ultraview DAB detection Ki67 clone MIB-1 (Dako); computer assisted quantitative IHC using Leica Aperio AT2 and Leica ImageScope Image analysis is dependent on the handling and processing of the tissue, quality of staining, density of tumor cells, the presence of stromal infiltrate, and staining artifacts. The clinical interpretation of any positive staining, or its absence, must be evaluated within the context of clinical history, morphology, and other histopathological criteria. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Addendum Sign-Out [REDACTED] Addendum Issued By: Claudine Habib M.D. Electronically signed out by: Dr. Claudine Habib (877) 259-9310 Report Date: [REDACTED] [REDACTED text about laboratory performance and disclaimers] Specimens processed and interpreted at CBLPath, Inc., 760 Westchester Ave, Wirth, Susan Page 2 of 2 Rye Brook, NY [REDACTED] (877) 225-7284. Dr. Crit-Christian Rizk, Accession #: [REDACTED] Laboratory Director, NY PP# 3954; CLIA# [REDACTED] CAP LAP# 7184143. A copy of this report has been sent to the referring physician [REDACTED] by the requesting physician's office. Document Information Other: Outside Pathology ADDENDUM BREAST PATH Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 9:12 AM 2/3 [REDACTED] 9:12 AM Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE PATHOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Priscilla P. Hazel | Msk Pas Wirth, Susan A (MR # 39100822) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 9:12 AM 3/3</data>
