      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: MMG.pdf] Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) 8:50 AM Media Information Page 1/2 Date: 11/12/2025 5:55:46 PM From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] [LOGO: MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY] Tel (718) 428-1500 • Fax (718) 428-2475 www.mainstreetradiology.com Bayside 32nd Ave 32-29 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11358 Bayside 41st Ave 44-01 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11361 Downtown Flushing 136-25 37th Ave, Flushing, NY 11354 Western Queens 72-06 Northern Blvd, Jackson Hts, NY 11372 Glendale 83-14 Cooper Ave, Glendale, NY 11385 : WONG LAP KOON, MD [REDACTED] SANFORD AVE, SUITE 2A FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Referrer Phone: [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] Phone: [REDACTED] Gender: F e-male DOB: [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] Exam Date: 9/23/2025 12:37 PM Acc #: 10118795 Secondary ID: [REDACTED] Exam Name: [REDACTED] Indication: Patient [REDACTED] screening. The patient has no [REDACTED] of breast cancer. The patient [REDACTED] Date of last clinical exam: Longer than one year ago Breast Cancer Risk: NCI 5 year: 0.5% NCI Lifetime: 2.7% Comparison: Multiple prior mammograms dating back to [REDACTED] Technique: 3D digital CC and MLO views of both breasts were obtained with reconstructed views. Deep learning algorithms (AI) were applied to mammography and DBT images as a concurrent reading aid. Findings: The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. There is a 0.6 cm spiculated mass at the 9:00 position of the left breast at a mid to posterior depth. Bilateral scattered coarse benign-appearing calcifications are unchanged. No significant calcifications or areas of architectural distortion are identified. Nonenlarged bilateral axillary lymph nodes are seen. Impression: 0.6 cm spiculated mass at the 9:00 position of the left breast. Further evaluation is required. No [REDACTED] BI-RADS CATEGORY: 0 - Incomplete - Need Additional Imaging Evaluation This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com 1/3 Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:50 AM 8:50 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page 2/2 Date: 11/12/2025 5:55:46 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Recommendation: Left 3D diagnostic mammogram and targeted left breast ultrasound. The patient [REDACTED] A letter will be sent to the patient [REDACTED] Approximately 10% of breast carcinomas are not radiographically detectable. A negative report should not delay biopsy if a clinically suspicious mass is present. Dense breasts may obscure an underlying neoplasm. Patient [REDACTED] a target due date for their next mammogram. BIRADS 1: Negative BIRADS 2: Benign BIRADS 3: Probably Benign BIRADS 4: Suspicious Abnormality - Biopsy should be considered. BIRADS 5: Highly Suspicious of Malignancy BIRADS 6: Known Malignancy BIRADS 0: Incomplete - Need Additional Imaging Evaluation and/or Prior Mammograms for Comparison The New York State Department of Health requires us to indicate the date of the patient's last clinical breast examination. Electronically signed by: Heather Frimmer MD [REDACTED] 8:44 AM Workstation: OUTREAD7 Report Electronically Signed by: Heather Frimmer MD Report Electronically Signed on: 9/24/2025 08:44 AM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Other: Outside Correspondence mammogram Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:50 AM 2/3 [REDACTED] 8:50 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: Karen Shih Source Information Kayshla Maldonado | Baic Bre Srg Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:50 AM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: US bx.pdf] 8:51 AM Media Information Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page 1/2 Date: 11/12/2025 5:53:51 PM MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY Tel (718) 428-1500 • Fax (718) 428-2475 www.mainstreetradiology.com Bayside-Hts Hills Bayside Hts Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11364 Bayside-44th Ave [REDACTED] 44-21 Francis Lewis Blvd [REDACTED], NY 11361 Downtown-Flushing 156-23 37th Ave, Flushing, NY 11354 Western Queens [REDACTED] Northern Blvd, Jackson Hts, NY 11372 Glendale 82-14 Cooper Ave, Glendale, NY 11385 : WONG LAP KOON, MD [REDACTED] SANFORD AVE, SUITE 2A FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Referrer Phone: [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] Phone: [REDACTED] Gender: Female DOB: [REDACTED] Acc #: 10207022 Patient [REDACTED] Secondary ID: [REDACTED] Exam Date: 10/29/2025 10:15 AM Exam Name: [REDACTED] EXAMS: US BREAST BIOPSY, MA 3D DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAPHY (LEFT BREAST) HISTORY: 71 years old female with left 10:00, 2 cm from nipple, ill-defined sonographic mass, which corresponds to a left upper central mammographic mass on recent diagnostic evaluation. The patient presents for ultrasound guided core biopsy. PROCEDURE: Ultrasound guided core biopsy of the left breast. Pertinent imaging studies and/or documents were reviewed prior to the procedure. The patient identification and procedure were verified. The patient's known allergies, current medications and adverse medication reactions were reviewed prior to the procedure. The procedure was explained, bleeding, were reviewed. Patient's questions were answered and written [REDACTED] infection and bleeding, were reviewed. Patient's questions were answered and written informed consent was obtained. A safety pause was performed immediately prior to the procedure. PRE PROCEDURE IMAGING: Re-demonstrates the lesion described above. The patient [REDACTED] was prepped for the procedure using standard aseptic technique. Local anesthesia was achieved with injection of 7 cc of 1% lidocaine in the skin/superficial tissues and the deeper tissues. The mass was biopsied using a lateral approach; ultrasound guidance and a 14 gauge spring loaded core biopsy needle device. 8 tissue samples were obtained. Adequate lesion sampling was confirmed by orthogonal ultrasound images. The tissue specimens were placed in formalin and submitted to the pathological [REDACTED] for analysis. A ribbon tissue marker was then deployed at the biopsy site. Digital post biopsy CC and MLO mammographic views were performed. The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Left central inner breast, posterior depth, This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 1/3 [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page 2/2 Date: 11/12/2025 5:53:51 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED]</data>
      <data key="d14" />
    </node>
    <node id="MET_KS_0001_e332a3">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
      <data key="d11">MET_KS_0001_e332a3</data>
      <data key="d2">MET_KS</data>
      <data key="d3">MET_KS</data>
      <data key="d12">5</data>
      <data key="d13">was obtained. A safety pause was performed immediately prior to the procedure. PRE PROCEDURE IMAGING: Re-demonstrates the lesion described above. The patient [REDACTED] was prepped for the procedure using standard aseptic technique. Local anesthesia was achieved with injection of 7 cc of 1% lidocaine in the skin/superficial tissues and the deeper tissues. The mass was biopsied using a lateral approach; ultrasound guidance and a 14 gauge spring loaded core biopsy needle device. 8 tissue samples were obtained. Adequate lesion sampling was confirmed by orthogonal ultrasound images. The tissue specimens were placed in formalin and submitted to the pathological [REDACTED] for analysis. A ribbon tissue marker was then deployed at the biopsy site. Digital post biopsy CC and MLO mammographic views were performed. The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Left central inner breast, posterior depth, This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 1/3 [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page 2/2 Date: 11/12/2025 5:53:51 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] ribbon biopsy marker with post biopsy changes is noted. The ribbon biopsy marker corresponds to the irregular mammographic mass, confirming correlation. Just superior to the ribbon clip there is no mammographic asymmetry on MLO projection, which appears relatively stable compared to prior exams. The patient [REDACTED] of biopsy was held in compression for several minutes and the needle entrance site was closed using Steri strips. Pain control was adequate and the patient was assessed and appropriate for discharge. Home care instructions for this procedure were reviewed with the patient. All patient questions were answered. IMPRESSION: Left ultrasound guided core biopsy of the sonographic mass at 10:00, 2 cm from the nipple complete. Ribbon biopsy marker was placed. Postbiopsy mammogram demonstrates the ribbon clip in the left central inner breast, corresponding to the irregular mammographic mass. Slightly superior, approximately 0.9 cm superiorly, to the ribbon clip on MLO view there is a second mammographic asymmetry, which appears relatively stable compared to prior exams. Given close proximity, this will likely be included in the treatment field. PATHOLOGY RESULTS: Invasive ductal carcinoma. Please refer to pathology report for complete results. Pathology shows malignant findings. The results are concordant with imaging. RECOMMENDATION: 1.Recommendation: Surgical consultation. Surgery consultation/excision and appropriate medical management is recommended for the left 10:00 (ribbon clip) biopsy-proven invasive ductal carcinoma. 2. Pre and postcontrast breast MRI can be considered to evaluate for extent of disease. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 6 - Known Malignancy - Biopsy Proven Attempt was made to contact Dr. WONG LAP KOON MD's office on [REDACTED] 9:28 AM. A copy of this report will be faxed to the doctor's office. A member of our staff will attempt to call the office at a later time. Electronically signed by: Mrugank Shukla MD [REDACTED] 9:34 AM Workstation: MSR2-MAMMOPC2 Report Electronically Signed by: Mrugank Shukla MD Report Electronically Signed on: [REDACTED] 09:34 AM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Other: Outside Correspondence bx report Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 2/3 [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: Karen Shih Source Information Kayshla Maldonado | Baic Bre Srg Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: dx MMG.pdf] [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Media Information Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 1/2 Date: 11/12/2025 5:54:11 PM MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY Tel (718) 428-1500 • Fax (718) 428-2475 www.mainstreetradiology.com Bayside-35rd Ave. Bayside 48th Ave Downtown Flushing Western Queens Chinatown 35-30 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11358 48-01 Francis Lewis Blvd [REDACTED] NY 11361 136-20 39th Ave, Flushing, NY 11354 74-09 Northern Blvd, Jackson Hts, NY 11372 32-44 College Ave, Flushing, NY 11355 - WONG LAP KOON, MD [REDACTED] SANFORD AVE, SUITE 2A FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Acc #: 10167656 Secondary ID: Exam Name: Referrer Phone: Name: Phone: Gender: Female DOB: Patient Exam Date: 10/15/2025 12:13 PM [REDACTED] EXAM: MA 3D DIGITAL DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAPHY (LEFT BREAST), US DIAGNOSTIC BREAST LEFT History: 71 years old female presents for evaluation of left breast mass seen on recent screening mammogram. Patient [REDACTED] Views obtained: LEFT 3-D tomosynthesis MLO/CC spot compression and ML views. Digital mammography was performed with additional image analysis utilizing CAD. Comparison: 9/23/2025, 1/29/2020, [REDACTED] FINDINGS: There are scattered areas of fibroglandular density. Left upper central breast, posterior depth there is a persistent irregular mass measuring 0.7 cm. BILATERAL BREAST ULTRASOUND, performed around the clock. Comparison: 1/29/2020, 6/12/2018. Breast composition: Heterogeneous RIGHT BREAST: No [REDACTED] 6:00, 1 cm from nipple there is a shadowing calcified nodule measuring 0.4 cm, stable. LEFT BREAST: 10:00, 2 cm from nipple there is an ill-defined mass measuring 0.4 x 0.3 x 0.4 cm, likely corresponding to the mammographic mass. No [REDACTED] axillary lymphadenopathy. This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 1/3 [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 2/2 Date: [REDACTED] 5:54:11 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] IMPRESSION: Left 10:00 sonographic 0.4 cm ill-defined mass, likely corresponding to the left upper central breast mammographic persistent irregular mass. Left breast ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy with clip placement and postprocedural mammogram is recommended. RECOMMENDATION: 1. Recommendation: Ultrasound Biopsy. Left breast ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy with clip placement and postprocedural mammogram. 2. If the clip does not correlate with the mammographic mass, stereotactic core needle biopsy would be recommended. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 4 - Suspicious Abnormality. Message left with medical secretary at Dr. WONG LAP KOON MD's office on [REDACTED] 12:20 PM. A copy of this report will be faxed</data>
