      <data key="d12">10</data>
      <data key="d13">nipple there is a shadowing calcified nodule measuring 0.4 cm, stable. LEFT BREAST: 10:00, 2 cm from nipple there is an ill-defined mass measuring 0.4 x 0.3 x 0.4 cm, likely corresponding to the mammographic mass. No [REDACTED] axillary lymphadenopathy. This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 1/3 [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 2/2 Date: [REDACTED] 5:54:11 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] IMPRESSION: Left 10:00 sonographic 0.4 cm ill-defined mass, likely corresponding to the left upper central breast mammographic persistent irregular mass. Left breast ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy with clip placement and postprocedural mammogram is recommended. RECOMMENDATION: 1. Recommendation: Ultrasound Biopsy. Left breast ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy with clip placement and postprocedural mammogram. 2. If the clip does not correlate with the mammographic mass, stereotactic core needle biopsy would be recommended. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 4 - Suspicious Abnormality. Message left with medical secretary at Dr. WONG LAP KOON MD's office on [REDACTED] 12:20 PM. A copy of this report will be faxed to the doctor's office. A letter has been sent to the patient [REDACTED] Approximately 10% of breast carcinomas are not radiographically detectable. A negative report should not delay biopsy if a clinically suspicious mass is present. Dense breasts may obscure an underlying neoplasm. BIRADS 0: Incomplete - Need Additional Imaging Evaluation and/or Prior Mammograms for Comparison BIRADS 1: Negative BIRADS 2: Benign BIRADS 3: Probably Benign BIRADS 4: Suspicious Abnormality - Biopsy should be considered. BIRADS 5: Highly Suspicious of Malignancy BIRADS 6: Known Malignancy The New York State Department of Health requires us to indicate the date of the patient's last clinical breast examination. Electronically signed by: Mrugank Shukla MD [REDACTED] 12:21 PM Workstation: OUTREAD11 Report Electronically Signed by: Mrugank Shukla MD Report Electronically Signed on: [REDACTED] 12:21 PM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Other: Outside Correspondence mmg and US Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 2/3 [REDACTED] 8:51 AM Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: Karen Shih Source Information Kayshla Maldonado | Baic Bre Srg Shih, Li (MR # 39111396) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:51 AM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: path.pdf] From ■■■■■■■ Page: 5/7 Date: ■■■■■■ 12:11:52 PM NewYork-Presbyterian Queens NewYork-Presbyterian Diagnostic Laboratories 56-45 Main Street Flushing, NY ■■■■ William H. Rodgers, PHD, MD Director of Clinical Laboratory Tel: ■■■■■■■■ Fax: 718-661-7745 Specimen Date: ■■■■■■■ In Lab Date: ■■■■■■■ Report Date: ■■■■■■■ Patient: ■■■ ■■ 59-35 175TH PLACE FRESH MEADOWS, NY ■■■■ Surgical Pathology Report with Addendum ■■■■■■■■■■ ■■■■■■■■■ ■■ ■■■■■■■ ■■ ■■■ 44-01 Francis Lewis Blvd. Bayside, NY ■■■■ NYP ■■■■ ■■■■■■■■ Encounter #: 324109209 DOB-Age-Sex: ■■■■■■■■ - 71 -F Location: NYPQ LAB OUTREACH Copy To: Wong Lap Koon, MD CLINICAL INFORMATION: Left breast 10:00 2cmfa, r/o cancer DIAGNOSIS: 1. Breast, left, 10:00 2 cm/n, core biopsy: Invasive ductal carcinoma, with calcifications. The invasive carcinoma is moderately differentiated, and spans 0.7 cm in greatest dimension. The results of ER, PR, HER2, and Ki-67 testing will follow. Note: An E-cadherin immunostain was used in the workup of this specimen. GROSS DESCRIPTION: 1. Received in formalin, the specimen is labeled "Left breast 10:00 2cm/n" and consists of five cores of yellow-white tissue ranging from 0.8 cm to 2.1 cm. The specimen was collected and placed in formalin at 10:00 a.m. on ■■■■■■■■ and placed into the tissue processor at 10:00 p.m. on ■■■■■■■■ ES 2C. ***Electronically Signed*** Esther Cheng, D.O. The attending pathologist ■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■ the diagnostic slides, and has edited the gross and microscopic portions of the report in rendering the final diagnosis. Addendum - Queens Date Ordered: ■■■■■■■■ Date Reported: ■■■■■■■■ Addendum Diagnosis SHIH, LI J. OP Marker Printed: 11/■■■■■■ 12:00 Page 1 of 2 This fax was received by GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com From ■■■■■■■■ Page: 6/7 Date: ■■■■■■■ 12:11:52 PM SHIH, LI J. Surgical Pathology Report ■■■■■■■■■■ Specimen: Left breast (invasive ca) Block: 1A RESULTS OF ANCILLARY IMMUNOPATHOLOGY STUDIES PERCENTAGE OF POSITIVE CELLS STAINING INTENSITY ESTROGEN RECEPTOR: ~70% STRONG PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR: 10-15% STRONG PROLIFERATION INDEX (Ki-67): 30% HER2: 1+ INTERPRETATION: Since ≥1% of tumor cell nuclei express estrogen receptors, this tumor is considered to be ESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE. Since &lt;1% of tumor cell nuclei express progesterone receptors, this tumor is considered to be PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE. HER2: Incomplete membrane staining that is faint/barely perceptible and within &gt;10% of invasive tumor cells. Thus, this result indicates NEGATIVE HER2 by immunohistochemistry. ER, PgR, HER2 and Ki-67 immunohistochemistry was performed on tissue fixed with neutral buffered formalin for at least 6 hours, up to a maximum of 72 hours using the Ventana 3D2 antibody clone for ER, the Ventana1E2 antibody clone for PgR, the Ventana 4B5 antibody clone for HER2neu and the Ventana 30-9 antibody clone for Ki-67. Cold ischemic times meet requirements specified in relevant version of the ASCO/CAP guidelines. Antibody performance was initially validated by NYPQ and is periodically verified. Interpretation of these antibodies is based on current CAP/ASCO scoring criteria. Esther Cheng, D.O. Billing Codes: 1, 88342_Q, 88360_Q, 88360_Q, 88360_Q, 88360_Q, 88305_Q (Epic Private Ambulatory) All controls for immunohistochemistry, histochemistry, histology, and cytology show appropriate reactivity. These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by NYPQ. Modified procedures such as decalcification, alcohol fixation, air dried smears, and frozen sections are subject to variation from the standard formalin fixed paraffin embedded specimens. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary. These tests are used for clinical purposes. They should not be regarded as investigational or research. Page 2 of 2 SHIH, LI J. Printed: ■■■■■■■ 12:00 OP Marker END OF REPORT This fax was received</data>
