      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: L MMG.pdf] 8:03 AM Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] OCHIN OCHIN Outside Information Results MAMMO LEFT W/ TOMO (Order [REDACTED]) ⓘ Information displayed in this report may not trend or trigger automated decision support. MAMMO LEFT W/ TOMO Order: [REDACTED] Narrative Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] ID: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Note: All result statuses are Final unless otherwise noted. Tests: (1) MAMMO LEFT W/ TOMO (77065TL) MAMMOGRAM Result Below... 20250914000000 RESULT: BI-RADs 5 - Highly suggestive of Malignancy PROCEDURE: LEFT MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS COMPARISON: MG, MAMMO BILATERAL SC W/ TOMO, [REDACTED] MG, MAMMO BILATERAL SC W/ TOMO, [REDACTED] INDICATIONS: New group of microcalcifications in the posterior upper-outer quadrant the left breast. LAST CLINICAL BREAST EXAM: [REDACTED] TECHNIQUE: Left 90 degree lateral and XCC views and left 90 degree lateral and CC magnification spot views. BREAST COMPOSITION: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. FINDINGS: There is a band of innumerable soft tissue densities over a distance of at least 4 cm, and extending 4 cm superior and 7 cm lateral to the nipple line. The calcifications are pleomorphic and highly suspicious. Several additional slightly separated calcifications are noted more medially and inferiorly. CONCLUSION: Highly suspicious band of calcifications in the upper-outer quadrant of the left breast, with several additional slightly separated suspicious calcifications more inferomedially. Biopsy is recommended. RECOMMENDATIONS: BI-RADS#5 - Highly Suggestive of Malignancy - Appropriate Action Should be Taken: Breast biopsy: LEFT BREAST Dense breasts may obscure an underlying neoplasm. As required by New York state law, the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] informed of her dense breasts for the mammogram in writing. Findings faxed to the referring physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Dictated and Approved by: Robert Lautin, M.D. on [REDACTED] Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:03 AM 1/2 8:03 AM Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] Note: An exclamation mark (!) indicates a result that was not dispersed into the flowsheet. Document Creation Date: [REDACTED] 4:46 PM (1) Order result status: Final Collection or observation date-time: [REDACTED] 15:29 Requested date-time: Receipt date-time: Reported date-time: [REDACTED] 16:29:20 Referring Physician: Ordering Physician: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Specimen Source: Source: CPAI Filler Order Number: [REDACTED] Lab site: CP Advanced Imaging Exam End: — Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:29 Received From: OCHIN Result Received: [REDACTED] 15:37 Received Information Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:03 AM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: MMG.pdf] [REDACTED] 8:02 AM Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [OCHIN] OCHIN Outside Information Results HISTORIC MAMMOGRAM (Order [REDACTED]) ⓘ Information displayed in this report may not trend or trigger automated decision support. HISTORIC MAMMOGRAM Order: [REDACTED] Narrative Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] ID: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Note: All result statuses are Final unless otherwise noted. Tests: (1) MAMMO BILATERAL SC W/ TOMO (77067T) MAMMOGRAM Result Below... 20250824000000 RESULT: BI-RADs 0 - Incomplete PROCEDURE: BILATERAL DIGITAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS COMPARISON: US, BREAST ULTRASOUND (LEFT), [REDACTED] MG, MAMMO BILATERAL SC W/ TOMO, [REDACTED] MG, MAMMO BILATERAL SC W/ TOMO, [REDACTED] INDICATIONS: Screening. Family history of breast cancer in maternal cousin. LAST CLINICAL BREAST EXAM: [REDACTED] TECHNIQUE: Digital CC and MLO views of both breasts with tomosynthesis are submitted for review. The study is interpreted with the use and aid of computer assisted diagnosis (CAD). BREAST COMPOSITION: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. FINDINGS: There is a new group of microcalcifications in the posterior upper-outer quadrant of the left breast spanning approximately 2.5 cm (3.5 cm superior to the nipple line, 6.5 cm lateral to the nipple line). A 1 cm nodule in the lower inner quadrant of the left breast is stable. The overlying skin and axillary tissue are within normal limits. CONCLUSION: 1. New group of microcalcifications in the posterior upper-outer quadrant the left breast. Recommend magnification ML and exaggerated lateral CC views for further evaluation. 2. Stable left breast nodule, previously characterized as a fibroadenoma. Dense breasts may obscure an underlying neoplasm. As required by New York state law, the patient [REDACTED] informed of her dense breasts for the mammogram in writing. RECOMMENDATIONS: BI-RADS#0 - Need Additional Imaging Evaluation: Additional mammographic views required: LEFT BREAST Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:02 AM 1/2 [REDACTED] 8:02 AM Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Dictated and Approved by: Heather Osborne, M.D. on [REDACTED] Note: An exclamation mark (!) indicates a result that was not dispersed into the flowsheet. Document Creation Date: [REDACTED] 5:01 PM (1) Order result status: Final Collection or observation date-time: [REDACTED] 15:44 Requested date-time: Receipt date-time: Reported date-time: [REDACTED] 16:56:24 Referring Physician: Ordering Physician: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Specimen Source: Source: CPAI Filler Order Number: [REDACTED] Lab site: CP Advanced Imaging Exam End: — Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:44 Received From: OCHIN ↻ Result Received: [REDACTED] 15:37 ↻ Received Information Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:02 AM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: MSK review.pdf] 8:04 AM Marino, Marlene [REDACTED] FOREIGN MR BREAST Status: Final result