      <data key="d13">Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Attached To: Marlene Marino Source Information OCHIN Last update on [REDACTED] 3:47 PM Wang, Minghuang Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:05 AM 6/6 [DOCUMENT: stc bx.pdf] [REDACTED] 8:05 AM Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Media Information [REDACTED] 12:29 PM (212) 772-0468 ➤ LHR COBBLE HILL pg 1 of 3 [LOGO: LHR LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY] [REDACTED] [LOGO: ACR] Queens Bronx Long Island Exam requested by: SITE PERFORMED: LHR COBBLE HILL MINGKE WANG MD SITE PHONE: (718) 282-7000 139 CENTRE ST, STE PH102 NEW YORK NY [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Phone: (917) 674-5280 Date of Exam: [REDACTED] Addendum 1 - [REDACTED] BREAST SURGICAL PATHOLOGY ADDENDUM: Left breast 1 o'clock axis calcifications, core biopsy: -Ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate to high nuclear grade, solid increased perforated patterns with necrosis and calcifications -Lymph node, negative for metastatic carcinoma. Left breast 2 o'clock axis calcifications, core biopsy: -Ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate to high nuclear grade, solid increased perforated patterns with necrosis and calcifications. - skeletal muscle. Pathology results indicate that the specimen is malignant. The pathology results are concordant with the imaging. Contrast-enhanced breast MRI is recommended to evaluate the extent of disease. Breast surgery consultation is recommended for further management. The critical results pathway was initiated on [REDACTED] 3:17 PM to facilitate the communication of these results and recommendations to the referring provider. Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. CAROLYN M HANNA MD - Electronically Signed: [REDACTED] 3:17 PM Physician [REDACTED] Original Report EXAM: STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY 2 SITES WITH VACUUM ASSISTANCE Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - www.lenoxhillradiology.com Printed: [REDACTED] 12:29 PM MARINO, MARLENE (Exam: [REDACTED] 11:00 AM) Page 1 of 3 Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:05 AM 1/4 [REDACTED] 8:05 AM Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) [REDACTED] 12:29 PM (212) 772-0468 ➤ LHR COBBLE HILL pg 2 of 3 [LOGO: LHR LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY] [REDACTED] [LOGO: ACR] Queens Bronx Long Island Continued: Page 2 of 3 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] HISTORY: The patient is 55 years old and was referred for stereotactic biopsies of calcifications at the left 1 o'clock axis and calcifications at the left 2 o'clock axis. COMPARISON: Prior breast imaging studies dated 9/14/2025 PROCEDURE: The procedure was explained to the patient. [REDACTED] All the not limited to infection and bleeding, were reviewed. All questions were answered, and the patient [REDACTED] procedure, signing the consent form. Universal timeout was performed. SITE 1: A scout film and subsequent prefire tomosynthesis imaging shows the suspicious calcifications within the operating window. Using sterile technique, 10 mL of 1% lidocaine and 10 mL of 1% lidocaine with epinephrine was administered. An introducer needle was placed prior to insertion of the biopsy needle. Biopsy was performed using a 9-gauge EVIVA vacuum-assisted breast biopsy standard needle utilizing a lateral-medial approach. Confirmatory pre-and post-fire images demonstrate adequate placement of the biopsy needle. The usual number [REDACTED] specimen radiograph confirms the presence of calcifications. A hourglass shaped Eviva biopsy clip was deployed at the biopsy site. Residual calcifications were present post core biopsy. SITE 2: A scout film and subsequent prefire tomosynthesis imaging shows the suspicious calcifications within the operating window. Using sterile technique, 10 mL of 1% lidocaine and 10 mL of 1% lidocaine with epinephrine was administered. An introducer needle was placed prior to insertion of the biopsy needle. Biopsy was performed using a 9-gauge EVIVA vacuum-assisted breast biopsy standard needle utilizing a lateral-medial approach. Confirmatory pre-and post-fire images demonstrate adequate placement of the biopsy needle. The usual number [REDACTED] specimen radiograph confirms the presence of calcifications. A top hat shaped Eviva biopsy clip was deployed at the biopsy site. Residual calcifications were present post core biopsy. A postprocedure mammogram demonstrates appropriate placement of the clips. The patient [REDACTED]. The specimens were subsequently sent to the pathology lab. IMPRESSION: 2 site stereotactic biopsies performed. Pathology results and concordance will follow as an addendum to this report. Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - www.lenoxhillradiology.com Printed: [REDACTED] 12:29 PM MARINO, MARLENE (Exam: [REDACTED] 11:00 AM) Page 2 of 3 Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:05 AM 2/4 [REDACTED] 8:05 AM Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) [REDACTED] 12:29 PM (212) 772-0468 ➤ LHR COBBLE HILL pg 3 of 3 [LOGO: LHR LENOX HILL RADIOLOGY] [REDACTED] [LOGO: ACR] Queens Bronx Long Island Continued: Page 3 of 3 Patient: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this patient. CAROLYN M HANNA MD - Electronically Signed: [REDACTED] 1:55 PM Physician [REDACTED] Confidential Tel: [REDACTED] - Fax: [REDACTED] - www.lenoxhillradiology.com Printed: [REDACTED] 12:29 PM MARINO, MARLENE (Exam: [REDACTED] 11:00 AM) Page 3 of 3 Document Information Other: Outside Procedure STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 8:05 AM 3/4 [REDACTED] 8:05 AM Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE PROCEDURE ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Jaslee Quinones | Msk Pas Marino, Marlene (MR # 39103258) Printed by Tracy-Ann Syreeta Moo, MD [REDACTED] 