      <data key="d12">1</data>
      <data key="d13">[DOCUMENT: MMG.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:51 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital Outside Information Results ℹ US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT (Order [REDACTED]) ℹ US BREAST DIAGNOSTIC BILAT Order: [REDACTED] Impression Indeterminate ultrasound finding in the upper right breast area of palpable concern for which representative ultrasound-guided biopsy is recommended. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] RECOMMENDATION: Ultrasound Biopsy Side: Right Follow-Up: Prompt follow up The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] BI-RADS mammogram: 2: Benign BI-RADS sonogram: 4: Suspicious Breast Cancer Risk Assessment The American College of Radiology recommends that all women undergo breast cancer risk assessment by age 25 so that those at higher-than-average risk can be identified and appropriate screening initiated. Black, Asian, Hispanic and Ashkenazi Jewish women are at higher risk in general. One widely used risk assessment tool is the Tyrer-Cuzick model at ibis.ikonopedia.com. The American Cancer Society, American College of Radiology and Society of Breast Imaging recommend screening breast MRI for women with 20% or greater lifetime risk of breast cancer. Electronically Signed By: Mark Francescone on October 09, 2025 05:22 PM I, , have personally reviewed this report and concur with its findings and conclusions, as affirmed by my electronic signature. Narrative EXAMINATION: BILATERAL DIAGNOSTIC DIGITAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS AND COMPUTER-AIDED DETECTION and BILATERAL BREAST SONOGRAM COMPLETE CLINICAL INFORMATION: 70-year-old female who presents for screening mammogram and also complains of a palpable lump in the right periareolar region. Date of last clinical breast exam: The patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] TECHNIQUE: Mammogram: CC and MLO views including tomosynthesis and 2D synthetic views were obtained. This examination was evaluated with computer-aided detection following primary review. Breast Ultrasound: Doppler and grayscale imaging of both breasts, complete: four quadrants, retroareolar COMPARISON: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] FINDINGS: Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:51 AM 1/2 [REDACTED] 7:51 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] MAMMOGRAM: Density: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. There is no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] A [REDACTED] was placed over the right superior periareolar region in the area of palpable concern. Additional imaging of this area with a spot tangential view demonstrates no [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] BILATERAL BREAST SONOGRAM: Breast composition: Heterogeneous background echotexture. Right breast: The entire breast was imaged. Along 2 o'clock 2 cm from nipple in the area of palpable concern there is a hypoechoic finding that extends over 24 mm. This appears different from the surrounding tissue; ultrasound-guided biopsy is warranted. Small inspissated cysts/fibrocystic changes were demonstrated along 12 o'clock. Left breast: The entire breast was imaged. No [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Small cysts and inspissated cysts were demonstrated, as on prior exams. Exam End: [REDACTED] 16:44 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 00:00 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 17:26 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 10:25 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital 📍View Encounter 📧 Received Information Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:51 AM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: MRI.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital Outside Information Results ⓘ MR BREAST W/WO CON W/CAD BILAT (Order [REDACTED]) ⓘ MR BREAST W/WO CON W/CAD BILAT Order: [REDACTED] Impression Biopsy-proven DCIS, ultrasound underestimates the extent of disease which reaches up to 4.6 centimeters on MRI. The non mass enhancement extends within 0.7 centimeters from the nipple areola complex. RECOMMENDATION: Surgical Consultation Side: Right BI-RADS MRI: 6: Known Malignancy Breast Cancer Risk Assessment The American College of Radiology recommends that all women undergo breast cancer risk assessment by age 25 so that those at higher-than-average risk can be identified and appropriate screening initiated. Black, Asian, Hispanic and Ashkenazi Jewish women are at higher risk in general. One widely used risk assessment tool is the Tyrer-Cuzick model at ibis.ikonopedia.com. The American Cancer Society, American College of Radiology and Society of Breast Imaging recommend screening breast MRI for women with 20% or greater lifetime risk of breast cancer. Electronically Signed By: Roberto Lo Gullo on November 14, 2025 07:52 PM I, Roberto Lo Gullo, have personally reviewed this report and concur with its findings and conclusions, as affirmed by my electronic signature. Narrative EXAMINATION: BILATERAL BREAST MRI WITH AND WITHOUT INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST WITH COMPUTER-AIDED DETECTION CLINICAL INFORMATION: Biopsy-proven DCIS, staging TECHNIQUE: Magnetic resonance imaging of the breasts was performed using multisequence, multiplanar technique with and without intravenous contrast. Subtraction images were also archived. Computer-Aided Detection: CAD analysis facilitated the interpretation of the contrast enhanced (DCE) series. CAD analysis was performed and 3D post-processing images were reconstructed and interpreted on an independent workstation by the radiologist, [REDACTED] Contrast: GADOPICLENOL (ELUCIREM) 0.5 MMOL/ML IV SOLN 6.6 mL COMPARISON: None FINDINGS: BREASTS: Fibroglandular tissue: Heterogeneous fibroglandular tissue with moderate background parenchymal enhancement RIGHT BREAST: In the superior breast there is heterogeneous non mass enhancement measuring 4.6 x 2.7 x 4.3 Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 1/2 [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] centimeters consistent with biopsy-proven DCIS. The suspicious enhancement appears to be 0.7 centimeters distant from the nipple-areolar complex. LEFT BREAST:No suspicious findings OTHER: None. Exam End: [REDACTED] 12:07 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 00:00 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 19:56 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 07:24 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital © ℣ᵨ View Encounter © Received Information Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: MSK review.pdf] 7:55 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] FOREIGN TOMO BREAST BILATERAL Status: Final result PACS Images (Link Unavailable) Show images for FOREIGN TOMO BREAST BILATERAL Study Result Narrative &amp; Impression ACCESSION#(s): A000271015, A000271014 DATE: [REDACTED] 2:16 PM EXAM: REVIEW OF SUBMITTED BREAST IMAGING: BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM WITH TOMOSYNTHESIS [REDACTED] Technique: bilateral mammogram: tomosynthesis images were obtained. BILATERAL COMPLETE BREAST ULTRASOUND [REDACTED] Technique: bilateral breast us: whole breast ultrasound was performed, including sonographic evaluation of all four quadrants and the retroareolar tissues. CLINICAL HISTORY: Palpable right breast DCIS, MSK path review pending. COMPARISON(S): Multiple priors dating from [REDACTED] to [REDACTED] FINDINGS: MAMMOGRAM: BREAST DENSITY: Heterogeneously</data>
      <data key="d14" />
