escone on October 14, 2025 03:37 PM I, Mark Francescone, have personally reviewed this report and concur with its findings and conclusions, as affirmed by my electronic signature. Narrative EXAMINATION: ULTRASOUND-GUIDED RIGHT BREAST CORE BIOPSY and RIGHT DIAGNOSTIC DIGITAL MAMMOGRAM CLINICAL INFORMATION: Ultrasound-guided biopsy of a right breast mass. COMPARISON: [REDACTED] TECHNIQUE: Following universal protocol, patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] out" prior to the procedure. Informed consent was obtained. Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:52 AM 1/2 [REDACTED] 7:52 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] OPERATOR: Dr. Francescone performedthe entire procedure. PREPARATION: Skin was cleansed with Betadine. LOCAL ANESTHETIC: Lidocaine BIOPSY DEVICE: Vacuum-assisted 12-gauge biopsy device TARGET: 2 cm irregular hypoechoic mass-like area along right 2 o'clock 2 cm from nipple NUMBER: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Formalin and hand delivered to Pathology drop-off for analysis. BIOPSY MARKER: Q shape Following the procedure, the wound was cleansed and compressed. Sterile skin closure adhesive strips and sterile gauze were applied and the patient [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] and left the Department in good condition. Right diagnostic Digital Mammogram: Post-biopsy CC and ML full-field digital images were obtained. Density: The breasts are heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. The biopsy marker is in accurately positioned in the expected location. FINDINGS: Breast composition: Heterogeneous background echotexture. Exam End: [REDACTED] 14:21 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 00:00 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:40 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 10:25 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital © ℗ View Encounter © Received Information Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:52 AM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: path.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Physicians, and New Outside Information York Presbyterian Hospital ⓘ Information displayed in this report may not trend or trigger automated decision support. SURGICAL PATHOLOGY Order: [REDACTED] Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 1/5 [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Component 2 mo ago Surgical Pathology (AP) COLUMBIA UNIVERSITY PATHOLOGISTS 630 West 168th Street | New York, New York [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Fax# [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] D.O.B. [REDACTED] Sex: F Physician: [REDACTED] Location: MAN 51W51 300 ULTRAS 51 W 51st Street, #300 Columbia Doctors Midtown Radiology New York, NY [REDACTED] SURGICAL PATHOLOGY OUTREACH **See Addendum/Procedure** SPECIMEN: Breast, right at 2:00 2cm fn, USG core biopsy CLINICAL INFORMATION: Order diagnosis: Encounter for follow-up examination after completed treatment for conditions other than malignant neoplasm. Right breast, 2:00, 2cm FN irregular mass on sono ? granulomatous mastitis, stromal fibrosis r/o ILC/IDC. GROSS DESCRIPTION: The specimen</data>
