      <data key="d13">00:00 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:40 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 10:25 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital © ℗ View Encounter © Received Information Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:52 AM 2/2 [DOCUMENT: path.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Physicians, and New Outside Information York Presbyterian Hospital ⓘ Information displayed in this report may not trend or trigger automated decision support. SURGICAL PATHOLOGY Order: [REDACTED] Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 1/5 [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Component 2 mo ago Surgical Pathology (AP) COLUMBIA UNIVERSITY PATHOLOGISTS 630 West 168th Street | New York, New York [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Fax# [REDACTED] Name: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] D.O.B. [REDACTED] Sex: F Physician: [REDACTED] Location: MAN 51W51 300 ULTRAS 51 W 51st Street, #300 Columbia Doctors Midtown Radiology New York, NY [REDACTED] SURGICAL PATHOLOGY OUTREACH **See Addendum/Procedure** SPECIMEN: Breast, right at 2:00 2cm fn, USG core biopsy CLINICAL INFORMATION: Order diagnosis: Encounter for follow-up examination after completed treatment for conditions other than malignant neoplasm. Right breast, 2:00, 2cm FN irregular mass on sono ? granulomatous mastitis, stromal fibrosis r/o ILC/IDC. GROSS DESCRIPTION: The specimen is received fixed in formalin in a container labeled with the patient's name, [REDACTED] irregular mass on sono ? granulomatous mastitis stromal fibrosis r/o ILD/IDC". It consists of 3 yellow, white, and focally hemorrhagic breast tissue cores ranging from 0.5-2.3 cm in greatest dimension. The specimen is submitted in toto in one cassette labeled A1. Cold ischemic time: Less than 1 minute Time in formalin: 1:35 PM on 10.14.2025 Total time in formalin: 26 hours 25 minute adm [REDACTED] adm DIAGNOSIS(ES): Breast, right at 2:00 2 cm fn, USG core biopsy: Ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS), nuclear grade 3 and 2-3, cribriform pattern, with comedo necrosis and focal calcifications, involving multiple ducts, of female mammary gland, p63 and SMM5-1 highlight primarily the presence of or attenuated presence of myoepithelial cells around the DCIS. The pan-CK immunostain Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 2/5 [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Component 2 mo ago highlight carcinoma and non neoplastic epithelial cells. While definite evidence of invasion is not seen evaluation is hampered/limited by extensive cancerization of lobules by DCIS, myoepithelial cells attenuation and stromal inflammation. Background shows foci of lymphocytic lobulitis. ER and PR immunostains pending. Date Dictated: 10.16.25 vg [REDACTED] This report has been electronically signed and results reported on [REDACTED] 15:20 by Hanina Hibshoosh, MD . Reviewed by: Attending: [REDACTED] The diagnosis was rendered by the attending [REDACTED] Receptor Expression Analysis Date Ordered: [REDACTED] Status: Signed Out INTERPRETATION Test Performed on formalin fixed paraffin embedded section of: Right breast, 2:00, 2 cm FN, core biopsy The results are for in situ carcinoma. Specimen part: A Slide#: A1 Results: ADEQUATE FIXATION: FIXATION: Ischemic time: &lt;1 min ADEQUATE FIXATION: FIXATION: Duration of fixation (adequate 6-72 hours): 26 hours and 25 mm Fixative: 10% neutral buffered formalin STAINING CONTROLS: ER external control positive: Yes STAINING CONTROLS: ER internal control positive NEGATIVE for estrogen receptor expression (suggest repeat testing Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 3/5 [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Component 2 mo ago on excision) No [REDACTED] an immunohistochemical stain utilizing an anti-estrogen receptor antibody (Ventana clone SP1). The specimen was adequate for evaluation for ER as per ASCO/CAP guidelines 2020 (see reference below). (Note: This assay has not been validated on decalcified tissues. If performed on a decalcified specimen, negative results should be interpreted with caution). Reference: Arch Pathol Lab Med. 2010 Jul;134(7):e48-72. American Society of Clinical Oncology/College of American Pathologists guideline recommendations for immunohistochemical testing of estrogen and progesterone receptors in breast cancer (unabridged version). Hammond ME, Hayes DF, et. al. STAINING CONTROLS: PgR external control positive: Yes STAINING CONTROLS: PgR internal control positive NEGATIVE for progesterone receptor expression. No [REDACTED] an immunohistochemical stain utilizing an anti-progesterone receptor antibody (Leica clone 16). The specimen was adequate for evaluation for PR as per ASCO/CAP guidelines 2020 (see reference below). (Note: This assay has not been validated on decalcified tissues. If performed on a decalcified specimen, negative results should be interpreted with caution). Reference: Arch Pathol Lab Med. 2010 Jul;134(7):e48-72. American Society of Clinical Oncology/College of American Pathologists guideline recommendations for immunohistochemical testing of estrogen and progesterone receptors in breast cancer (unabridged version). Hammond ME, Hayes DF, et. al. [REDACTED] This procedure/addenda has been electronically signed and results reported on [REDACTED] 10:2 by Hanina Hibshoosh, MD. Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 4/5 [REDACTED] 7:53 AM Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] Component 2 mo ago Interpreted by: Attending: [REDACTED] Addendum Date Ordered: [REDACTED] Status: Signed Out ADDENDUM This case has been reviewed in Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center (their case # S25-092449) and their diagnosis of the right breast biopsy is that there is 1 focus of microinvasive carcinoma, as well as ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate to high nuclear grade, with cribriform pattern with necrosis and calcifications. Note: please see our original report citing ductal carcinoma in situ. Regarding microinvasion: complete exclusion of microinvasion is not possible but nor is it definitive in our opinion. [REDACTED] This procedure/addenda has been electronically signed and results reported on [REDACTED] 15:2 by Hanina Hibshoosh, MD. Interpreted by: Attending: [REDACTED] Resulting Agency NYP_Columbia Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 13:35 Performed by: NYP HOSPITAL COLUMBIA LAB Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:20 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 07:06 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital ℂ 🔗 View Encounter ℂ Received Information Order Tracking 📋 🧪 📊 Ordered Collected Final Result (Corrected) 10/14 13:35 10/14 13:35 12/11 07:06 Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 5/5 [DOCUMENT: post MMG.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:54 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital Outside Information Results MAMMOGRAPHY FOLLOWING PROCEDURE - RIGHT (Order [REDACTED]) ⓘ Information displayed in this report may not trend or trigger automated decision support. MAMMOGRAPHY FOLLOWING PROCEDURE - RIGHT Order: [REDACTED] Impression BI-RADS sonogram: Post procedure mammograms for marker</data>
