      <data key="d13">biopsy is that there is 1 focus of microinvasive carcinoma, as well as ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate to high nuclear grade, with cribriform pattern with necrosis and calcifications. Note: please see our original report citing ductal carcinoma in situ. Regarding microinvasion: complete exclusion of microinvasion is not possible but nor is it definitive in our opinion. [REDACTED] This procedure/addenda has been electronically signed and results reported on [REDACTED] 15:2 by Hanina Hibshoosh, MD. Interpreted by: Attending: [REDACTED] Resulting Agency NYP_Columbia Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 13:35 Performed by: NYP HOSPITAL COLUMBIA LAB Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 15:20 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 07:06 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital ℂ 🔗 View Encounter ℂ Received Information Order Tracking 📋 🧪 📊 Ordered Collected Final Result (Corrected) 10/14 13:35 10/14 13:35 12/11 07:06 Moncada-Wolhers, MARLENE [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:53 AM 5/5 [DOCUMENT: post MMG.pdf] [REDACTED] 7:54 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital Outside Information Results MAMMOGRAPHY FOLLOWING PROCEDURE - RIGHT (Order [REDACTED]) ⓘ Information displayed in this report may not trend or trigger automated decision support. MAMMOGRAPHY FOLLOWING PROCEDURE - RIGHT Order: [REDACTED] Impression BI-RADS sonogram: Post procedure mammograms for marker placement Ultrasound-guided radar reflector placement in the right breast with mammographic documentation of positioning. Electronically Signed By: Mark Francescone on November 13, 2025 11:28 AM I, Mark Francescone, have personally reviewed this report and concur with its findings and conclusions, as affirmed by my electronic signature. Narrative EXAMINATION: ULTRASOUND-GUIDED RADAR REFLECTOR PLACEMENT IN THE RIGHT BREAST and RIGHT DIAGNOSTIC DIGITAL MAMMOGRAM CLINICAL INFORMATION: Ductal carcinoma in situ COMPARISON: [REDACTED] TECHNIQUE: INFORMED CONSENT: The risks, benefits, and alternatives were explained to the patient [REDACTED] and obtained. Following universal protocol, patient [REDACTED] "[REDACTED] out" prior to the procedure. OPERATORS: Dr. Francescone performed the entire procedure. PREPARATION: Breast was cleansed with Betadine. LOCAL ANESTHETIC: Lidocaine NUMBER [REDACTED] TARGET: 1.6 cm mass at the 2 o'clock axis,2 cm from the nipple. PROCEDURE: A 16-gauge needle containing the radar reflector (SCOUT Radar Localization Device, Merit Medical) was used to localize the target. Ultrasound scanning was utilized to confirm proper depth of the localization needle and the radar reflector was deployed. The patient [REDACTED] in good condition. RIGHT DIAGNOSTIC DIGITAL MAMMOGRAM: CC and ML views were obtained using full-field digital technique following placement of the radar reflector. Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:54 AM 1/2 [REDACTED] 7:54 AM Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] FINDINGS: Density: The breast is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Post-localization mammographic CC and ML views document the radar reflector to be positioned in the expected position. Annotated images were archived. Exam End: [REDACTED] 10:06 Specimen Collected: [REDACTED] 00:00 Last Resulted: [REDACTED] 11:31 Received From: Weill Cornell Medicine, Columbia Result Received: [REDACTED] 13:37 Physicians, and New York Presbyterian Hospital ☾ ☾ View Encounter ☾ Received Information Moncada-Wolhers, Marlene [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 7:54 AM 2/2</data>
