      <data key="d12">10</data>
      <data key="d13">by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:09 PM 2/3 [REDACTED] 10:09 PM Yeh, Wen Mei-Ing (MR # 39094834) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Priscilla P. Hazel | Msk Pas Yeh, Wen Mei-Ing (MR # 39094834) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:09 PM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External6.pdf] 10:10 PM Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) Media Information From: Main Street Radiology To: ALICE Page: 1/3 Date: 9/16/2025 9:15:42 AM MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY Tel (718) 225-1500 • Fax (718) 426-2473 www.mainstreetradiology.com Bayside 32nd Ave 32-52 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11358 Bayside 44th Ave 44-01 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11361 Downtown Flushing 136-24 37th Ave, Flushing, NY 11354 Whitestone Queens 75-06 Northern Blvd, Jackson Hts, NY 11372 Glendale 83-14 Cooper Ave, Glendale, NY 11385 HELEN HSIEH, MD 133-47 SANFORD AVE, SUITE 1B FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Referrer Phone: (718)661-6630 Name: WEN MEI YEH Phone: (347)661-6693 Gender: Female DOB: [REDACTED] Acc #: 10107541 Patient #: [REDACTED] Secondary ID: [REDACTED] Exam Date: 9/6/2025 12:04 PM Exam Name: [REDACTED] ***THIS IS AN ADDENDED REPORT*** Addendum 1 The above findings and recommendations were discussed with Caroline from Dr. Hsieh's office on 9/12/2025 12:46 PM. The patient will be contacted by the referrers office. Electronically signed by: Allison Rubin MD 9/12/2025 1:20 PM Workstation: NYPQARUBIN This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:10 PM 1/4 10:10 PM Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) From: Main Street Radiology To: ALICE Page: 2/3 Date: 9/16/2025 9:15:42 AM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: [REDACTED] ULTRASOUND-GUIDED RIGHT BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY The patient [REDACTED] for biopsy of a suspicious right breast mass as seen on [REDACTED] corresponding to mammographic focal asymmetry. After risks, benefits and alternatives to the procedure were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] informed consent was obtained. Targeted ultrasound of the right breast demonstrates a 0.4 cm irregular hypoechoic mass at 11:00, 8 cm from the nipple. The lesion was targeted under ultrasound biopsy. The skin was cleansed with ChloraPrep. Lidocaine was used for local anesthetic. A 12-gauge spring activated core biopsy needle was used. 3 passes were made through the lesion. A Venus shaped biopsy clip was deployed at the biopsy site. Patient tolerated procedure well with no [REDACTED] complication. Postprocedure digital mammogram demonstrates biopsy clip in expected location, located just posterior to mammographic irregular focal asymmetry on the MLO image. The area mammographic finding in the lateral right breast is obscured on CC imaging by adjacent postbiopsy change. The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Impression: Ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy of a suspicious right breast mass.. Final pathology results: Invasive ductal carcinoma. Pathology shows malignant findings. The results are concordant with imaging. The biopsy marking clip This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:10 PM 2/4 10:10 PM Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) From: Main Street Radiology To: ALICE Page: 3/3 Date: 9/16/2025 9:15:42 AM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: WEN MEI YEH Date of Birth: [REDACTED] in the right upper outer quadrant is located just posterior to the mammographic focal asymmetry. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 6-Known Malignancy, Biopsy Proven Recommendation: Surgical consultation regarding biopsy results. Recommendation: Surgical consultation The above findings and recommendations were relayed to the patient [REDACTED] and discussed with Caroline from Dr. Hsieh's office on [REDACTED] 12:46 PM. [REDACTED] Electronically signed by: Allison Rubin MD [REDACTED] 12:47 PM Workstation: NYPQARUBIN Report Electronically Signed by: Allison Rubin MD Report Electronically Signed on: 9/12/2025 12:47 PM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Misc Administration: Outside Radiology, Breast US BREAST BX Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:10 PM 3/4 10:10 PM Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Priscilla P. Hazel | Msk Pas Yeh, Wen Mei-lng (MR # 39094834) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 10:10 PM 4/4 [DOCUMENT: Path_Biopsy.pdf] [REDACTED] 10:10 PM Yeh, Wen Mei-Ing (MR # 39094834) Media Information [LOGO] NEW YORK NY Cancer &amp; Blood Specialists CANCER &amp; BLOOD 1500 Route 112 SPECIALISTS Port Jefferson Station, NY [REDACTED] Conquering Cancer Together™ CLIA# 33D214I642 NY PFI# 9194 BREAST BIOPSY REPORT Patient: YEH, WEN MEI I Physician: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Age/Sex: 75/F [REDACTED] Main Street Radiology Pathologist [REDACTED] DOB: 02/[REDACTED] Physician [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Phone: (347) 661-6693 Address: 136-25 37th Ave Date Collected: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] Specimen Type: Breast Date Reported: [REDACTED] Clinical Information Clinical History: Right Breast 11:00 8cm FN - 0.6cm Irregular Hypoechoic Mass. Rule Out Cancer. ICD Code(s): C50.911 Percentage Positive Cells Staining Intensity Interpretation Estrogen Receptor (ER) 91-100% Strong Positive Progesterone Receptor (PR) 91-100% Strong Positive Score (0-3+) Interpretation HER2 IHC 1+ Negative Percentage Positive Cells Ki-67 5% ERclone: ER clone ( #F11) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. PRclone: PR clone (16) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Her2clone: HER2 clone ( CB11) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Ki-67 clone (MM1) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Diagnosis &amp; Interpretation: BREAST, RIGHT BREAST 11:00 8CM FN (ULTRASOUND-GUIDED BIOPSY): - INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA - NOTTINGHAM SCORE: 5 OF 9 (ARCHITECTURE = 2 + NUCLEI = 2 + MITOSIS = 1 ). - TUMOR INVOLVES</data>
