      <data key="d13">[REDACTED] Clinical Information Clinical History: Right Breast 11:00 8cm FN - 0.6cm Irregular Hypoechoic Mass. Rule Out Cancer. ICD Code(s): C50.911 Percentage Positive Cells Staining Intensity Interpretation Estrogen Receptor (ER) 91-100% Strong Positive Progesterone Receptor (PR) 91-100% Strong Positive Score (0-3+) Interpretation HER2 IHC 1+ Negative Percentage Positive Cells Ki-67 5% ERclone: ER clone ( #F11) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. PRclone: PR clone (16) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Her2clone: HER2 clone ( CB11) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Ki-67 clone (MM1) BOND Polymer Refine Detection. Negative and positive (internal if applicable) controls show appropriate results. This evaluation is performed according to guidelines issued by CAP/ASCO. Diagnosis &amp; Interpretation: BREAST, RIGHT BREAST 11:00 8CM FN (ULTRASOUND-GUIDED BIOPSY): - INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA - NOTTINGHAM SCORE: 5 OF 9 (ARCHITECTURE = 2 + NUCLEI = 2 + MITOSIS = 1 ). - TUMOR INVOLVES 2 CORES AND MEASURES AT LEAST 5.5 MM Gross Description: BREAST, RIGHT BREAST 11:00 8CM FN (ULTRASOUND-GUIDED BIOPSY): RECEIVED IN FORMALIN WITH PROPER PATIENT 11:00 8CM FN" ARE MULTIPLE CORES OF YELLOW-WHITE SOFT TISSUE RANGING "0.3 TO 2.2" CM IN LENGTH. THE ENTIRE SPECIMEN IS SUBMITTED IN CASSETTE(S) (A1). ISCHEMIC TIME: (1) MIN, FIXATION TIME: (13) HRS. GROSSED BY: GABRIELLE PRATT Technical Component performed by: NY Cancer &amp; Blood Specialists, CLIA# 33D214I642, PFI# 9194, 1500 Route 112, Port Jefferson Station, NY 11776