cm from nipple, a 0.5 cm hypoechoic mass with indistinct borders is noted. 6:00 retroareolar, a 0.5 cm hypoechoic mass is stable and benign. IMPRESSION: A 0.5 cm indeterminate mass is identified at 3:00 4 cm from nipple in the left breast, newly visualized. An ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy with post-procedure diagnostic mammogram is recommended for further evaluation. Recommendation: Ultrasound Biopsy BI-RADS CATEGORY: 4 - Suspicious Abnormality A letter will been sent to the patient ■■■■■ ■■■■■■■■■■■■■ Approximately 10% of breast carcinomas are not radiographically detectable. A negative report should not delay biopsy if a clinically suspicious mass is present. Dense breasts may obscure an underlying neoplasm. Patient ■■■■■■■■■■■■ ■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■ a target due date for their next mammogram. BiRADS 1: Negative BiRADS 2: Benign BiRADS 3: Probably Benign BiRADS 4: Suspicious Abnormality - Biopsy should be considered. BiRADS 5: Highly Suspicious of Malignancy BiRADS 6: Known Malignancy BiRADS 0: Incomplete - Need Additional Imaging Evaluation and/or Prior Mammograms for Comparison The New York State Department of Health requires us to indicate the date of the patient's last clinical breast examination. If NCI risk has been calculated, the results are based on information provided by the patient. Electronically signed by: Ron Benjamin MD ■■■■■■■■ 11:34 AM Workstation: OUTREAD2 Report Electronically Signed by: Ron Benjamin MD Report Electronically Signed on: ■■■■■■■■ 11:34 AM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Misc Administration: Outside Radiology, Breast MAMMO 2/3 Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD ■■■■■■ at ■■■■■■■■ 11:28 PM ■■■■ 11:28 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) ■■■■■■ 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE RADIOLOGY ORDER ■■■■■■■■■ Orders Only on ■■■■■■ with Historical Provider, ■■■ Source Information Rea Kate Toy | Msk Pas Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD ■■■■■■ at ■■■■■■■■ 11:28 PM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Imaging_External3.pdf] [REDACTED] 11:30 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Media Information From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 1/2 Date: 9/5/2025 4:45:41 PM MAIN STREET RADIOLOGY Tel (718) 329-1500 • Fax (718) 439-2575 www.mainstreetradiology.com Bayside 32nd Ave. 35-20 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11358 Bayside 44th Ave. 44-01 Francis Lewis Blvd, Bayside, NY 11361 Downtown Flushing 136-25 37th Ave, Flushing, NY 11354 Western Queens 72-06 Northern Blvd, Jackson Hts, NY 11372 Glendale 84-14 Cooper Ave, Glendale, NY 11385 :: HUI WEN HUANG, NP :: 135-27 38th Ave, 2nd Fl FLUSHING, NY [REDACTED] Referrer Phone: [REDACTED] Name: FENGMEI SUN Chart: [REDACTED] Gender: Female DOB: 3/4/1954 Patient [REDACTED] Acc #: 10064459 Exam Date: 9/3/2025 12:41 PM Secondary ID: Exam Name: [REDACTED] EXAMS: US BREAST BIOPSY, MA POST BIOPSY MAMMO HISTORY: 71 years old female presents with a hypoechoic mass in the left breast. The patient presents for ultrasound guided core biopsy. PROCEDURE: Ultrasound guided core biopsy of the left breast Pertinent imaging studies and/or documents were reviewed prior to the procedure. Patient identification and procedure were verified. After risks, benefits and alternatives to the procedure were discussed with the patient [REDACTED] informed consent was obtained. Time-out was performed. [REDACTED] agreed to the procedure and written informed consent was obtained. Time-out was performed. Targeted ultrasound redemonsirates a 0.6 cm hypoechoic mass in the left breast, 3:00 axis, 4 cm the nipple. The lesion was targeted for ultrasound-guided biopsy. The patient [REDACTED] was prepped and draped using the procedure using standard aseptic technique. Local anesthesia was achieved with injection of 5 cc of 1% lidocaine in the skin/superficial tissues and the deeper tissues. A 14-gauge spring activated biopsy device was advanced to the preselected target through a 13-gauge coaxial guide. Biopsy specimens were obtained with pre- and post-fire images documenting needle placement for each pass. The tissue specimens were submitted to the pathologist [REDACTED] A rod shaped clip marker was then deployed at the biopsy site. The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Post procedure digital mammogram discloses the rod shaped shaped marker at the expected location. The patient [REDACTED] the biopsy was held in compression for several minutes and the needle entrance site was closed using Steri strips. Pain control was adequate and the patient was assessed and appropriate for discharge. Home care instructions for this procedure were reviewed with the</data>
      <data key="d14" />
    </node>
    <node id="TM_FS_DCIS_0002_b83018">
      <data key="d0">EvidenceChunk</data>
      <data key="d11">TM_FS_DCIS_0002_b83018</data>
      <data key="d2">TM_FS_DCIS</data>
      <data key="d3">TM_FS_DCIS</data>
      <data key="d12">10</data>
      <data key="d13">obtained. Time-out was performed. [REDACTED] agreed to the procedure and written informed consent was obtained. Time-out was performed. Targeted ultrasound redemonsirates a 0.6 cm hypoechoic mass in the left breast, 3:00 axis, 4 cm the nipple. The lesion was targeted for ultrasound-guided biopsy. The patient [REDACTED] was prepped and draped using the procedure using standard aseptic technique. Local anesthesia was achieved with injection of 5 cc of 1% lidocaine in the skin/superficial tissues and the deeper tissues. A 14-gauge spring activated biopsy device was advanced to the preselected target through a 13-gauge coaxial guide. Biopsy specimens were obtained with pre- and post-fire images documenting needle placement for each pass. The tissue specimens were submitted to the pathologist [REDACTED] A rod shaped clip marker was then deployed at the biopsy site. The breast tissue is heterogeneously dense, which may obscure small masses. Post procedure digital mammogram discloses the rod shaped shaped marker at the expected location. The patient [REDACTED] the biopsy was held in compression for several minutes and the needle entrance site was closed using Steri strips. Pain control was adequate and the patient was assessed and appropriate for discharge. Home care instructions for this procedure were reviewed with the patient [REDACTED] This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 11:30 PM 1/3 [REDACTED] 11:30 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) From: Main Street Radiology To: [REDACTED] Page: 2/2 Date: 9/5/2025 4:45:41 PM Continued... Main Street Radiology Name: [REDACTED] Date of Birth: 3/4/1954 IMPRESSION: Ultrasound guided core biopsy of hypoechoic mass in the left breast, 3:00 axis. Final pathology results: Ductal carcinoma in situ, DCIS of the papillary and cribriform form type with intermediate grade nuclei. Surrounding breast tissue shows calcifications. Pathology shows malignant findings. The results are concordant with imaging. RECOMMENDATION: Surgical consult/excision is recommended. A bilateral breast MRI with contrast may also be considered to evaluate for extent of disease. Localization of the rod shaped clip can be performed prior to excision. BI-RADS CATEGORY: 6 - Known Malignancy - Biopsy Proven RECOMMENDED FOLLOW UP: Appropriate surgical and oncological evaluation is recommended. These findings were communicated to NP Huang's office on [REDACTED] Electronically signed by: Alicia DeRobertis MD [REDACTED] 1:02 PM Workstation: NYPRDEROB Report Electronically Signed by: Alicia DeRobertis MD Report Electronically Signed on: [REDACTED] 01:02 PM This fax was sent with GFI FaxMaker fax server. For more information, visit: http://www.gfi.com Document Information Other: Outside Procedure US Bx Procedure Report &amp; Post MMG Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 11:30 PM 2/3 [REDACTED] 11:30 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE PROCEDURE ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Rea Kate Toy | Msk Pas Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 11:30 PM 3/3 [DOCUMENT: Path_Biopsy1.pdf] [REDACTED] 11:31 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Media Information [REDACTED] 09:19 (FAX)7184282475 P.001/002 NewYork-Presbyterian Queens Diagnostic Laboratories 56-45 Main Street Flushing, NY [REDACTED] William H. Rodgers, PHD, MD Director of Clinical Laboratory Tel: 718-670-1374 Fax: [REDACTED] Specimen Date: [REDACTED] Surgical Pathology Report with Addendum In Lab Date: [REDACTED] QS25-14681 Report Date: [REDACTED] Patient: [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] 92ND AVE 136-25 37th Ave QUEENS VILLAGE, NY [REDACTED] Flushing, NY [REDACTED] NYP MRN: 1401911569 Telephone: [REDACTED] Encounter #: 316901249 Location: NYPQ LAB OUTREACH DOB/Age-Sex: [REDACTED] - 71-F Copy To: Hui Wen Huang, FNP CLINICAL INFORMATION: Left breast 3:00 4cm/n 0.5cm mass, #9 IDC, DCIS DIAGNOSIS: 1. Breast, left, 3:00 4 cm/n, core biopsy: Ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS). DCIS is of the papillary and cribriform types with intermediate grade nuclei. Surrounding breast tissue shows calcifications. The result of ER testing will follow. Note: SMM and p63 immunostains were used in the workup of this specimen. GROSS DESCRIPTION: 1. Received in formalin, this specimen is labeled "Left breast 3:00 x 3 passes" and consists of four cores of yellow-white tissue admixed with bloody tissue ranging from 0.2 cm to 1.5 cm in length x 0.1 cm in diameter. The specimen was collected and placed in formalin at 12:07 pm on [REDACTED] and placed into the tissue processor at 10:00 pm on 9/5/25. ES 2C. ****Electronically Signed**** Esther Cheng, D.O. The attending [REDACTED] reviewed the diagnostic slides, and has edited the gross and microscopic portions of the report in rendering the final diagnosis. Addendum - Queens Date Ordered: [REDACTED] Date Reported: [REDACTED] Addendum Diagnosis SUN, FENGMEI Printed: 09/06/2025 09:54 Page 1 of 2 QP Marker Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 11:31 PM 1/3 [REDACTED] 11:31 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) 09/06/2025 09:19 (FAX)7184282475 P.002/002 SUN, FENGMEI Surgical Pathology Report [REDACTED] Specimen: Left breast (DCIS) Block: 1A RESULTS OF ANCILLARY IMMUNOPATHOLOGY STUDIES PERCENTAGE OF POSITIVE CELLS STAINING INTENSITY ESTROGEN RECEPTOR: &gt;95% STRONG INTERPRETATION: Since ≥1% of tumor cell nuclei express estrogen receptors, this tumor is considered to be ESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE. ER, PgR, HER2 and Ki-67 immunohistochemistry was performed on tissue fixed in 10% neutral buffered formalin for at least 6 hours, up to a maximum of 72 hours. The specimen was partially or entirely clonal for ER, the Ventana E2 antibody clone for PgR, the Ventana 4B5 antibody clone for HER2, and the Ventana 30.9 antibody clone for Ki-67. Additional antibody clones for Ki-67 and HER2 were represented given the background staining of the ASO/CAP guidelines. Antibody performance was initially validated by NYP/Q and is periodically verified. Interpretation of these antibodies is based on current CAP/ASCO scoring criteria. Esther Cheng, D.O. Billing Codes: I; 88360_Q, 88305_Q, 88342_Q, 88341_Q (Epic Private Ambulatory) All controls for immunohistochemistry, histochemistry, histology, and cytology show appropriate reactivity. These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by NYP/Q. Modified procedures such as decalcification, alcohol fixation, air dried smears make this assay not subject to variations from the standard formalin fixed paraffin embedded specimen. They have not been cleared or approved</data>
      <data key="d14" />
