      <data key="d12">15</data>
      <data key="d13">1A RESULTS OF ANCILLARY IMMUNOPATHOLOGY STUDIES PERCENTAGE OF POSITIVE CELLS STAINING INTENSITY ESTROGEN RECEPTOR: &gt;95% STRONG INTERPRETATION: Since ≥1% of tumor cell nuclei express estrogen receptors, this tumor is considered to be ESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE. ER, PgR, HER2 and Ki-67 immunohistochemistry was performed on tissue fixed in 10% neutral buffered formalin for at least 6 hours, up to a maximum of 72 hours. The specimen was partially or entirely clonal for ER, the Ventana E2 antibody clone for PgR, the Ventana 4B5 antibody clone for HER2, and the Ventana 30.9 antibody clone for Ki-67. Additional antibody clones for Ki-67 and HER2 were represented given the background staining of the ASO/CAP guidelines. Antibody performance was initially validated by NYP/Q and is periodically verified. Interpretation of these antibodies is based on current CAP/ASCO scoring criteria. Esther Cheng, D.O. Billing Codes: I; 88360_Q, 88305_Q, 88342_Q, 88341_Q (Epic Private Ambulatory) All controls for immunohistochemistry, histochemistry, histology, and cytology show appropriate reactivity. These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by NYP/Q. Modified procedures such as decalcification, alcohol fixation, air dried smears make this assay not subject to variations from the standard formalin fixed paraffin embedded specimen. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary. These tests are used for clinical purposes. They should not be regarded as investigational or research. SUN, FENGMEI Printed [REDACTED] 09:54 Page 2 of 2 QP Marker END OF REPORT Document Information Other: Outside Pathology PATH 2/3 Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 11:31 PM [REDACTED] 11:31 PM Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) [REDACTED] 00:00 Attached To: OUTSIDE PATHOLOGY ORDER [REDACTED] Orders Only on [REDACTED] with Historical Provider, [REDACTED] Source Information Jaslee Quinones | Msk Pas Sun, Fengmei (MR # 38307961) Printed by Solange Bayard, MD [REDACTED] at [REDACTED] 11:31 PM 3/3</data>
      <data key="d14" />
    </node>
